	file.0000000000000001.title: "Fabled Wylds"
	image.3E5ED4E172944013.title: "Click here to join our Discord!"
	image.4B4A1262804A76C5.title: "support the modpack and play with friends!"
	image.7EE333354E93796B.title: "Click here to visit our Github Wiki!"
	quest.001588EAB32E428A.quest_desc: ["To achieve this advancement, &6feed a &eSnifflet&r something it enjoys!"]
	quest.00B1A6C679547AF2.quest_desc: [
		"The first boss you must face is the block-destroying &eNaga&r. It is a long serpent who slowly shrinks in length as you damage him."
		""
		"If the player flees the courtyard, the Naga will return to the center."
		""
		"Once he's defeated, &6be sure to loot the chest that he spawns&r, as you will need the &bNaga Trophy&r inside of it."
	]
	quest.00B1A6C679547AF2.quest_subtitle: "Nag your local Naga"
	quest.00B1A6C679547AF2.title: "Find a Naga Courtyard"
	quest.00BDE15DD24045A6.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know that you can &aspeed up the tick speed of a block&r? This can be used on things like &bCompost&r to make them progress faster."
		""
		"Craft the &bTime in a Bottle&r and hold it in your inventory to accumulate time. Then, you can &6shift right click&r on certain blocks to apply that time to them."
	]
	quest.00BDE15DD24045A6.title: "Capture Time in a Bottle"
	quest.010D5F21ACF6C3D0.title: "Obtain a Spell"
	quest.0191F41344B7250D.quest_desc: [
		"What's a witch without &bCandles&r? Well, still pretty great. But not as well-lit!"
		""
		"Show your dedication to your craft by making &aone of each type of candle&r."
		""
		"Turn the page for more &oreal life information&r about what each color of candle stands for!"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"All information comes from &oforestofwisdom.com.au&r:"
		""
		"&fWhite&r - &7Attracting, Purifying, Cleansing, Protection, Balancing, Clarity, Divination, Grounding, Guidance, Healing, Higher Self, Hope, Innocence, Optimism, Peace, Spirituality, Truth, Will Power and Workplace Magic.&r"
		""
		"&o&7White is also thought of as an all purpose candle. White candles can generally be used to replace other colours when they are not available.&r"
		""
		"&0Black&r - &7Absorbing, Acceptance, Anger, The Afterlife, Banishing, Binding, Challenges, Determination, Death, Endings, Justice, Loss, Release, Break Hexes, Security, Grief, Negativity, Magic, Patience, Persistence, Rebirth, Karma, Secrets, Spirituality, Strength and Self Control.&r"
		""
		"&4Red&r - &7Courage, Assertiveness, Business, Creativity, Energy, Desire, Love, Loyalty, Motivation, Passion, Romance, Strength, Power, Action, Survival, Change and Overcoming obstacles.&r"
		""
		"&eYellow&r - &7Action, Communication, Friendships, Learning new skills, Loans and Credit, Business, Happiness, Intellect, Inspiration, Intuition, Knowledge, Wisdom, Pleasure, Stimulation and Travel.&r"
		""
		"&dPink&r - &7Acceptance, Affection, Beauty, Compassion, Reconciliation, Children, Healing Abuse, Fidelity, Family, Friendship, Femininity, Kindness, Love, Marriage, Nurturing, Passion, Sensuality and Love.&r"
		""
		"&2Green&r - &7Abundance, Acceptance, Action, Agriculture, Beauty, Change, Creativity, Family, Fertility, Harmony, Healing, Luck, Longevity, Environment, Nurturing, Partnerships, Peace and Prosperity.&r"
		""
		"&5Purple&r - &7Astrology, Authority, Enlightenment, Spiritual Development, Psychic Protection, Emotions, Imagination, Influence, Independence, Power, Spirituality, Truth, Wisdom, Writing,  Addiction and Overcoming Fears.&r"
		""
		"&6Orange&r - &7Abundance, Adaptability, Ambition, Celebration, Confidence, Creativity, Courage, Discipline, Vitality (Energy), Independence, Freedom, Goals, Justice, Money, Positivity, Pleasure, Reconciliation, Stimulation, Strength and Travel.&r"
		""
		"&bBlue&r - &7Honesty, Trust, Communication, Dreamwork, Sleep, Mental obstacles, Wisdom, Pregnancy, Leadership, Justice, Career, Marriage, Interviews and Study.&r"
		""
		"Brown - &7Material matters, Endurance, Hard Work, Animals, Balance, Courage, Grounding, Finding lost objects, Stability, Material Protection.&r"
		""
		"Silver - &7Awareness, Healing, Intuition, Divination, Money, Psychic Powers, Purification, Hidden Potential, Fertility, Feminine Energy, Stability, Success, Sea, Moon and Star Magic and The Goddess.&r"
		""
		"Gold - &7Abundance, Fame and Fortune, Ambitions, Money, Positivity, Happiness, Creativity, Divination, Power, Influence, Luxury, Masculine Energy, Sun Magick and The God.&r"
	]
	quest.0191F41344B7250D.quest_subtitle: "s-candle-ous"
	quest.0191F41344B7250D.title: "A Rainbow of Candles"
	quest.02000A977B04C84A.quest_desc: [
		"&eUmvuthi, the Sunbird&r is deity to his people, who he both protects and creates. "
		""
		"&eUmvuthi&r can be found in the &cSavannah&r, and if you are wearing &athe correct type of mask&r, then he and his people will be friendly to you. However, they do not look kindly upon &dvandalism or theft&r."
		""
		"The ancient texts have this to say of him:"
		""
		"&o&eUmvuthi&r &ois the creator of the &eAbavuthana&r, &oresiding in a stationary seat upon a throne in &csavannah groves&r. &oHe draws his power from the sun, &acalling forth sunstrikes, solar flares, and massive solar beams&r. &oHe can also &acreate &eUmvuthana &afollowers&r &o- including healers called Umvuthana Cranes - from masks to defend him during combat. As such, his masked children revere him as a god. Unequipped travelers should keep their distance from his grove, lest they be smitten by his heliomancy."
		""
		"&oThose strong enough to face and defeat him, however, are rewarded with his mask: the &bSol Visage&r. &oThis mask allows its wearers to breathe life into masks to create Umvuthana followers. Unfortunately, the mask does not bestow heliomancy upon its bearer; this power is innately carried by Umvuthi, and thus dies with him. &dPerhaps there is another way&r...?&r"
	]
	quest.02000A977B04C84A.quest_subtitle: "praise the sun...or else"
	quest.022A9FF2DA695F94.title: "Catch Overworld Lava Fish"
	quest.0291249FFD51DD05.quest_desc: [
		"To read a book in your &bEccentric Tome&r, &6right click&r while holding the book and &6select the book you want&r."
		""
		"To &areturn the Eccentric Tome&r to its regular form, &6hold it and left click in the air&r."
		""
		"To &aremove a book from the tome&r, you need to &6crouch and throw&r the item (default keybind is Q)."
		""
		"To &aadd a book&r, you should &6craft the book with the &bTome&r."
		""
		"&lIf you ever lose your Eccentric Tome&r, you can easily &6craft a new one&r with a &bBook&r and a &bStick&r."
	]
	quest.02CA3D4397E8BA25.quest_desc: [
		"You can attach a &bSatchel&r to your &bBroom&r both as a cute decoration, and as a way to store items on the go!"
		""
		"There are three Satchel items: &bSmall Satchel&r, &bMedium&r, and &bLarge&r. Only one can be equipped at any given time."
		""
		"The Medium Satchel requires a Small Satchel in order to craft. The Large requires one Small and one Medium, and combines them together on your Broom."
		""
		"Crouch and right-click your Broom to access its &aaccessories and inventory&r."
	]
	quest.02CA3D4397E8BA25.quest_subtitle: "Portable storage"
	quest.02CA3D4397E8BA25.title: "Obtain a Small Satchel"
	quest.03102B4CD0BE7031.quest_desc: [
		"One of the features in the Twilight Forest is the &aHedge Maze&r. It is a labyrinth filled with spawners and chests full of loot!"
		""
		"It does not count towards, nor require, any progression through the Forest."
	]
	quest.03102B4CD0BE7031.quest_subtitle: "Now you can be a Hedge Witch!"
	quest.03102B4CD0BE7031.title: "Find a Hedge Maze"
	quest.0323243BE6D015C7.quest_desc: [
		"The &bPickarang&r is a tool which can &aremotely break blocks and return the drops to you&r."
		""
		"It can also be used to &agrab dropped items&r and &adamage enemies&r."
		""
		"You can upgrade it to the &bFlamarang&r, and both versions can be Enchanted."
	]
	quest.03C828F2F895A23C.quest_desc: ["While you're fighting the &eAlpha Yeti&r, why not trip him up a little bit by &6casting &bRoses Thorns&r at his feet?"]
	quest.041330E9AC7E1769.quest_desc: [
		"The &cSwamp Dungeon&r is an ancient ruin filled with &eUndead&r, but home to &apotential treasures&r! You can find them, oddly enough, in &cSwamps&r, and you can of course use the &bExplorer's Compass&r to locate one!"
		""
		"And while you're in there... don't forget to &dcheck behind the stairs&r..."
	]
	quest.041330E9AC7E1769.title: "Find the Swamp Dungeon"
	quest.047370ADE354D8DB.quest_desc: [
		"In order to read your &bBook of Shadows&r, you must first place it on a &bWooden Altar&r. In order to craft this magical pedestal, you'll need to find a &bMahogany Tree&r, located in &aJungle&r Biomes."
		""
		"The &bWooden Altar&r can also display items if you &6right click them onto its surface&r. You can also &6shift right click&r to place a block on top of them. Placing &bWooden Altars&r around your primary 2x3 &bAltar&r will &aprovide more power to it&r!"
		""
		"Also note that if you place &lHexerei&r &bcandles&r on your &bWooden Altar&r and light them, they will &afloat around as they burn&r!"
	]
	quest.047370ADE354D8DB.quest_subtitle: "A focal point for magic"
	quest.0496A62983DE2ABB.quest_desc: ["These exotic crops may be hard to come by, but if you manage to collect one of each, you'll be rewarded!"]
	quest.0496A62983DE2ABB.title: "Compact Your Crops: Exotic"
	quest.04973320B5F27BD7.quest_desc: ["Collect one each of every flower in the game to earn rewards!"]
	quest.04973320B5F27BD7.title: "Flower Picking: Black and White"
	quest.04CB1359F805B396.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Trio of Stews"
	quest.04D06CBCA0CB74BC.quest_desc: [
		"Your &bCanvas&r is, well... your &bCanvas&r. It's where you paint your masterpiece!"
		""
		"Or, if you're me, your disasterpiece. It's okay. We'll get there someday."
	]
	quest.04D06CBCA0CB74BC.title: "Obtain Canvas"
	quest.04E69B80121E8192.quest_desc: [
		"To &aremotely link Sophisticated Storages&r which are not touching the main network, you need to &6place a &bStorage Link&6 on them&r, and then &6right click the &bStorage Tool&r on the &bLink&r and the &bStorage Controller&r."
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/storagelinking.png width:100 height:70 align:1 fit:true}"
	]
	quest.04E69B80121E8192.title: "Connected at a Distance"
	quest.04EA0AA493E41274.title: "High Sensitivity B\\&W Film"
	quest.04FD578146464FA6.quest_desc: [
		"The &eHamster&r is a surprisingly complex creature. You may think of them as small, brainless balls of fluff, and you're partly right. But did you know they are also &avicious warriors&r who will &aeat their own offspring if threatened&r? Pretty metal."
		""
		"Anyway, in nature as with witchcraft, there are many layers of nuance, but I am getting ahead of myself."
		""
		"Find a cute little &eHamster&r, and &6crouch, then approach it and right click with these &bCucumber Slices&r, and you'll make a little friend!"
		""
		"You can reference the &bHamster Guide&r in your &bEccentric Tome&r for more information!"
	]
	quest.04FD578146464FA6.quest_subtitle: "hampter"
	quest.0545DF70043D964A.quest_desc: ["Crops can be easily compacted into Bags or Crates in order to &asave on storage space&r. &6Place 9 of each material in a Crafting Grid&r to obtain a Crate or Bag of it!"]
	quest.0545DF70043D964A.quest_subtitle: "Crops but compact"
	quest.0545DF70043D964A.title: "Compact Your Crops"
	quest.056F7888052BBEF2.quest_desc: [
		"The &bEnhanced Broom Brush&r has increased durability. Don't forget to hang it out to dry once you've crafted it!"
		""
		"Your &bBroom Brush&r can also be &aEnchanted&r with Unbreaking and Mending, so that its durability is better!"
	]
	quest.056F7888052BBEF2.quest_subtitle: "Fancy enhancery"
	quest.056F7888052BBEF2.title: "Obtain an Enhanced Broom Brush"
	quest.05772A2D60C9FF3D.quest_desc: [
		"The &bHerb Jar&r can be crafted by smelting 8 &bSand&r in your &bMixing Cauldron&r. Each Herb Jar can carry &aonly one type&r of Herb, but can &acontain up to 1024&r of that herb!"
		""
		"The Herb Jar label will &areflect what is stored inside of it&r, and can be named using an &bAnvil&r. When broken, the Herb Jar retains its inventory."
		""
		"&6Left click an &bHerb Jar to withdraw&r 1 item. &6Crouch and left click&r to remove a stack."
		""
		"&eFamiliar Ravens&r will &agather and deposit harvested herbs&r if the button inside the jar (&6crouch right click&r to access) is pressed."
	]
	quest.05772A2D60C9FF3D.quest_subtitle: "Totally herbaceous, dude"
	quest.05772A2D60C9FF3D.title: "Obtain an Herb Jar"
	quest.057C8372ED1CBDC0.quest_desc: [
		"Okay so YES, &otechnically&r these aren't all vegetables. &bTomatoes&r are a fruit, &bPotatoes&r are a tuber, and no one really knows what &bCabbage&r is or why it exists. Stop being so pedantic and get your @$#%# together."
		""
		"(&8@$#%# means vegetables. get them together into a crate&r)"
	]
	quest.057C8372ED1CBDC0.title: "Compact Your Crops: Veggies"
	quest.05B5DD9990917317.quest_desc: [
		"The &bWaymaker&r is a spell focus which allows you to &ateleport to specific locations&r."
		""
		"Crafting the &bWaymaker&r is trivial - a &bBone Needle&r and a &bFlint&r. However, you'll then need to &abind it to a location&r."
		""
		"There are two rituals for this - one requires your &bAltar&r and 500 altar power, and the other requires &aslightly more ingredients&r, but you don't have to lug your &bAltar&r out into the field in order to cast it. Both rituals require plain &bRitual Chalk&r and &dsmall ritual circles&r. You'll need &bOtherwhere Chalk&r to use the finished product, however!"
		""
		"You'll need an &bEnder Pearl&r for some &bEnder Dew&r, and also a &bDiamond&r to craft into an &bAttuned Stone&r. Consider these a gift from me."
	]
	quest.05B5DD9990917317.quest_subtitle: "making my way downtown"
	quest.05B5DD9990917317.title: "Traversal using Waymakers"
	quest.05EFC8F18818E8DD.quest_desc: [
		"So you've caught like 4,000+ fish trying to catch a &bMending Book&r, huh? And now you want to know what to do with all the fish?"
		""
		"Let me introduce the humble &bSelling Bin&r. Placing your fish in this bin will &aallow you to sell them&r one-by-one, or toggle \"Autosell\" to sell them in bulk. If you have a &bBank Card&r, you can insert it to &ahave the funds sent straight to your bank&r!"
		""
		"{image:quest_enhance:textures/ftb/clipboard_1786044324131.png width:345 height:229 align:center click_action:none:}"
	]
	quest.05EFC8F18818E8DD.quest_subtitle: "become a sellout!"
	quest.05EFC8F18818E8DD.title: "Obtain a Selling Bin"
	quest.063A5C650B0846FF.quest_desc: ["This unique End-enchanted item will only &afall when provided with a Redstone signal&r. If it is provided a redstone signal and &acannot fall, it will float up instead&r."]
	quest.063A5C650B0846FF.quest_subtitle: "this sand doesn't follow your rules"
	quest.063A5C650B0846FF.title: "Sand Which Disobeys Gravity"
	quest.063AD4FD6E8FB943.quest_desc: ["Similar to the &bDisplay Case&r, the &bPedestal&r is a way to decoratively display a single item. However, when stacked, it becomes a pillar."]
	quest.063AD4FD6E8FB943.quest_subtitle: "Don't put people on these"
	quest.06DC33669C98F5A4.quest_desc: [
		"&bWarp Plates&r function alongside &bAttuned Shards&r to teleport you between two defined places. Once placed and right clicked, a Warp Plate will create an Attuned Shard which is bound to that Warp Plate. The Shard will be &ainscribed with unique runes&r that match those in the Plate's GUI upper right corner."
		""
		"In you &6insert the shard into another Warp Plate&r, it will now teleport you to the Plate inscribed on that stone. You can create multiple Shards with &bFlint&r and &bWarp Dust&r."
	]
	quest.06DC33669C98F5A4.quest_subtitle: "Quickly back and forth"
	quest.06DC33669C98F5A4.title: "Obtain a Warp Plate"
	quest.076F2A55BD9D0BCA.quest_desc: [
		"Are you an artist? Of course you are. Everyone has the ability to paint, to put pigment onto parchment. The simple act of creation is one of the most meditative pastimes there is."
		""
		"To begin, you'll need an &bEasel&r, and a &bPalette&r. You'll also need &bCanvases&r to paint on."
	]
	quest.076F2A55BD9D0BCA.title: "The Joy of Painting"
	quest.0781A21B04D458DE.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Amethyst"
	quest.07A746772D2FE875.quest_desc: [
		"&eJumping spiders&r are some of the most curious, amiable, and intelligent arthropods out there! You can &6tame them with &bDragonfly Wings&r, and as pets, they will &aprotect their owner&r!"
		""
		"If you should be so heartless as to kill one, they do &adrop &bSpider Silk&r, but as &dyou can find this resource through &bCocoons&r found throughout the world, there's little reason to hurt these sweet little beans."
	]
	quest.07A746772D2FE875.quest_subtitle: "Hi, My name is Lucas. "
	quest.07A746772D2FE875.title: "Meet the Jumping Spider"
	quest.084BB53F414CF215.quest_desc: [
		"As you go about your life in this world, you will &again and lose reputation&r among the founts of magic that invisibly cohabitate with you."
		""
		"These founts, which are not quite spirit and not quite energy, run through the world as ley lines, and can &aprovide you with abilities&r, if you are enough in tune with them. You can &acheck your reputation at any time by &6pressing R&r."
		""
		"- &l&aCultivation&r: You increase your reputation with this spring by nurturing crops, composting items, growing huge mushrooms, and breeding &eSprouts&r. You lose reputation by killing &eSprouts&r."
		""
		"- &l&cElemental&r: You increase your elemental reputation by growing &belemental crops&r, fighting the &eWither&r, and when you first enter the &cNether&r."
		""
		"- &l&dFairy&r: You increase your Fairy reputation by trading with &eVillagers&r, curing &eZombie Villagers&r, bartering with &ePiglins&r, and of course, trading with a &bFairy Hut&r. You lose reputation by killing &eVillagers&r, including &eWandering Traders&r."
		""
		"- &l&3Fungal&r: You increase your Fungal reputation by composting items, casting &bGeas&r, growing huge mushrooms, and killing &eundead&r."
		""
		"- &l&ePrimal&r: You increase your Primal reputation by growing &bcrops&r, breeding and taming &eanimals&r, harvesting &bBeehives&r, and milking &eCows&r. You lose reputation by &akilling peaceful creatures&r."
		""
		"- &l&5Twilight&r: You increase your Twilight reputation by growing certain crops and killing peaceful creatures. "
		""
		"Each fount will also get a large boost of attunement/reputation when you &afirst learn or cast an associated spell&r. "
	]
	quest.08FFDD3033FC7A9B.title: "Druid Horns"
	quest.09827E9E92823643.quest_desc: ["&bCollars&r can be used to name your pets, but they can also be &aenchanted&r to give your pet special abilities."]
	quest.09ED0DFEB72DFD71.quest_desc: ["You've found your way to &dThe End&r, congratulations. With luck, your journey will continue."]
	quest.09ED0DFEB72DFD71.quest_subtitle: "Haha, get it? \"The End\"?"
	quest.09ED0DFEB72DFD71.title: "The Beginning of the End"
	quest.0A60EB3B10E89FE2.quest_desc: [
		"&bPacking Tape&r is an incredibly helpful item which can be used to &apackage up a storage block&r for transport. Although &dit can only be used on Sophisticated Storage&r."
		""
		"You need to &6right click the &bTape&r onto the desired item. Then you can &6break the block&r and it will retain its inventory."
	]
	quest.0A6B50D21095E2AA.quest_desc: ["The &bFramed Key&r allows &alocking certain Framed Blocks in their current shape&r to suppress neighbor updates. This allows &aplacing blocks in configurations that would not be possible&r with the desired neighbors (i.e. placing Framed Stairs in the corner shape without keeping the necessary neighbors to force that shape)."]
	quest.0A76B3D9CF688878.quest_desc: [
		"The &bItem Pipe&r is a way for you to easily transfer items from one inventory to another."
		""
		"It can &aconnect to an individual chest, barrel, or a whole network&r via a &bInventory Connector&r."
		""
		"You can use a &bWrench&r (either from &lPipez&r or &lCreate&r - the one from &lSupplementaries&r doesn't work) to &achange its mode&r."
		""
		"&6Shift right click the wrench&r onto one side of the &bPipe&r to connect/disconnect it, and also to &aset to Extract mode&r."
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/depositextract.png width:300 height:150 align:1}"
		""
		"Once in &aExtract Mode&r, you can &6right click on the pipe&r to access its menu."
		""
		"&dDo not use Time in a Bottle on Pipez&r. In certain (admittedly uncommon) cases, it can cause severe lag or a complete crash."
	]
	quest.0A76B3D9CF688878.quest_subtitle: "Organize your Storage Network"
	quest.0A8AD22B188FA65B.quest_desc: [
		"Are you tired of saplings &anot giving you &bFumes&r? Why not add a &bFume Funnel&r to either side of your &bWitch's Oven&r to increase your chances?"
		""
		"Read the &bArt of Witchcraft&r to learn more."
	]
	quest.0A8AD22B188FA65B.quest_subtitle: "im fuming mad"
	quest.0A8AD22B188FA65B.title: "Obtain a Fume Funnel"
	quest.0AC22F22CD346EEB.quest_desc: [
		"As you improve your backpack, you will unlock upgrade slots. Just like with &lSophisticated Storage&r, you can use those slots to &aincrease stack size&r with the &bStack Upgrades&r or &aautomatically compact items&r with the &bCompacting Upgrade&r to maximize storage space."
		""
		"To get the most of these upgrades, we suggest &6checking out the settings tab&r for each one. "
		""
		"Your settings will be saved for each upgrade &aeven if you remove it.&r"
	]
	quest.0AC22F22CD346EEB.quest_subtitle: "mary poppins got nothing on this"
	quest.0AC22F22CD346EEB.title: "Inventory Management"
	quest.0AC47FF8FD45B289.quest_desc: [
		"There are many ways to carry items with you while you adventure, but not all of them are quite as terrifying as a &bLuggage&r. It has little concern for others, and loves to &agobble up dropped items&r. "
		"And yet, it's strangely endearing."
		""
		"You can &6access its inventory with right click&r, and &6pick it up with shift right click&r. It &aretains its inventory&r when picked up, and it cannot die."
		""
		"The &eLuggage&r can &awear a collar&r, which will grant it the enchanted abilities. However, &dplacing the Luggage in your inventory will delete the collar&r, so be sure to remove it before picking it back up."
	]
	quest.0AC47FF8FD45B289.quest_subtitle: "om nom nom nom"
	quest.0AC47FF8FD45B289.title: "Not Exactly a Pet"
	quest.0AD64024D055FF01.quest_desc: [
		"Another way you can customize your &aStarcatching experience&r is by &achanging your &bHooks&r. "
		""
		"- &bShiny Hook&r: You can no longer see what fish you're catching, but it guarantees a treasure if you correctly hit 3 sweet spots."
		"- &bGold Hook&r: Golden fish are more likely to bite. Pair this with the &bGolden Bobber&r!"
		"- &bMossy Hook&r: A perfect catch has a chance to award a treasure."
		"- &bAmethyst Hook&r: Allows for lava-fishing."
		"- &bStone Hook&r: Increases lure time."
		"- &bSplit Hook&r: One extra fish upon perfect catch."
		"- &bHeavy Hook&r: Slows down moving sweet spots."
		"- &bVanilla-Flavored Hook&r: When paired with the &bVanilla-Flavored Bobber&r, it skips the minigame (and you can only catch vanilla fish)."
		"- &bCopper Hook&r: Increases handle rotation speed slightly."
		"- &bExposed Copper Hook&r: Increases handle rotation speed more."
		"- &bWeathered Copper Hook&r: Decreases handle rotation speed slightly."
		"- &bOxidized Copper Hooks&r: Decreases handle rotation speed more."
		"- &bEchoing Hook&r: Increases likelihood of unknown fish biting, but hitting sweet spots allows darkness to consume you."
		"- &bFrozen Hook&r: Hitting a frozen sweet spot will freeze your handle for a few seconds"
	]
	quest.0AD64024D055FF01.quest_subtitle: "hook, line, and sinker"
	quest.0AD64024D055FF01.title: "Different Hooks"
	quest.0ADDED8D0A193EF8.title: "Black and White Film"
	quest.0ADE58E9E0DFD059.quest_desc: [
		"There are two types of &bHoney Compass&r."
		""
		"The first, and most common one, will help you to locate the &cCell Maze&r, a &aloot filled dungeon&r."
		""
		"The second is found within the &cCell Maze&r, and it will help you locate the &cThrone Room&r!"
	]
	quest.0ADE58E9E0DFD059.title: "Obtain a Honey Compass"
	quest.0AF3D2A62E51E5B2.quest_desc: [
		"A full set of &bNetherite Armor&r takes..."
		""
		"*counts on fingers*..."
		""
		"..."
		""
		"&aAt least &ofour&r &bNetherite&r. Anyway - the important thing isn't the math, just go do it and take the reward."
	]
	quest.0B0B5160EA821956.title: "Pestle and Mortar"
	quest.0B131225FEDAA6AC.title: "Catch Frozen Fish"
	quest.0B1646339D14D055.quest_desc: [
		"An &bEnder Chest&r is like cloud storage for your items. This inventory is accessible through any &bEnder Chest&r, anywhere in the world."
		"It's not a bad idea to fill it with emergency items. You can &again more storage space&r by &6filling it with Shulker Boxes&r."
	]
	quest.0B947B43262CD036.title: "Scavenger Hunt: 5 Disc"
	quest.0BDF6D5ED0A22E48.quest_desc: [
		"The &bDis-enchanting Table&r is a very valuable workspace, as it allows you to &atransfer enchantments from items onto books&r. Simply provide it with an &benchanted item&r and a &bBook&r, and copy the magic from one to the other."
		""
		"To &aseparate enchantments&r, you can &6place the book with multiple enchantments&r in one slot and a &bBook&r in the next, and it will &aremove just one enchantment at a time&r."
	]
	quest.0BDF6D5ED0A22E48.title: "Obtain a Dis-Enchanting Table"
	quest.0C0EB5F8CF5970B2.quest_desc: ["Need to tame something quickly? Why not &atame it instantly&r with the &bHeartseed&r!"]
	quest.0C3A4C2AADB4DCD8.quest_desc: ["Although you can &acraft many of the &bFramed Blocks&r &adirectly&r, it's highly recommended to get a &bFraming Saw&r, which acts very similarly to a &bStonecutter&r, and will allow you to craft the basic &bFramed Cube&r and then &6alter it to a different shape&r."]
	quest.0C66306B20F7844C.quest_desc: ["Compact your &bberries&r into these &ahelpful (and decorative) storage blocks&r!"]
	quest.0C66306B20F7844C.title: "Compact Your Crops: Berries"
	quest.0C72B71937E0F79F.quest_desc: [
		"You can use &bpowdered or magical herbs&r to create &bMutandis&r, a powerful mutagen with the ability to &atransform a mundane plant into a magical one&r. In fact, there are many capabilities of this bizarre powder, but you'll have to experiment with those for yourself."
		""
		"Why not &atry clicking it on blocks&r?"
	]
	quest.0C72B71937E0F79F.title: "Mutating Plants"
	quest.0C7EA86F283677BB.quest_desc: [
		"A &bKnife&r is a perfectly useful tool to have for any reason - you can skin potatoes, cut red tape, and stab a b - I mean, anyway, let's move on."
		""
		"Most knives cause &acertain unique drops&r to be obtained from various creatures, such as &bBat's Wool&r and &bCreeper Hearts&r."
		""
		"&bKnives&r can not only procure unique drops, but can be used for &aForaging&r, which is to say, breaking &bLeaves&r and &bGrasses&r to garner extra items from them as well. You'll be looking for &bGrove Moss&r, &bGrove Spores&r, and &bWildroot&r, as these are important ingredients in your magical journey."
		""
		"But the &bGolden Knife&r is special, as it can be used to craft an &bAthame&r, which you'll need for certain types of witchery."
	]
	quest.0C7EA86F283677BB.quest_subtitle: "it's pronounced \"kuh-niff-ee\""
	quest.0C7EA86F283677BB.title: "Obtain a Golden Knife"
	quest.0CE78F66E92FB026.quest_desc: [
		"The &bDipper&r is used for making candles. It can be placed above a &bMixing Cauldron&b filled with &bTallow&r (rendered Animal Fat) and hung with String in order to &6create Candles&r."
		""
		"Unlike basic Candles, these can be placed together with Candles of different colors, and may be lit separately!"
		""
		"&bTallow&r is created in the Mixing Cauldron with &bAnimal Fat and Honeycombs&r."
	]
	quest.0CE78F66E92FB026.quest_subtitle: "where's Mabel?"
	quest.0CE78F66E92FB026.title: "Obtain a Dipper"
	quest.0D51CFD77E404109.quest_desc: ["The &bAttuned Stone&r is a crafting ingredient used in many recipes, such as the &bPoppet Shelf&r and &bDistillery&r."]
	quest.0D51CFD77E404109.title: "Obtain Attuned Stone"
	quest.0D8DA3376EF50A60.quest_desc: ["Equip your &eRaven&r with this &bAnkh&r to protect it from danger. It will grant it &aRegen&r while it's playing dead, and &aacts as a &bTotem of Undying&r in case the &eRaven&r dies."]
	quest.0D9CF1E8881559EC.quest_desc: ["The &bRunic Shears&r are a tool which will allow you to &aharvest materials from animals without harming them&r. Helpful if you are a pacifist!"]
	quest.0DC28A267878E6E1.quest_desc: ["Collect all the modded music discs. "]
	quest.0DC28A267878E6E1.quest_subtitle: "Play that funky music"
	quest.0DC28A267878E6E1.title: "Music Lover - Modded"
	quest.0DCDAC4C7D4F9F0B.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to Cottage Witch 2!"
		""
		"As you enter the overworld, you may be in want of some creature comforts - namely, a good book, and a safe haven."
		""
		"The &bEccentric Tome&r contains guidebooks (and some other goodies) from this modpack, to be perused at your leisure, whether that's all at once, or bit by bit. The controls will be explained in a future quest."
		""
		"You can use the &bSpyglass&r to &aresearch creatures and plants&r, as well as to see long distances. Learn more about this in the &lDiscovery&r chapter."
		""
		"The &bCharting Map&r will let you &agraph out paths in the world&r and eventually &afast travel&r! More on that later, as well."
		""
		"The &bSoul Key&r will allow you to perform your first bit of magic, by bringing you into yourself! Let me explain - actually, no, there is too much. Let me sum up: &6pressing and holding the right mouse button with the key in your hand&r will bring you to a pocket dimension in the safest place: your soul. In your &bSoulHome&r, it is always peaceful, and no creatures will spawn."
		""
		"Be aware that &devery creature within a 2.5 block radius around you will teleport as well&r."
	]
	quest.0DCDAC4C7D4F9F0B.quest_subtitle: "we're back, witches"
	quest.0DDBFB778B945B97.quest_desc: [
		"The &bEnder Drawer&r allows you to access the same inventory from &amultiple locations&r. Very useful if you need to access the same blocks frequently in different workshops!"
		""
		"To link them, you'll need a &bLinking Tool&r. &6Left click the main &bEnder Drawer&r, and it should say \"stored frequency in the tool&r. Then, &6shift right click&r the second inventory to have it mimic the first!"
	]
	quest.0DDBFB778B945B97.quest_subtitle: "the same inventory in two places"
	quest.0E2749D8FEEF0D49.quest_desc: ["You can make &bPasta with Meatballs&r in a &bCooking Pot&r. Eating Full-Course meals, such as this one, will grant you the &aNourishing&r effect, which &aprevents you from losing hunger and saturation&r for a time. Helpful if you'll be going somewhere dangerous, as it will keep your health regenerating!"]
	quest.0E2749D8FEEF0D49.quest_subtitle: "Touched by his noodly appendage."
	quest.0E2749D8FEEF0D49.title: "Make Hearty Meals"
	quest.0E28D4A9544EAF0E.quest_desc: [
		"Up to two &bSign Posts&r can be placed on any fence block, in order to form directional signs!"
		""
		"&6Shift and right click&r the placed Sign in order to reverse the direction."
		""
		"If you &6right click them with a compass&r, they will point in the direction the compass points to. Useful for spawn points and Lodestones!"
	]
	quest.0E28D4A9544EAF0E.quest_subtitle: "Show the way"
	quest.0E28D4A9544EAF0E.title: "Obtain a Sign Post"
	quest.0E7E3853C02CE06C.quest_desc: ["The &bCenser&r is a device which can &ahold up to 2 herbs for burning&r. Depending on which herbs you use, you can &again different effects&r."]
	quest.0ED4E7CE946E5F48.quest_desc: ["You can perhaps guess where the &bGuardian Eye&r can be located. Beneath the surface of the choppy sea, in the belly of an &eElder Guardian&r."]
	quest.0F55C73877E7FD90.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &bMagic Map Focus&r with a &bRaven Feather&r, some &bGlowstone Dust&r, and &bTorchberries&r (which can be found in Twilight Forest caves)."
		""
		"Then you can surround it with &bPaper&r to create a Magic Map, which will prove invaluable to your quest through the &dTwilight Forest&r."
	]
	quest.0F55C73877E7FD90.quest_subtitle: "Come on, Focus!"
	quest.0F5E5A0B0C05ACD2.quest_desc: [
		"The lava pools at the base of the &cNether&r are surprisingly full of life! Using a &bspecial Fishing Rod&r, you can &areel them in&r and enjoy the fruits of your labor!"
		""
		"Many of the fish can either be &acooked&r or &aprocessed into other byproducts&r. Use &lJEI&r to see what can be done with each fish!"
	]
	quest.0F5E5A0B0C05ACD2.title: "Catch Nether Fish"
	quest.0FFEC186DEA6C730.title: "Catch Weather-Specific Fish"
	quest.104D0C28773A1DD4.quest_desc: [
		"You can now &ago fishing in lava&r! Grab yourself a &bLava Fishing Rod&r and cast your line! You'll find you can catch some &areally interesting new fish&r."
		""
		"However, if you want to go &aStarcatching&r in lava, well, you'll need an &bAmethyst Hook&r, or a &bStarcatching Rod&r that's been &aupgraded with &bNetherite&r."
	]
	quest.104D0C28773A1DD4.quest_subtitle: "i've nether fished so well"
	quest.104D0C28773A1DD4.title: "Lava Fishing"
	quest.10522CDFCA586C03.quest_desc: [
		"The &bFramed Hammer&r can be used to &aremove the &acosmetic block&r from a &framed block&r by &6right clicking&r."
		""
		"It can also be used to &acustomize the slope of a &bFramed Collapsible Block&r. &6Left click&r the corner on the face you want to change to &amove the face inward&r and &6left click the corner while sneaking&r to &amove the face outward.&r"
		""
		"The latch of the &bFramed Chest&r can be switched between three modes by &6left clicking the chest with a &bFramed Hammer&r: "
		"- Default chest latch (default state) "
		"- Camo-textured latch "
		"- No latch"
		""
		"The &bFramed Pressure Plates&r (all variants) can be switched between &awaterloggable and non-waterloggable&r by &6left-clicking them with a &bFramed Hammer&r. Their default state is non-waterloggable to match vanilla behaviour."
	]
	quest.106FDB5A3E89127E.title: "Goblin Ears"
	quest.10842BA380044BC5.quest_desc: [
		"Being worshipped like a god tends to go to your head, and &eUmvuthi&r is no exception. And what do puffed-up, arrogant, self-absorbed - oh, sorry, I was ranting. What do such people like? &aTribute&r, of course."
		""
		"Bring &bGold Blocks&r to &eUmvuthi&r and perhaps you can strike a deal..."
	]
	quest.10842BA380044BC5.title: "Trade Gold with Umvuthi"
	quest.10AD8A01B9D0CD17.quest_desc: ["To catch these fish, check in places such as &cSwamps&r and &cDark Oak Forests&r."]
	quest.10AD8A01B9D0CD17.title: "Catch Fish in Murky Waters"
	quest.10C91592DCBC6FBD.quest_desc: [
		"Located in the gloomy depths of the &dDark Forest&r, the Knight Stronghold is infested with &eGoblins&r, and you cannot enter without one of the &bTrophies&r from the previous bosses."
		"You can use &bMaze Maps&r here, but the structures are so massive that you may need a number of them."
		"It is recommended to &6mark your path with torches&r to ensure that you don't double back by mistake."
		"The end of this dungeon contains a fight against the &eKnight Phantoms&r. These will not follow you out of the room, and can swarm you if you simply charge in. It is recommended to &6retreat out to the hallway periodically if healing is needed&r."
		"Once you defeat them, you can now challenge the &dDark Tower&r."
	]
	quest.10C91592DCBC6FBD.quest_subtitle: "Better bring some extra torches"
	quest.10EF479191689632.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCharting Map&r is an item which will allow you to engage in some light &acartography&r, which will ultimately allow you to &afast travel&r!"
		""
		"You see, there will be roads criss-crossing your world, which you can &achart to determine easy paths&r, and &6placing signs along these paths&r will allow you to then &atravel from one sign to another&r."
		""
		"Of course, you can &abuild your own path as well&r - who are we witches if not trailblazers - to set up an easy network of instant traversal!"
	]
	quest.10F079B6E31FCF17.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Clay Ball"
	quest.1109A266D4045ABD.quest_desc: ["Whether you're visiting to &apay respects&r or to &ado a little graverobbing&r, seek out a &cVillager's Grave&r."]
	quest.1109A266D4045ABD.title: "Visit a Villager's Grave"
	quest.112917940415A7B1.quest_desc: [
		"An important part of &aDeath&r is to share it with others.* Now that you've dealt an obscene amount of damage, probably at least some of those things have died."
		""
		""
		"* for legal reasons, this is a joke"
	]
	quest.112917940415A7B1.title: "Doling Death to Others"
	quest.114EFE7EF75B22F3.quest_desc: [
		"It's time to play &aGoat in a Boat&r! The rules are simple:"
		"1. Get a &eGoat&r."
		"2. Get a &bBoat&r."
		"3. Get that &eGoat&r in that &bBoat&r."
		"4. Get your &abutt&r in that &bBoat&r."
		"You win!"
	]
	quest.114EFE7EF75B22F3.quest_subtitle: "captainsparklez intensifies"
	quest.1184EA40A20DEB5D.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCopy Paste Gadget&r is a robust and therefore complicated tool. It allows you to use &aSchematics found online&r to build automatically, and also allows you to - as you could guess - &acopy and paste structures you've built&r."
		""
		"In order to use it, you'll need &bPaper&r, and the &bTemplate Manager&r."
		""
		"I cannot put all the information in this quest description. &oMore information can be found on YouTube, at 8:12 into the \"Mod Spotlight Building Gadgets v2\" video by Direwolf20&r."
	]
	quest.1184EA40A20DEB5D.quest_subtitle: "Copypasta but for buildings"
	quest.1184EA40A20DEB5D.title: "Gadgets, Part 2"
	quest.11A001C9B2413F91.title: "High Sensitivity Color Film"
	quest.124F16ECDD4B26A2.quest_desc: ["Using the tools you just acquired, you can now make &bStrawberry Preserves!&r"]
	quest.125AC0EEF7096532.quest_desc: ["The &bImproved Upgrade&r gives you &aRedstone Mode&r control, and also allows you to change the &aDistribution mode&r, such as whether to deliver to the &afirst inventory&r, &aRound Robin&r, or &acompletely random&r."]
	quest.126325966A77DF87.quest_desc: ["The &bSculk Eye&r is a treasure sought by the eyeless &eWarden&r. No one knows its origin, but it is only natural for those without sight to desire an eye of their very own. Search &cAncient City&r chests and hope that you find this eye before the &eWarden&r finds either of you."]
	quest.129EB9D48551AA2E.quest_desc: ["The &bObsidian Pressure Plate&r can &aonly be activated by players&r, making it very useful for base entrances and such."]
	quest.129EB9D48551AA2E.quest_subtitle: "It can sense your sentience"
	quest.129EB9D48551AA2E.title: "A Player-Only Pressure Plate"
	quest.12BC0C79FE723230.quest_desc: ["On this &atower in the middle of the &csea&r, there live a lonely group of &eFishermen&r. They eke out a living through fishing and occasional trade with travelers - like you!"]
	quest.12BC0C79FE723230.title: "Discover the Island Tower"
	quest.12BD390D5D9BA40F.quest_desc: ["Adding mushrooms to your hat is a glorious aesthetic choice, although it doesn't offer any tangible benefits."]
	quest.12BD390D5D9BA40F.quest_subtitle: "The best upgrade, honestly"
	quest.12BD390D5D9BA40F.title: "Cover your Hat in Mushrooms"
	quest.12C571F5FBC6B57C.quest_desc: ["Normally, when you enter water while flying, your Broom will dismount you. However, by adding this tip to the end, you can remain in the water without getting thrown off, for a limited time."]
	quest.12C571F5FBC6B57C.quest_subtitle: "you too can be a sea witch"
	quest.12C571F5FBC6B57C.title: "Obtain Broom Waterproof Tip"
	quest.12CC2182B839D954.quest_subtitle: "wither? i barely know 'er!"
	quest.12FEBAA96A443199.quest_desc: ["Once you &acomplete the &lWitchery&r chapter, this quest will be completable!"]
	quest.130C66471B8C8E27.quest_desc: [
		"From &lHexalia&r. A small, standalone brewing vessel for Hexalia's custom Herbal Brews."
		""
		"&lHow it works&r:"
		"- Place over any heat source"
		"- Throw in the required herb ingredients"
		"- Output is a Brew item - a custom potion unique to Hexalia"
		""
		"&lWhat it makes:&r All 8 Hexalia Brews: Brew of Bloodlust, Slimewalker, Spikeskin, Siphon, Daybloom, Arachnid Grace, Homestead, Hollow Silence. These are not vanilla potions - they come in Rustic Bottles and have unique effects!"
	]
	quest.130C66471B8C8E27.title: "The Small Cauldron"
	quest.134ACEA76F0200AD.title: "Compact Your Crops: Dry Goods"
	quest.13555E89D6122D88.quest_desc: ["To obtain the &bWitch Eye&r, you must first &dslay an evil witch&r and get the &bWitch’s Pupil&r, then craft it together with an &bEnder Eye&r."]
	quest.1371F9B501187A91.quest_desc: ["The &bRedstone Illuminator&r is a light source which is on by default. It grows dimmer depending on how much &aRedstone signal&r it receives. One can use a &bCrank&r instead of a &bLever&r for more fine-tuned control."]
	quest.1371F9B501187A91.quest_subtitle: "Beware the power of the Illuminate-y"
	quest.13B72F5C0CF9E9FB.quest_desc: [
		"Blood Sigils are used to collect blood for rituals. They are crafted with &bRedstone&r and &bPolished Blackstone&r."
		""
		"Once you have crafted the Sigil, place it in the bottom of your &bMixing Cauldron&r (by &aright-clicking and placing it in the left slot of the crafting interface&r)."
		""
		"Once it is installed, make sure there is no liquid in your Cauldron, and then &ajump inside of it&r. Blood must be taken from a willing participant, and that means you! Jump 3 times to obtain enough Blood for 1 Bottle. Then, right click the Cauldron with a &bGlass Bottle&r to collect it."
	]
	quest.13B72F5C0CF9E9FB.title: "Obtain a Blood Sigil"
	quest.13C0DC76BB0AD7CB.quest_desc: [
		"You've entered the &aNether&r for the first time! We hope you enjoy your stay in this hostile environment. :)"
		""
		"You can use the reward from this quest to &aset your respawn point in the Nether&r, if you so choose. Simply &6place it down&r and &6feed it &bGlowstone&r."
	]
	quest.13C0DC76BB0AD7CB.quest_subtitle: "welcome to hell"
	quest.141887F26E89BAE8.quest_desc: ["&bRope&r can be used to make tools such as the &bSafety Net&r, which &anegates falling damage when landed on&r. It can also be crafted into &bRope Arrows&r, which will unroll a length of rope to the ground beneath where the arrow lands, allowing you to climb up it."]
	quest.141887F26E89BAE8.quest_subtitle: "Always practice rope safety"
	quest.141887F26E89BAE8.title: "Obtain Rope"
	quest.148F84D7DB06E5D1.quest_desc: ["Congratulations, you have compacted all of the crops! For your hard work, here is a reward."]
	quest.14B45702F0F82689.quest_desc: ["Defeat &eNaga&r in the &dTwilight Forest&r to obtain their scales. Then, relinquish those scales in exchange for loot!"]
	quest.14B45702F0F82689.quest_subtitle: "A chance to use unwanted scales"
	quest.14B45702F0F82689.title: "Purchase Quest: 20 Naga Scales"
	quest.151CAB60A18AA07C.quest_desc: ["These upgrades will help you &aprocess items in your storage&r, by smelting, blasting, or smoking. The &aautomatic versions&r will do so without the player needing to manually input the items."]
	quest.151CAB60A18AA07C.title: "Process Your Inventory"
	quest.152F190C5689B5C0.quest_desc: ["&eSporelings&r are cute little mushroom folk who primarily &alive in &cSwamps&r, and can be fed &bBone Meal&r!"]
	quest.152F190C5689B5C0.title: "Meet the Sporeling"
	quest.1539D3DAD97F8A1D.quest_desc: [
		"You will no doubt want something to &ahold all your tools&r, now that you are ready to draw like a professional. As reward for completing these quests, please take this &bPencil Case&r."
		""
		"The &bPencil Case&r can be opened by &6holding it and pressing shift + right click&r, at which point you can fill it with your tools! What a perfect fit."
	]
	quest.153DBE782905BF62.quest_desc: [
		"There have long been superstitions about whether &aphotography holds magical sway&r in our world. Some say photographs steal souls - others say they grant a form of immortality."
		""
		"Whatever you believe the power of the picture truly is, it cannot be denied that it &ais at least somewhat magical&r. The ability to capture light from a moment in time and look back on it long since it has passed? That's a small miracle without a doubt."
		""
		"You, too, can &acapture photos with a camera&r! &6Right click&r the camera to enter photo mode. From here, you can &6crouch&r to access the &aphoto settings&r - Focal Length, Shutter Speed, Flash Mode, and Composition Guides."
		""
		"But first, you'll need some &bFilm&r, and you can also upgrade your camera with &aother items&r!"
		""
		"Continued on next page."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Shift right click&r while holding the &bCamera&r to access the interface. Here you can load &bFilm&r - color, or black and white. You can also add the following:"
		""
		"- &bRedstone Lamp&r to add a &aflash&r"
		"- &bSpyglass&r to add a &azoom&r"
		"- &bGlass Pane&r to add &afilters&r"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/cameraui.png width:100 height:100 align:1 fit:true}"
	]
	quest.153DBE782905BF62.title: "Photography is Witchcraft"
	quest.1547891EBE53934F.quest_desc: [
		"The &bWrench&r is an item which can &arotate blocks&r. Just &6right click the block&r with the &bWrench&r, and it will adjust the position based on where you click it."
		""
		"Does not work on objects which have the same texture on all sides (such as planks)."
	]
	quest.15781BD4547097E9.quest_desc: ["Your bed might be a little bare-bones as is. Why not make a &bsheet&r and &bCushion&r to go on top? These can be &adyed any color you like&r."]
	quest.15781BD4547097E9.title: "Make Your Bed"
	quest.160EE610C4B660D8.quest_desc: ["&eGoblin Traders&r are friendly fellows who are always happy to do business with humans! They're not the smartest, though, so they tend to &aoffer deals&r that are quite good."]
	quest.160EE610C4B660D8.quest_subtitle: "Eager but not too bright"
	quest.160EE610C4B660D8.title: "Meet the Goblin Trader"
	quest.1641BFB24F43B94B.quest_desc: [
		"&bOtherwhere Chalk&r contains the essence of &cThe End&r, and is used for spells such as &aTransposition&r of either person or items."
		""
		"It is also an ingredient for &bPoppets&r."
	]
	quest.1661059D340835FC.quest_desc: ["The &bCommand Drum&r is an item which allows you to command multiple tamed creatures at one time."]
	quest.16797E1EF5450E7E.quest_desc: [
		"Villagers who have &abeen zombified and then cured&r will offer &asignificant discounts&r."
		""
		"Should you find a &eZombie Villager&r, &6hit them with a Splash Potion of Weakness&r, and then &6give them a golden apple&r. After a time, they will be cured!"
		""
		"Once you've done this, you will be rewarded with a &bConverter&r, which can be used to &aconvert zombie villagers automatically&r by providing it with a &bPotion of Weakness&r and a &bGolden Apple&r."
	]
	quest.16797E1EF5450E7E.quest_subtitle: "extreme couponing"
	quest.1689A10C4DBBE5B0.quest_desc: ["The first of these new items is called &bThe Old Eye&r, which once belonged to one of the now-extinct Great Sandworms. This sallow eye can be looted from &dDesert Temple&r chests."]
	quest.169272849A588544.title: "Eat Meef Stroganoff"
	quest.1698226644682207.quest_desc: [
		"There are three types of &bBrooms&r, &bWillow&r, &bWitch Hazel&r and &bMahogany&r. Of these, the Mahogany Broom is &afaster and fire-resistant&r. The Willow and Witch Hazel Brooms, on the other hand, are susceptible to fire, but are much &acheaper to make&r."
		""
		"You can &6crouch and right click&r your &bBroom&r in order to access its customization options, as well as switch it from &aFloat Mode&r to &aRest Mode&r, which determines what the Broom will do when you dismount."
		""
		"You will also need a &bBroom Whistle&r."
		""
		"Lost your broom? No worries! Just &6right click&r with your &bBroom Whistle&r to call it to you!"
		"First, you'll need to &6place the &bWhistle&6 and &bBroom&r in a crafting grid&r to bind them. You can &aunbind&r them by &6putting the &bWhistle&r in alone."
		""
		"Be aware that this &dworks best when your broom is in sight&r. It will try to fly to you, but it's just a broom so it's &anot very smart&r and often gets stuck on things."
	]
	quest.1698226644682207.quest_subtitle: "Any kind works!"
	quest.1698226644682207.title: "Make A Broom and Whistle"
	quest.16E1276D35BDE7D5.quest_desc: [
		"Now you take the thing, and the other thing, and you do the thing!"
		""
		"Which is to say, &6hold the &bPoppet&6 in your main hand&r and the &bTaglock Kit&6 in your offhand&r and &6hold right click&r until the two combine. Ta-da! Now you have a &bBound Poppet&r."
		""
		"In order to use this, the &bArmor Poppet&r needs to be either &ain your inventory or hotbar&r, or &aon a &bPoppet Shelf&r. Take these materials, they'll help you for the next step..."
	]
	quest.16E1276D35BDE7D5.title: "Advanced Poppetry"
	quest.171D4EACF7B9F4D5.quest_desc: [
		"This modpack adds a lot of new sounds. So to help you filter the ones you don't like, it also includes &aSuper Sound Muffler&r."
		""
		"&6Press F6 to open the menu&r. From here, you can click &aRecent&r to see what you've recently heard. You can play the sound to confirm it's the one you don't like, and then &6mute it!&r"
	]
	quest.171D4EACF7B9F4D5.quest_subtitle: "Selective hearing. Literally."
	quest.171D4EACF7B9F4D5.title: "Extreme Sound Muffler"
	quest.17348DDF7E369519.quest_desc: [
		"This pack has a lot of &bkeybindings&r, so to help you manage them better, we have organized a few &bKeybind Bundles&r!"
		""
		"They are marked in red in the image below. To use them, &6hold down the hotkey&r and then &bLeft Click the option you want&r. You can also configure it to activate the macro upon hotkey release instead, if you wish."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/keybindatlas.png width:345 height:271 align:center fit:true click_action:none:}"
	]
	quest.178EB94C72B16D88.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Bucket of Tadpole"
	quest.17B0994740977E5A.quest_desc: [
		"The &bChicken Coop&r is a block in which &ayour chickens can live&r! Similar to a &bBeehive&r, your chickens will pop inside, lay eggs, and leave when they feel like it."
		""
		"You can &aeject your chickens&r by &6right clicking a &bPitchfork&r onto the &bCoop&r."
		""
		"Note that currently &da bug makes it so that if a coop is broken and placed elsewhere, its chickens will never enter it - or any other coop - again&r."
	]
	quest.181F5C00C8DE417B.quest_desc: ["Vegetarian? No worries, we got you covered! Why not make some delicious &avegetarian dishes?&r"]
	quest.181F5C00C8DE417B.title: "Delicious Veggies"
	quest.182C1C3812C31B0B.quest_desc: [
		"One of the most important tools in a witch's bag is their &bLibrary&r, in which they learn about the magical world around them, and also record their knowledge and experience as they follow their path!"
		""
		"As it so happens, you &dalready own these books, they are in your &bEccentric Tome&r. &6Select each book, shift and press Q&r to eject them and get credit for this quest's tasks."
		""
		"There are several primary mods which grant you magical powers: &lHexerei&r, &lEnchanted&r, &lHexalia&r, and &lRoots&r. In this modpack, they are &awoven together to provide a cohesive experience&r, and as such may surprise you if you've played them before."
		""
		"&lHexerei's&r &bBook of Shadows&r will serve as a reference for the mechanics of that mod, and &lEnchanted's&r &bArt of Witchcraft&r - and the other volumes you'll discover as you go - will do the same for that mod. When the mechanics of the mods diverge from the guidebooks, &dthese quests will provide you the correct steps&r."
		""
		"&dNote&r: Books are important in real life, as well! &aIf you are interested in modern witchcraft&r, I recommend the following books:"
		""
		"&oWitchery&r, by Juliet Diaz"
		""
		"&oThe Witch's Path&r, by Thorn Mooney"
	]
	quest.182C1C3812C31B0B.quest_subtitle: "books are a witch's best friend"
	quest.182C1C3812C31B0B.title: "Happy Witch: Books"
	quest.184493C9F7227C64.title: "Happy Witch: Garden [Part 2]"
	quest.187BD92930BA8670.quest_desc: [
		"There is little point trying to mine through the incredibly tough blocks of the Labyrinth. Unless, however, you loot this item: &bThe Mazebreaker&r."
		"This tool mines Labyrinth blocks faster, and with less durability loss, than any other. It can be looted from the Labyrinth chests."
	]
	quest.187BD92930BA8670.quest_subtitle: "Now why would you break a perfectly good maze?"
	quest.187BD92930BA8670.title: "Obtain the Mazebreaker"
	quest.187EB99C04A3BE37.quest_desc: [
		"There are two types of eraser - &bregular&r and &bkneaded&r."
		""
		"The &bEraser&r is rather self explanatory, however - a &bKneaded Eraser&r is softer and allows you to only partially erase something, in case you want it just a bit lighter."
		""
		"Note that everything, including markers, can be erased!"
	]
	quest.187EB99C04A3BE37.title: "Erasers"
	quest.18B7D6B02C97FF23.quest_desc: [
		"A skilled farmer doesn't just wait for nature to take her course - they help it along! One of the ways you can do this is through &bFertilizer&r. Now, you may have already encountered this, but &bBone Meal&r no longer works the way you may be used to. Although it can still be used &aon grass&r, and to &aduplicate small flowers&r, if you want to grow &bSaplings&r or &bCrops&r with it, you will want &bFertilizer&r!"
		""
		"You can craft a single &bFertilizer&r by &6inserting rotten flesh&r to either the &bSilo&r or the &bMincer&r (the latter is much faster but requires manual grinding). Then, if you wish, you can make that Fertilizer &amore potent by aging it&r. Place the &bFertilizer&r in a &bAging Cask&r with some organic matter such as &bTree Bark&r or &bStraw&r, and &await for nature to take her course&r."
		""
		"What? What do you mean, I just said not to do that? Oh. So I did. Well, you can always use &bTime in a Bottle&r to help it along, little guppy..."
	]
	quest.18D433FB887CE31B.quest_desc: [
		"The &bPoppet Shelf&r is a place for you to safely store your &bPoppets&r while still having them &aprovide their effects while out in the world&r."
		""
		"The exception to this is the &bVoodoo Poppet&r, which we'll cover elsewhere in the chapter."
	]
	quest.18D433FB887CE31B.quest_subtitle: "don't be shelf-ish"
	quest.18D433FB887CE31B.title: "Obtain a Poppet Shelf"
	quest.18E1F3797BC552D0.quest_desc: ["Every time you go Starcatching, there is a 1% chance that you will catch a &bGolden variant&r of the fish you're reeling in! Equip the &bGold Hook&r and &bGold Bobber&r to increase those chances ever so slightly."]
	quest.18E1F3797BC552D0.title: "Golden Fish"
	quest.18FD7541912B5772.quest_desc: ["Create some &bMixed Seeds&r in order to tame &eWild Ravens&r. Once you tame a Raven Familiar, they will help you with tasks around your hut!"]
	quest.18FD7541912B5772.quest_subtitle: "Squawk goals"
	quest.18FD7541912B5772.title: "Mix some Seeds in your Mortar"
	quest.196ECF57CAC465DF.quest_desc: ["Hidden away in &cSwamps&r is the &cDark Coven&r, a city of &eWitches&r who are up to no good. If you are &6wearing their robes&r, they will ignore you. But anyone not perceived to be one of them is considered an enemy."]
	quest.196ECF57CAC465DF.title: "Discover the Dark Coven"
	quest.19ED6330FD3E968C.quest_desc: [
		"Normally, to get to &dThe End&r requires regular old &bEnder Eyes&r, for both seeking and filling the portal frames. However, magic has warped this world, making it more difficult to face the final dimension."
		"There are, instead, 16 other eyes (of which you need 12), which can be found in various ways. &6See the following quests&r for more information on them."
	]
	quest.19ED6330FD3E968C.quest_subtitle: "I've got my eye on the End"
	quest.19ED6330FD3E968C.title: "Obtain an End Eye"
	quest.1ACFAAF917E5016A.quest_desc: ["While we're gearing up like bees (bee-ring up? No, no... sorry), why not &acraft some of their weaponry&r?"]
	quest.1ACFAAF917E5016A.title: "Bee Weaponry"
	quest.1AFE0FBF887D22FD.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBuilding Gadget&r is a useful tool for building larger structures quickly. It &aplaces multiple blocks at once&a from your inventory. &6Shift right click a block in world&r to set that as your building block."
		""
		"The &bExchanging Gadget&r is a tool which will &areplace blocks in the world with a specific block from your inventory&r. As with the BG, &6shift right click the replacer block&r and then you can &6right click with the gadget&r."
	]
	quest.1AFE0FBF887D22FD.quest_subtitle: "The Building Gadget and Exchanging Gadget"
	quest.1AFE0FBF887D22FD.title: "Gadgets, Part 1"
	quest.1B36681F6C07B478.quest_desc: [
		"Collecting lots of water or lava but don't want to carry all those buckets? The &bTank Upgrade&r allows you to &6add and remove buckets of fluid from the tank&r, storing far more while only sacrificing a few slots of the backpack. &bStack Upgrades&r also increase your tank size."
		""
		"Going on a deep mining trip with your mending tools? Consider equipping the tank alongside an &bExperience Pump&r to store exp and dish it out as needed. Keep in mind, you will need to &dfully empty the previous fluid&r before using the pump."
		""
		"To get the most of these upgrades, we suggest &6checking out the settings tab&r for each one. "
		""
		"Your settings will be saved for each upgrade &aeven if you remove it.&r"
	]
	quest.1B36681F6C07B478.quest_subtitle: "baby got camelback"
	quest.1B36681F6C07B478.title: "Fluid On The Go"
	quest.1B8E61A0872EEA1C.quest_desc: [
		"Inside the &dLich Tower&r is the undead noble of the Twilight Forest. His &aCastle&r is fraught with mobs, but also filled with loot."
		""
		"It is recommended to be well-geared before attempting this structure."
		""
		"At the top of the tower, you will find the &eLich&r, who is surrounded by a shield which protects him. &6He must be defeated first with his own magic&r, then martial might can finish the fight."
		""
		"And beware of the copies he summons during the fight!"
		""
		"Defeating the &eLich&r grants you access to the &dYeti's Lair&r, the &dDark Forest&r, and the &dSwamp&r."
		""
		"Also, make sure you have your &bCamera&r - you'll need it for the next quest."
	]
	quest.1B8E61A0872EEA1C.quest_subtitle: "Where my liches at?"
	quest.1BCBFB8A5AAE9E37.quest_desc: ["A &bStrawberry Cupcake&r is one of many things you can make with &bSweet Dough&r, and also uses the delicious &bStrawberry Jam&r you made in the last quest!"]
	quest.1C37EDEA99A890EF.quest_desc: ["The &bDeed of Ownership&r is an item used in &amultiplayer&r. You can &6right click it on an animal&r and then give the &bDeed&r to a friend. When they use it, the pet will now be linked to them, &aas if they had tamed it themself&r."]
	quest.1D27E531CF01450E.quest_desc: [
		"The &bApothecary Cauldron&r is a unique and delightful alternative to traditional &apotion brewing&r. The modern witch is handy with a potion or two, but why not challenge yourself with some &afreeform potion making&r? Not only does the &bApothecary Cauldron&r allow you to brew more powerful effects (such as &abroomless flight&r!), but it also comes with a complimentary &bApothecary Mortar&r."
		""
		"&lHow it works&r:"
		"1. Grind 2–3 ingredients in your new &bApothecary Mortar&r to create Potion Essence"
		"2. Place Potion Essence + nether wart + water in the &bApothecary Cauldron&r"
		"3. Put fire or a heat source below the cauldron"
		"4. After some time, it will outputs &bCondensed Potion&r, which can be collected in a &bCondensed Vial&r"
		""
		"&lWhat it makes&r: Custom potions unlike regular vanilla ones!"
	]
	quest.1D27E531CF01450E.title: "Apothecary Cauldron \\& Mortar"
	quest.1D28D1DF0BA0F0D6.quest_desc: ["The &bFramed Reinforcement&r is an item which, when &6right clicked on a &bFramed Block&r, will &agrant it &bBlast Resistance&r."]
	quest.1E1E47B50314B64A.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Cookies"
	quest.1E43FCEBA416DCFF.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know you can &apin quests&r so they &ashow on your main screen&r? You can!"
		""
		"Just &dbe warned that this overlaps your pinned Notes&r."
		""
		"Also, perhaps I should mention that you can &apin notes&r to your screen as well! &6Press N to access your Notes menu&r."
	]
	quest.1E43FCEBA416DCFF.title: "Pinning Other Things"
	quest.1E53C205AD76513E.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBlackboard&r will allow you to draw a 16x16 black and white image. Perfect for creative signage!"
		""
		"It will &aretain its image when broken&r, but can be crafted with a &bWater Bucket&r to clear it."
	]
	quest.1E53C205AD76513E.quest_subtitle: "Finally, your schoolhouse will be complete"
	quest.1F389C8E9F4CFB59.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you've got your artifact, the next step is to &aidentify the spell&r! &6Right clicking your artifact&r on an &bArcheology Table&r will complete this quest - though to actually identify, just &6insert your new artifact&r into the &bTable&r along with a &bBrush&r, and all the hard work is done for you!"
		""
		"Your enchantment is now identified and ready to use. If you'd like to translate its name, you can simply &6right-click your &bIdentified Artifact&r onto an &bEnchantment table&r, just like any other book!"
	]
	quest.1F389C8E9F4CFB59.quest_subtitle: "zoom in. zoom in. enhance. "
	quest.1F389C8E9F4CFB59.title: "Identify an Artifact"
	quest.1F4569590B7666F5.quest_desc: [
		"The &bNature's Compass&r is a magical tool, similar to a &bDowsing Rod&r, which will allow you to find your way to a particular type of biome."
		"Simply &6right click while holding it&r in order to search for the biome you want to find."
	]
	quest.1F4569590B7666F5.title: "Find Biomes with the Nature's Compass"
	quest.1F80DCFD23DD5592.quest_desc: ["With some delicious &bPeanuts&r, you can make &bPeanut Butter&r. Combine that with some fresh-reduced &bJam&r and some &bBread&r and you've got yourself a nutritionally sound, delicious lunch."]
	quest.1F80DCFD23DD5592.quest_subtitle: "A classic meal for both depression and joy"
	quest.1F80DCFD23DD5592.title: "PBJ Deliciousness"
	quest.1F8B3B9C1641187E.quest_desc: [
		"Once you &6enter the dimension&r, you may be struck by its majesty. Confounded by its splendor! Enchanted by its inhabitants! And... maybe wondering how you get back home."
		""
		"To &aexit the Bumblezone&r, you can either dig &cdown past y level zero&r or &cup above 7 level 255&r. You can also &6use /home&r or &6use this &bWarp Scroll&r to go to a &bWaypoint&r."
		""
		"You can also &ause a &bMap&r to help your exploration!"
		""
		"The &cBumblezone&r contains 8 biomes: &cHive Wall&r, &cHive Pillar&r, &cSugar Water Floor&r, &cCrystal Canyon&r, &cPollinated Fields&r, &cPollinated Pillar&r, &cFloral Meadow&r, and &cHowling Constructs&r. These are distributed &aboth vertically and horizontally&r, so take care if using a &bNature's Compass&r."
		""
		"Generally, Hive Wall Biome creates the flat walls of the dimension. Hive Pillar biome creates the large support columns that upholds the space. Sugar Water Floor takes up the rest of the space with low land and filled with Sugar Water. The other biomes such as Crystal Canyon, Pollinated Fields, Floral Meadow, and Howling Constructs can be found scattered throughout the dimension, so start exploring!"
		""
		"Within the dimension, &eBees&r spawn frequently, but you can also uncommonly find &dHoney Slimes&r, and even more rarely, a &eBeehemoth&r. In &cFloral Meadows&r, you can meet &eRootmin&r!"
	]
	quest.1F8B3B9C1641187E.quest_subtitle: "home of the humble bumble"
	quest.1F8B3B9C1641187E.title: "Enter the Bumblezone"
	quest.1FD157BDA5AF3BE9.quest_desc: ["Obtain all vanilla music discs."]
	quest.1FD157BDA5AF3BE9.quest_subtitle: "I can't get this song out of my head!"
	quest.1FD157BDA5AF3BE9.title: "Music Lover"
	quest.1FDD653A3C13DFDF.quest_desc: ["Wow, you've caught 999 fish? That's bonkers."]
	quest.1FDD653A3C13DFDF.quest_subtitle: "so long and thanks for all the fish"
	quest.1FDD653A3C13DFDF.title: "Catch Em All (and Then Some)"
	quest.203124368972BE74.quest_desc: ["Use your &bSpyglass&r to research 10 &bPlants&r!"]
	quest.203C69CA13DFF734.quest_desc: ["Buy yourself a brand new &bBody Curios Slot&r!"]
	quest.203C69CA13DFF734.title: "New Body Slot"
	quest.207C60DC8889AC0F.quest_desc: [
		"To begin with the delicious art of &aBakery&r, there are a few tools one will need. The &bCaking Station&r, the &bSimmer Pot&r, the &bCrafting Bowl&r, and, of course, an &bOven&r. We'll begin with the &bCaking Station&r and the &bOven&r."
		""
		"Each of these tools will allow you to do unique things."
		""
		"The &bOven&r allows you to bake &bBreads&r, &bBuns&r, &bTarts&r, and &bmore&r!"
		""
		"The &bCaking Station&r is for the creation of &bCakes&r, &bCookies&r, and &bCupcakes&r! To use the &bCaking Station&r, you must &6right click to place the &bCake Dough&r on top! Then you'll &6right click&r the &bBlank Cake&r with the desired items."
	]
	quest.207C60DC8889AC0F.quest_subtitle: "let's bake it happen"
	quest.207C60DC8889AC0F.title: "Baking Time"
	quest.20857C9F84A08F08.title: "Tarot Cards 2"
	quest.2086E3E58435ED32.quest_desc: ["This quest only exists to give you some &bCod&r so you can &atame a cat when you meet one&r."]
	quest.2086E3E58435ED32.quest_subtitle: "this cod is for you"
	quest.2086E3E58435ED32.title: "Meet the Cat"
	quest.2093240CD42882CF.quest_desc: [
		"Scattered around the world, you can find &bWild Crops&r growing. Find all of them to build your &alovely witchy garden&r!"
		""
		"Did you know that even vegetables can be used in household magic? For example, &bCorn&r hung over a mirror will bring good luck to your household. Or, you can take a small white &bOnion&r and stick it full of black-headed pins, and when placed in the window, this will protect against negativity. Or! You can eat some &bGarlic&r and then when you go to close to others, they will hold their nose."
		""
		"Click to the next page for information on &awhich items can be found where&r!"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&bWild Tomatoes&r can be found in &chot, dry biomes&r."
		""
		"&bWild Rice&r can be found growing in &bwater&r in &cwet biomes&r."
		""
		"&bWild Cabbages&r can be found in &cbeach biomes&r."
		""
		"&bWild Coffee&r can be found in &cthe Nether&r!"
		""
		"&bOnions&r, &bCarrots&r, and &bPotatoes&r can be found in most any biome!"
		""
		"&bBarley&r can be found in &cPlains&r and &cSavannahs&r."
		""
		"&bEmmer&r is located in &cForests&r."
		""
		"&bOats&r are found in &cTaiga&r biomes."
		""
		"&bCorn&r can be found in &cSavannah&r and &cBadlands&r biomes."
		""
		"&bNettles&r and &bRibwort&r spawn in &cSwamps&r and &cMangrove Swamps&r."
		""
		"&bBlueberries&r, &bRaspberries&r, and &bPeanuts&r come from &ctemperate overworld biomes&r, so think plains, forests, meadows, birch forests."
		""
		"&bWild Green Grapes&r come from &chot biomes&r: savannas, deserts, badlands, jungles."
		""
		"&bWild Red Grapes&r are from &ccold biomes&r: taiga, snowy plains, etc."
		""
		"&bWild Cotton&r can be found in &csavanna&r, &cbadlands&r, etc."
	]
	quest.2093240CD42882CF.title: "Forage Wild Crops"
	quest.20BAF307F1556BC5.quest_desc: [
		"This delightful item not only &aplays a lovely tune&r when you &6hold right click while holding it&r, but it also &asummons all non-sitting pets nearby&r to your location."
		""
		"You can optionally bind your flute to a specific pet by &6shift right clicking&r on the animal with the flute."
	]
	quest.20BAF307F1556BC5.quest_subtitle: "This is literally so adorable"
	quest.20F9C02AF5CBE665.quest_desc: [
		"FTB Teams allows you to add other players to your party, which can allow you to &ashare quest progress&r if desired, and also &aallow access to your claimed chunks&r."
		""
		"The Teams screen is accessible in the &ctop left of your inventory&r. From there, you can &acreate a party&r. You can invite others if you want to share quest progress, otherwise you can simply add other players as allies via the &bManage Allies&r screen."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/ftbmenu.png width:200 height:150 align:1}"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/createaparty.png width:100 height:75 align:1 fit:true}"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/manageallies.png width:200 height:150 align:1}"
		""
		"Note that &din order for Deployers and such to work in claimed chunks&r, you have to &6allow Fake Player access&r via FTB Teams. Press E and click on \"My Team\" in the top left. Then click the gear in the top right, and you'll see this menu:"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/fakeplayers.png width:871 height:342 align:1 fit:true}"
		""
		"Set \"Allow All Fake Players\" to true."
	]
	quest.217230971261385C.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Crying Obsidian"
	quest.2186A6F69ADBE795.quest_desc: [
		"They say not to waste your diamonds on a hoe. But you've taken this a step further."
		""
		"To honor your commitment, please take this reward."
	]
	quest.21A12DEE3432EF7F.quest_desc: ["In order to obtain &bStrider Slices&r, you need to slay &eStriders&r with a &bKnife&r. It's quite tragic, really. But if you do so, you can &6cook them as they are&r, or place the Slices on the &bCutting Board&r to obtain &bGround Strider&r, which has further recipe uses."]
	quest.21A12DEE3432EF7F.quest_subtitle: "Heartless!"
	quest.21BCCEDD06A1C052.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to &zCrazy Joe's Paper Emporium&r - where we sell &bPaper&b at &zCRAZY PRICES&r!!"
		""
		"Yes, that's right, you can get &l16 whole Paper&r for only &b3 Spurs&r!!!!!one1!!! A price so low, you'd have to be CRAZY!!!"
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		""
		"&8my wife left me and i'm so alone please buy my paper&r"
	]
	quest.21BCCEDD06A1C052.title: "16 Paper"
	quest.223792FEBB2154CA.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Egg"
	quest.2249A1823E842BAB.quest_desc: [
		"Do you want to &abe an artist&r in addition to a practitioner? Well, I should warn you that it's a rigorous process! Not anyone can just waltz in and say they belong to the same category as the great masters!!"
		""
		"In order to become a &zReal Artist&r (TM), you must complete this list of tasks!!"
		""
		"1. Make some art"
		""
		"..."
		""
		"Yeah, that's all. You do not have to be good, you do not have to be prolific, you do not have to have experience. &dIf you make art, you are an artist, period&r."
		""
		"So with that in mind, take this reward and &ago do the other quests&r."
	]
	quest.226368447EC1C9A9.quest_desc: ["Sick of boring old flat beds? Make a &afancy one&r! To craft a &bBed&r, you'll need planks, wool, and &ba Cushion&r!"]
	quest.226368447EC1C9A9.title: "Customize Your Bed"
	quest.226D1B09B2958EFC.quest_desc: [
		"This modpack has a number of building and decoration mods which are all worth looking into. &dMost of them do not have associated quests&r."
		""
		"So how are you supposed to know they're there? Why, &lJEI&r of course. &6Opening your inventory&r will show you a wall of items to your right. You can search through these items at the bottom right. Type &d@&r and the name of a mod to search for only items from that mod."
		""
		"For example, you can &asearch \"@whimsy\"&r to view everything from &lWhimsy Deco&r. &6Left click the item&r to view its crafting recipe. &6Right click it&r to view what recipes it's used in."
		""
		"This will let you view how to make anything in the game!"
	]
	quest.226D1B09B2958EFC.quest_subtitle: "Take a little look-see"
	quest.226D1B09B2958EFC.title: "Window Shopping"
	quest.2288D26992644668.quest_desc: [
		"These &bGlass Item Frames&r display items on a surface just like the normal kind, but they will &abecome invisible&r once they have an item inside them."
		""
		"&6Place a Banner inside&r to display its pattern on that block."
	]
	quest.2288D26992644668.title: "Invisible Frames"
	quest.229F4C47C5A09466.quest_desc: [
		"I don't have any way of verifying that you actually did this quest, so I guess you can cheat if you want to."
		""
		"But if you do actually finish a painting, then I'm very proud of you, and you've earned this reward! Hopefully, your painting is better than mine."
	]
	quest.22ECD917EB584573.quest_desc: [
		"Once you've &acollected all the different fossils&r, you can &6craft their combined versions&r! These can be used as display items."
		""
		"They may even have other features!"
	]
	quest.22ECD917EB584573.quest_subtitle: "put them back together"
	quest.22ECD917EB584573.title: "Completed Fossils"
	quest.230F870FB86A18B6.quest_desc: ["Similar to the &bPickarang&r, this item can be used to &amine blocks&r and &adefeat enemies&r. However, it also has an &aauto-smelting&r function!"]
	quest.232A634140B19B03.quest_desc: [
		"To make a &bGrove&r, you'll first need &bGrove Stones&r, which can be crafted on the &bGrove Crafter&r once you've obtained sufficient &areputation&r. However, unlike the &bWild Grove Stone&r, these will not immediately be active once placed."
		""
		"Instead, you must &6perform the &bGrove Supplication&r ritual. For this, you will need the following:"
		""
		""
		"- &bA Door&r, any kind will do, this symbolizes opening new opportunities."
		"- &bBread&r, as an offering to the fount."
		"- &bA Sapling&r of some kind, symbolizing growth."
		"- &bA Flower&r of some kind, symbolizing dedication."
		"- &bA Bowl&r, to hold your offerings."
		""
		"Place these items on your &bPyre&r and &6light it with &bFlint and Steel&r - then &dwait patiently&r for the ritual to complete!"
	]
	quest.232A634140B19B03.title: "Making a Grove"
	quest.232A8F9F6388C377.quest_desc: [
		"Axolotls are cute lil guys, but they're also &astrong&r and &avicious&r. If you tame one, it will &afight alongside you&r should you decide to take on an underwater threat."
		""
		"They'll also sometimes &agive you Regeneration&r, and once they do so, you'll know that you are &dbest friends 5ever&r."
	]
	quest.2356716DE94666CF.quest_desc: ["The &bCursed Eye&r is found within the &dTreasure Bastion&r’s chests. It is a powerful, destructive artifact which the Piglins will defend with their lives."]
	quest.236484A484723F55.quest_desc: ["Make yourself a &bRaw Stuffed Hoglin&r and &6place it in a &bCooking Pot&r with some other tasty ingredients, to create a &bStuffed Hoglin&r, which can be placed down and eaten as the centerpiece of the most indulgent feast!"]
	quest.236484A484723F55.title: "Stuff a Hoglin"
	quest.238028A4423EAF3F.quest_desc: ["&bNether Chalk&r is an advanced form of ritual chalk which calls upon &athe spirit of the Nether&r. It is used largely to cast &bCurses&r, or, if you like to make things very complicated, to &acook food&r. Beware burning it, however."]
	quest.23E5790A6CC6524C.quest_desc: ["Earn yourself some loot by slaying a few Hydras and trading in their blood for something valuable!"]
	quest.23E5790A6CC6524C.quest_subtitle: "A chance to use unwanted blood"
	quest.23E5790A6CC6524C.title: "Purchase Quest: 20 Fiery Blood"
	quest.24993E3FC9E3BA2D.quest_desc: [
		"You want to make &bArt&r? You'll need &bColor&r. Whether you're &apainting&r, &asketching&r, or &adeveloping color photos&r, you'll need lots of &bDye&r."
		""
		"Collecting one of each kind will reward you with more!"
		""
		"[ \"You can also purchase more dye from our \", { \"text\": \"Mail Order Catalogue\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"4971EB753FE0E6CC\" } }]"
	]
	quest.24993E3FC9E3BA2D.quest_subtitle: "omg i'm literally dyeing rn"
	quest.24993E3FC9E3BA2D.title: "Obtain One of Each Dye"
	quest.2499CAE3934539A8.quest_desc: [
		"You did it! You beat the game. Congrats, you can all go home now."
		"...."
		"...."
		"...oh, you're staying. Well, hooray! Maybe check out the other quests, since you're here!"
	]
	quest.24C19E2033095FFA.quest_desc: ["The &bMortar and Pestle&r is a tool for grinding herbs. It will allow you to &amake &bSeed Mixture&r for taming &eRavens&r, craft &bmagical ingredients&r, and most importantly - &aconcoct new spells&r!"]
	quest.24C19E2033095FFA.quest_subtitle: "pester a mortal"
	quest.24C19E2033095FFA.title: "Obtain a Pestle and Mortar"
	quest.252C5BD652764DB8.quest_desc: ["You've found a &aLittle Joy&r! The &lLittle Joys&r mod provides little &adig spots&r, &afishing boost spots&r, and more! Seek them out and get a little extra reward out of your day. :)"]
	quest.257F1DCDEC619664.quest_desc: ["The &bReplacer Satchel&r is incredibly useful, as it will &areplace broken &bBroom Brushes&r with ones in its inventory, beginning with the &6top left&r."]
	quest.25CB8D0869249D24.quest_desc: ["Once you complete the &eFinal Castle&r, obtained the &bLamp of Cinders&r, and even &6Completed the &eQuest Ram&r, you will finally have earned this unique armor set. Wear it with pride!"]
	quest.25CB8D0869249D24.title: "Complete the Twilight Forest"
	quest.25EF8B31172278DA.quest_desc: [
		"The &bRitual Braziers&r are &acarved from &bPlanks&r by &6right clicking them with an &bAthame&r."
		""
		"Once they have been &acarved&r, you must &aanoint them with &bSalt&r before offerings can be placed atop them. Should you do this in the wrong order, you can &aretrieve items from a &bBrazier&r by &6right clicking with an empty hand&r."
	]
	quest.2602582F440361DB.quest_desc: [
		"The &cCell Maze&r is a structure which is filled with &aunique loot&r such as &bBee Armor&r, and will also give you something to help lead you to &aThe Queen&r. These mazes are normally located at &csea level&r."
		""
		"Entering the Maze without &bProtection of the Hive&r or having consumed the &bEssence of Bees&r (an endgame item) will give you &bWrath of the Hive&r, so be careful! Make sure to bring plenty of &asweet things&r to feed to &eBees&r and &bBrood Blocks&r!"
	]
	quest.2602582F440361DB.title: "Find the Cell Maze"
	quest.2615CD06E32EC741.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCooking Pot&r will allow you to make uniquely filling and delicious dishes! The more different foods you try, the &amore hearts you'll gain&r, making this an important tool for the kitchen witch adventurer."
		""
		"Place the &bCooking Pot&r on top of a heat source such as &bfire&r, &bcampfire&r, &bmagma block&r, or &bstove&r, to heat it. Then, &6place your ingredients inside&r."
		""
		"You'll also need something to serve your dish in, such as a &bbowl&r, &bbottle&r, or a &bpumpkin&r!"
		""
		"When the &bCooking Pot&r is broken, it retains its contents."
	]
	quest.2615CD06E32EC741.quest_subtitle: "Despite the name, it's not for cooking pot."
	quest.2615CD06E32EC741.title: "Obtain a Cooking Pot"
	quest.264135E887281098.quest_desc: ["The &bMarket&r is a stall which allows you to &abuy seeds, soils, and saplings&r without needing to traverse the whole world finding them. However, this convenience will cost a pretty &bgem or two&r."]
	quest.264135E887281098.title: "The Stalk Market"
	quest.26D8EAD9D892805E.quest_desc: [
		"If you want your base to stay active even when you're not there, you want &achunk loading&r. This will also help if you &ahave a vanilla-style mob farm&r."
		""
		"Open your inventory and look at the top left of your screen. The &amap icon&r will lead you to the &aFTB Chunks&r screen."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/ftbmenu.png width:200 height:150 align:1}"
		""
		"Choose &bClaimed Chunks&r and &6left click&r on a chunk to claim it for your own. To unclaim, &bright click&r it. To &aload the chunk when you're not in it&r, &6shift and left click the claimed chunk&r. You can unload it by holding &6shift and right clicking&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/claimchunks.png width:200 height:120 align:1}"
		""
		"When a chunk is claimed, &dother server members cannot break or interact with blocks in it&r. In order to grant someone access to your chunks, you need to &aadd them or their Team as an Ally&r."
	]
	quest.26D8EAD9D892805E.quest_subtitle: "When you're away, your base will play"
	quest.26D8EAD9D892805E.title: "Chunk Loading"
	quest.26E52D95C9C75019.quest_desc: ["Swimming in &bEggs&r? That sounds unpleasant. You can &atrade in a &bDragon Egg&r to receive a &bDragon Head&r."]
	quest.26E52D95C9C75019.quest_subtitle: "you egghead"
	quest.26E52D95C9C75019.title: "Getting Ahead in the End"
	quest.26E8A9DFDC4C1635.quest_desc: ["If you manage to defeat 500 &eWither Skeletons&r, then you deserve this reward: a &bWither Skeleton Spawn Egg&r, and a &bSpawner&r to put it in."]
	quest.26FD7EF75B2303E8.quest_desc: ["The &bTrial Eye&r was once part of a being called &eArgos the Watcher&r, who presided over &aTrial Chambers&r. Argos had many such eyes, and used them to determine whether challengers were true of heart. Received as a reward from the Ominous Vault in the &cTrial Chambers&r while under the effect of &bTrial Omen&b."]
	quest.2742C01D29A1E90A.quest_desc: [
		"The &bNetherite Upgrade&r is the most impressive drawer upgrade available, allowing you to store a &amultiplicative 32 times&r the base storage amount, or extend the &bController&r's range by 8 blocks."
		""
		"What are you going to store?"
	]
	quest.2742C01D29A1E90A.title: "Fully Upgraded"
	quest.279947E4FB1A366F.quest_desc: ["Catch one each of the &cOcean&r fish to complete this quest."]
	quest.279947E4FB1A366F.quest_subtitle: "ocean commotion"
	quest.279947E4FB1A366F.title: "Catch Ocean Fish"
	quest.27A6A7ADD9B0A8AE.quest_desc: [
		"The &eLuggage&r, when &astruck by lightning&r, will have its inventory increased."
		""
		"You can use a good, old-fashioned &bLightning Rod&r for this, but you can also use &aanything which summons lightning&r."
	]
	quest.27A6A7ADD9B0A8AE.title: "Upgrade your Luggage"
	quest.27AFCBF70AA24760.title: "Defeat the Aurora Snow Queen"
	quest.286F4DD16E3755B0.quest_desc: ["Got extra fur lying around? Why not turn some in here for cold, hard cash."]
	quest.286F4DD16E3755B0.quest_subtitle: "a chance to use unwanted fur"
	quest.286F4DD16E3755B0.title: "Purchase Quest: 5 Alpha Yeti Fur"
	quest.289832F0B384ABA7.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have &abound your &cSoulhome&r, it's a good idea to set up a &bMailbox&r. Many quest rewards in this modpack will be &adelivered to your mailbox&r rather than clutter up your inventory."
		""
		"You can tell which way a reward will be delivered by &aviewing the reward's icon&r. If the icon shows a sub-icon like a &bRed Packet&r or a &bParcel&r, it will arrive to your &bMailbox&r."
		""
		"The reward from this quest is a &bHearth Recall&r - a rune which, when activated, will &aallow you to either set your home or teleport there&r. In order to switch between Binding and Teleporting modes, &6shift right click&r the item."
		""
		"&dPlaying on a multiplayer team?&r This quest also gives you a &bTeam Binding Card&r, which you can &6crouch-click onto your mailbox&r to have your team's winnings sent there! Anything mailed before then will wait and arrive once it's bound. Lost the card? Grab another from the &6sidebar button&r in your questbook."
	]
	quest.289832F0B384ABA7.title: "Choose a Mailbox"
	quest.28ABA60CD070005E.quest_desc: [
		"To use color in your &bSketches&r, you'll need &bColored Pencils&r and/or &bMarkers&r!"
		""
		"These can be filled with all vanilla dye colors by &6right clicking the &bDye&r onto the &bEmpty Marker/Pencil&r &6in your inventory&r. Then, you can select &aany color&r from the &bColor Wheel in the bottom right&r in your Sketching interface."
	]
	quest.290D8441BBC918A1.quest_desc: ["Collect one each of every flower in the game to earn rewards!"]
	quest.290D8441BBC918A1.title: "Flower Picking: Purple"
	quest.292B26978E644D9F.quest_desc: [
		"The &bExplorer's Compass&r replaces &bEnder Eyes&r as the primary way to locate &aStrongholds and other Structures&r."
		""
		"Simply &6right click while holding it&r in order to search for the structure you want to find."
	]
	quest.292B26978E644D9F.title: "Find Structures with the Explorer's Compass"
	quest.293AFFA188D96753.quest_desc: [
		"Introspection is a good thing - why not &ado some Soul searching&r? Literally. Use the &bSoul Key&r to enter a tiny pocket dimension &ainside yourself&r."
		""
		"With the &bSoulKey&r in your main hand, &6hold down right click&r for a few seconds to open a portal to your innermost being."
		""
		"It's a surprisingly pleasant place! Some sunshine, grass, flowers, and even a small pond. It's an excellent place to &abegin a garden&r or &borganize your goods&r as you explore. And you can easily put down a &bCrafting Table&r and a &bFurnace&r without the need to pick them back up when it's time to move on!"
		""
		"&dWant to invite others to your &bSoulHome&r? Craft a &bBound Soul Key&r and gift it to them (perhaps via mailbox)!"
		""
		"This quest's reward allows you to choose the mailbox in the color of your dreams~! Once you place the mailbox, &6crouch right click with empty hands&r to claim it."
		""
		"And don't forget to check out the quest on &dLoading Chunks&r to keep your garden and furnace active while you're away!"
		""
		"🔗 Click below to view the relevant quest:"
		"[{\"text\": \"Loading Chunks\", \"clickEvent\": {\"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"26D8EAD9D892805E\"}}]"
	]
	quest.293AFFA188D96753.quest_subtitle: "i found myself inside myself"
	quest.293AFFA188D96753.title: "Soul Searching"
	quest.29612C509F96B63D.title: "Elf Ears"
	quest.2973338AB622C5D6.quest_desc: ["Similar to &bCrates&r, many crops can be compacted into &bSacks&r. These can be used decoratively, or &aused to free up storage space&r!"]
	quest.2973338AB622C5D6.title: "Sack Up"
	quest.29A6066615C12448.quest_desc: ["Obtain a full set of &bDiamond Armor&r to keep those cute cheeks of yours safe and sound."]
	quest.29A6066615C12448.title: "The Full Set: Diamond Armor"
	quest.2A171EE16DA22152.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.2A171EE16DA22152.quest_subtitle: "compact deez"
	quest.2A171EE16DA22152.title: "Compact Your Nuts"
	quest.2A52CFAE2D88AC1D.quest_desc: [
		"You've finally reached the Highlands! This is going to sound suspicious, but hear me out: you need to find some &bMagic Beans&r."
		""
		"You can obtain some either by killing &eTrolls&r underground, or by looting their obsidian-bound Caches."
		""
		"Then, find a large patch of &bUberous Soil&r, above which the &eGiants&r live. You'll need to defeat their Miner to obtain his &bGiant Pickaxe&r."
		""
		"Then, you can &6return underground and use the Giant Pick&r to break open the large Obsidian Vault. It will take a while."
	]
	quest.2A52CFAE2D88AC1D.quest_subtitle: "You did it!"
	quest.2A52CFAE2D88AC1D.title: "Finally: The Highlands!"
	quest.2A61057B25357F37.quest_desc: ["If you can manage to slay 500 &eCreepers&r, then you shall have earned this &bCreeper Spawn Egg&r."]
	quest.2A930C9591A317A3.quest_desc: ["Although &eWraiths&r are not hostile, they sure are spooky. Put 50 of them &aout of their misery&r to earn this ingredient in crafting the &bUndead Eye&r."]
	quest.2A97D3E6C140611E.title: "Frog on Head"
	quest.2AABE6469023F950.quest_desc: [
		"Burning Sage is an ancient and well-documented method of purifying an area of negative or wayward energy. In this world, this &aprevents hostile mobs from spawning in a rather large radius around the bundle&r."
		""
		"To burn a &bSage Bundle&r, first hang it on a &bDrying Rack&r until the moisture is gone and the leaves are dessicated. Then, place the Bundle on the &bSage Burning Plate&r and light it with a &bFlint and Steel&r."
		""
		"The Bundle can be &aextinguished&r (&6shift right click with empty hand&r) during the daytime and it will &aretain its durability&r in order to be used again the next night."
		""
		"A side note: Sage burning is a multicultural practice which is not to be confused with Smudging. Smudging is a closed practice, sacred to First Nations people, and should probably not be attempted in Minecraft."
	]
	quest.2AABE6469023F950.quest_subtitle: "A sage choice"
	quest.2AABE6469023F950.title: "Obtain a Sage Bundle"
	quest.2ACCE2B7760206C9.quest_desc: ["Break down the &aLiveroots&r beneath a Tree in order to obtain them. This item can be combined with &bIron&r and &bGold&r in order to create &bIronwood&r, which can be used to create pre-enchanted pieces of gear."]
	quest.2ACCE2B7760206C9.quest_subtitle: "These roots...they're alive!"
	quest.2ACCE2B7760206C9.title: "Obtain Liveroot"
	quest.2AD594A3F740B338.quest_desc: [
		"Although similar in form, &bIdols&r are different from &bPoppets&r in the effects that they have. Rather than &aacting as a stand-in for an entity&r, they are instead a &afocus for a certain spell&r, such as rainfall, clear skies, or banishing curses."
		""
		"To make one, &awrap a &bMandrake&r in &bSilk Thread&r, and then &ainfuse it with the elements&r of your desired outcome."
		""
		"&bRainfall Idol&r - summons a gentle rain"
		"&bClarity Idol&r - clears the skies"
		"&bTempest Idol&r - summons a thunderstorm"
		"&bPurity Idol&r - upholds antiquated patriarchal notions of feminine - oh what? Not that kind of purity. Oh, that's right. Let me try again."
		""
		"&bPurity Idol&r - Removes &acurses&r from enchanted gear."
	]
	quest.2AD594A3F740B338.quest_subtitle: "idol hands are the devil's tools"
	quest.2AD594A3F740B338.title: "Obtain a Silk Idol"
	quest.2AD60B373912C5A4.quest_desc: ["The &bCage&r is similar to the &bCapture Cell&r, in that you can &6right click it on a small mob&r to pick it up and transport it. You can &6right click a block to release&r the mob, or you can &6shift right click&r to place the &bCage&r down and display your new friend in their enclosure!"]
	quest.2AD60B373912C5A4.quest_subtitle: "Despite all my rage, I am still just a...oh you know"
	quest.2B1B9108FF7A3FB3.quest_desc: [
		"Now, the focus of your &asacred space&r will eventually be your &bAltar&r, but let's not get ahead of ourselves. In order to make &bAltar blocks&r, you'll need to &6collect fumes&r - namely, the &bBreath of the Goddess&r and the &bExhale of the Horned One&r."
		""
		"&aFume collection&r is done in a &bWitch's Oven&r, which is crafted with &bIron&r (to deter the fey)."
		""
		"It works similarly to a &bFurnace&r, but is limited in what it can cook, and it has additional slots which can accommodate &bClay Jars&r to &atrap the fumes&r. Take these &bSaplings&r - you may wish to plant them and obtain more before you continue - and fire these &bClay Jars&r when you get the chance."
	]
	quest.2B1B9108FF7A3FB3.title: "Happy Witch: Sacred Space"
	quest.2B73F9B609ABE980.quest_desc: [
		"The &bUltimate Upgrade&r gives you all the previous benefits, while also transporting &aone stack at a time&r, making it the fastest option."
		"It is also significantly more expensive."
	]
	quest.2B8E1553C1487EBA.quest_desc: [
		"In the heart of the &cThorns&r lies a castle. Eerily empty and silent, the runes carved into its walls are meaningless to any still living."
		""
		"Atop the castle, however, is its lord - the &eCastle Keeper&r. He once reigned mercifully over the entire &cTwilight Forest&r, but his mind is rotted, and he now &asimply lays in wait&r, attacking all who dare draw near."
	]
	quest.2B8E1553C1487EBA.quest_subtitle: "your kobold is in another castle"
	quest.2B8E1553C1487EBA.title: "Gain Access to the Final Castle"
	quest.2BB8D1410BD7C040.quest_desc: [
		"In addition to your spyglass, you can also &aresearch using your &bCamera&r! Anything you snap a photo of will be unlocked in your &bField Guide&r, all at once!"
		""
		"It's...actually a bit overwhelming, to be honest. So be careful!"
	]
	quest.2BB8D1410BD7C040.title: "Bulk Research"
	quest.2BFD231209D227FC.quest_desc: [
		"&lAstikor Carts&r adds some delightful horse-drawn &bCarts&r, which are both useful and decorative. For this quest, let's focus on the latter."
		""
		"Place &bsome flowers&r above some &bdirt&r in the cart's inventory to attain this cute look! Note that you have to &6shift right click on the &bWheel&r in order to access the inventory."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/astikorflowers.png width:100 height:100 align:1 fit:true}"
	]
	quest.2BFD231209D227FC.title: "Decorative Carts"
	quest.2C24C18C174AD842.quest_desc: ["The &bNether Eye&r once belonged to a demon, who lost it in a mighty battle between the Aether and Nether. It can be found in chests inside - you guessed it - &dNether Fortresses&r."]
	quest.2C2D6CE0A2EC3305.quest_desc: ["These fish are located in the &cOverworld&r, in &anegative y levels&r."]
	quest.2C2D6CE0A2EC3305.title: "Catch Deep Fish"
	quest.2C5A66D41574D508.title: "Catch Common Fish"
	quest.2C760E07C84C91F2.quest_desc: [
		"Ravens love music! If you ever lose track of them, you can instantly summon them using the &bRaven Flute&r. You'll need &bMahogany Wood&r and some &bDye&r in order to craft."
		""
		"&6Right click while holding the Flute&r to play a tune to call your &eFamiliars&r."
		""
		"If you &6crouch and right click a Raven with the Flute&r, you can Select it with the &aSelect&r button. Then, you can select &aPerch&r, and &6crouch and right click a block/inventory item with the Flute&r in order to tell your Raven to perch there. Ravens will bring items back to their perch when told to &aGather&r."
	]
	quest.2C760E07C84C91F2.quest_subtitle: "Utterly Charming"
	quest.2C905E4DE5051CC5.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSnow Queen&r is found at the top of the &dAurora Palace&r, a treacherous mansion filled with icy monsters and slippery parkour."
		"The Queen herself has three phases, and cannot be damaged through her &aIce Throne&r, so only her upper body can be targeted."
		"When she is defeated, you have completed one of three tasks to gain access to &dThe Highlands&r."
	]
	quest.2C905E4DE5051CC5.quest_subtitle: "There's an Elsa joke in here somewhere"
	quest.2CA80140F624D0AE.quest_desc: [
		"Expand your farm with these delicious &bnew crops&r! Crops that &agrow in soil&r can have their &agrowth boosted&r by using &bRich Farmland&r."
		""
		"&bCorn&r can only be found naturally in &cAbandoned Farms&r, but you can also &6buy it from the &bMarket Stall&r!"
	]
	quest.2CA80140F624D0AE.quest_subtitle: "you're grounded"
	quest.2CA80140F624D0AE.title: "Obtain New Ground Crops"
	quest.2CAAC737A4D4FF60.quest_desc: [
		"Can't get enough &bBucketed Fish&r? You can &aobtain more&r by trading in &bthe fish you've caught&r."
		""
		"&dThis quest is repeatable&r."
	]
	quest.2CAAC737A4D4FF60.title: "Deliver Fish"
	quest.2D0CDD91CFAA0937.quest_desc: [
		"Summoning a &eSilk Moth&r, if you cannot find one in the wild, will require a &asmall ritual&r and a teensy bit of &ablood sacrifice&r. Oh, don't worry, the blood can come from any old thing, including the &eZombie&r you'll get as a reward for this quest!"
		""
		"To summon the &eSilk Moth&r, you'll need &bRitual Braziers&r set up around a &bRitual Table&r - you have one of those, right? Make sure to &asalt the &bBraziers&r, and &agrow 8 crops to maturity&r as power for the spell!"
		""
		"Then, place on the &bRitual Table&r a &bFragrant Nectar&r - this will be the central focus. Surrounding the Table, place on the Braziers the following:"
		""
		"- &bString&r"
		"- &bWhite Wool&r"
		"- &bSpirit Powder&r"
		"- &bCelestial Bloom&r"
		"- &bGlowstone Dust&r"
		"- &bWitchweed&r"
		""
		"{image:quest_enhance:textures/ftb/clipboard_1790374356249.png width:345 height:274 align:center fit:true}"
		""
		"Then &6click the &bRitual Table&r with your &bHex Focus&r, wait for the offerings to be accepted, and then &6slay a hostile creature within 8 blocks&r of the Ritual Table &6using an &bAthame&r."
		""
		"Be aware that &dthe summoned entity will be wild&r - be prepared with a &bLasso&r or other way to contain it!"
	]
	quest.2D0CDD91CFAA0937.title: "To Summon Silk"
	quest.2D137E6E0AD9F560.quest_desc: ["&eApple Cows&r are delightful creatures which grow &bApples&r upon their backs. You can &ashear them&r to obtain these tasty treats, but beware that &dthey do not regrow&r."]
	quest.2D8511D462DFF413.quest_desc: [
		"&eStonelings&r are very timid creatures! They can be found &cin caves underground&r, and will often be carrying &asomething shiny they found&r."
		""
		"Most times, they will &aimmediately flee&r the player and poof into their home dimension. However, if they are killed, they can drop the very valuable &bHeart of Diamond&r, used to make a &bPickarang&r."
		""
		"To obtain this, you'll need to &6sneak up on the &eStoneling&r."
	]
	quest.2D8511D462DFF413.title: "Meet the Stoneling"
	quest.2DB59F4A5BB3CE73.quest_desc: [
		"In addition to &apainting and photography&r, &asketching&r is a great way to capture the world around you! You will need a &bSketchbook&r and a &b Pencil&r to begin with, as well as an &bEraser&r to &aremove your mistakes&r."
		""
		"There are many other accessories for the &bSketchbook&r, so read on to learn more!"
		""
		"&dAll tools can be selected from the bottom of the Sketching interface, and can be put back with &6right click&r."
	]
	quest.2DB9642460401BB0.quest_desc: ["What has eyes but cannot see? A &bPotato&r! However, most of those eyes are simply roots seeking soil. The &bPotato Eye&r is something rather more magical... it can be found rarely when &aharvesting ripe &bPotatoes&r."]
	quest.2DC00391DC52D716.title: "Top Hat with a Frog"
	quest.2DCD3962DBC7E1F4.quest_desc: ["Starting a &aRaid&r might be the easiest way of obtaining the &bMagical Eye&r, which are used by &eEvokers&r for their powerful properties."]
	quest.2DDA757CE80078C3.quest_desc: [
		"Once you collect all the flowers, tick this box for &athe ultimate reward&r."
		""
		"Ya-ha-ha!"
		""
		"&dCan only be claimed once all previous quests are completed&r."
	]
	quest.2E07A04D5589B674.quest_desc: [
		"&bSharestones&r allow for travel &aonly within their colored network&r. From a Red Sharestone, you can teleport to any other Red Sharestone. However, you cannot do so from an Orange Sharestone."
		""
		"This makes them very useful for having private or separate networks of travel. They cannot be accessed from &bWarp Stones&r or any &bScrolls&r."
	]
	quest.2E07A04D5589B674.title: "Obtain a Sharestone"
	quest.2E1A6A93F48AAF58.quest_desc: [
		"The &bWarp Stone&r is an item which will allow you to &awarp to any Waystone from anywhere in the world&r. It is a multi-use item, which has a cooldown between uses."
		""
		"Simply &6hold right click with it in your hand&r in order to activate it. If you take damage or let go while it is charging, &dthe warp will cancel&r."
	]
	quest.2E1A6A93F48AAF58.title: "Obtain a Warp Stone"
	quest.2E3769733A0BFF69.quest_desc: [
		"All witches ought to have a &etrusty familiar&r - traditionally, these are spirits that take the form of cats!"
		""
		"Having a &efamiliar&r will not only make you resistant to curses, but will strengthen your curse magic. More importantly, though, it's nice to have a companion. To tame a familiar, you will first need a &eCat&r. Tame it with your &bfish&r of choice, and guide it into a &bRitual Circle&r."
		""
		"Read &bArt of Witchcraft&r; the chapter on &aSummoning Familiars&r will give you instructions on how to perform the rite."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/ritual_circle.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.2E3769733A0BFF69.quest_subtitle: "cats are also a witch's best friend"
	quest.2E3769733A0BFF69.title: "Happy Witch: Cats"
	quest.2E5DB4D84367E11B.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCoffer&r is a storage box which functions similarly to a &bShulker Box&r, as it &aretains its inventory&r once broken. It also &adisplays its contents&r when the player draws near, making it both useful and decorative!"
		""
		"The Coffer can be both dyed and renamed."
	]
	quest.2E5DB4D84367E11B.quest_subtitle: "Much better than a coffin"
	quest.2E5DB4D84367E11B.title: "Obtain a Coffer"
	quest.2EAC1A939E22DF84.quest_desc: ["For the low, low price of only 1 &bCog&r, you can add &ban additional Belt Slot&r to your &acurios screen&r!"]
	quest.2EAC1A939E22DF84.title: "New Belt Slot"
	quest.2EF910B028DA06B7.quest_desc: ["You can breed two tamed &eRavens&r by gifting one of them a shiny &bGolden Nugget&r. It will then bring it to its potential mate, and the two will pair up!"]
	quest.2EF910B028DA06B7.quest_subtitle: "Oooh, shiny!"
	quest.2EF910B028DA06B7.title: "Breeding Ravens"
	quest.2F0321A50945B2B5.quest_desc: [
		"The &bFilter Upgrade&r is meant to be used in conjunction with &bPipez&r or other item transport system."
		""
		"It will &ahelp control what items get placed&r in the storage you use it on."
	]
	quest.2F267ADA86FA5503.title: "Defeat the Alpha Yeti"
	quest.2F6C2F4DD36AE5E7.quest_desc: [
		"Collect a whole set of &bFur Armor&r to complete this quest."
		""
		"When a full set is equipped, the wearer is granted &a+2 Knockback Resist&r! However, it is mostly a cosmetic set."
	]
	quest.2F6C2F4DD36AE5E7.title: "The Full Set: Fur Armor"
	quest.2F933DC876021A85.quest_desc: [
		"Once you meet your first &eRaven&r, you're ready to tame. Bring lots of &bSeed Mixture&r because they can be hard to win over!"
		""
		"Once you have tamed the Raven Familiar, you can &6crouch and right click it&r to &aaccess its menu&r."
		"If you &6right click without crouching&r, you will &achange its mode&r to Sit, Follow, and more. You can do that in the menu, as well. By default, it will Follow and sit on your shoulder, unless you crouch."
		""
		"&aRavens can be equipped with hats and weapons&r via the menu. It can wear most helmets and wield most melee weapons. "
		""
		"{image:hexerei:textures/book/pictures/crow_gui.png width:100 height:100 align:1}"
		""
		"Through the menu, you can instruct your &eFamiliar&r to help you farm your crops, or to follow you in combat, or even to &apickpocket villagers&r."
	]
	quest.2F933DC876021A85.quest_subtitle: "You look oddly Familiar"
	quest.2F933DC876021A85.title: "Meet a Raven"
	quest.2FC0EAD96E3C41D4.quest_desc: [
		"&eTadpoles&r, otherwise known as \"the forbidden boba,\" are cute lil wiggly fellas who are particularly susceptible to &eAxolotls&r."
		""
		"They're also susceptible to &bBuckets&r, and if you should capture one in such a way, then you've completed this quest."
	]
	quest.303CFA0591015A89.title: "Antlers"
	quest.3052EF7FA42720A9.quest_desc: [
		"The &bIron Rod&r is not just a decoration, it is also functional. When it is placed on a &bSticky Piston&r, it will &abreak the block&r the Piston pushes it into."
		""
		"This only works on blocks which can be pushed, so blocks like &bObsidian&r will not be affected."
	]
	quest.3052EF7FA42720A9.quest_subtitle: "that's my grindr screenname"
	quest.3057155A3A2B5F47.quest_desc: ["This quest is repeatable."]
	quest.306EAF9F6F78ACC1.quest_desc: ["Obtain a &bfull set of Diamond Tools&r to earn an &darmor trim of your choice&r!"]
	quest.306EAF9F6F78ACC1.title: "The Full Set: Diamond Tools"
	quest.30C8AAFCE9EB2BA6.quest_desc: [
		"Love that \"hunting lodge\" look? Want to show off your best hunts? Want to let everyone know you really, really hate &eGoats&r?"
		""
		"Well, why not &adecorate your house with these attractive trophies&r."
		""
		"(only some animals were hurt in the making of this quest)"
	]
	quest.30C8AAFCE9EB2BA6.quest_subtitle: "get them cheevos"
	quest.30C8AAFCE9EB2BA6.title: "Trophy Unlocked"
	quest.30CF344B2B4C22E8.quest_desc: ["Every witch needs a good &bhat&r. You can craft yours out of &bInfused Fabric&r, or find it in a &dWitch Coven&r in a Swamp biome."]
	quest.30CF344B2B4C22E8.quest_subtitle: "The icon, the myth, the legend"
	quest.30EA6BEFEEBF9650.quest_desc: [
		"The &bApothecary Cauldron&r is a vessel in which &bPotion Essences&r can be turned into, well, &bPotions&r. In order to use it, you'll also need the &bApothecary's Mortar&r. Now, it's &dvery important not to mix potion essences in a regular &bMortar&r! Some of the effects can be grave. Literally."
		""
		"Once you have your &bApothecary Set&r, you'll need &breagents&r! Crafting &bPotion Essences&r involves finding &atwo or more ingredients&r that &ashare the same effects&r. For example, combining &bMugwort&r and &bBelladonna&r can create &aNight Vision&r. However, some ingredients will carry more than one effect, and if you &amatch two negative effects&r, it can taint your potion. &dNote that the dried version of an item is generally safer&r."
		""
		"\"But how can I know what effects an item has?\" I hear you ask. Well. I recommend that you &aengage in a little bit of experimentation&r, to see what sorts of things you can &aconvert to &bPotion Essences&r. However, here's a cheat sheet to get you started:"
		""
		"- &bBelladonna&r flowers can create &aNight Vision&r, but also &aPoison&r."
		"- &bMugwort Flowers&r grant &aNight Vision&r, &aSlow Falling&r, and &aSpeed&r."
		"- Certain parts of &bMandrake&r will cause &aRegeneration&r, but also &aNausea&r."
		"- &bSage&r grants &aRegeneration&r and &aGrowth&r."
	]
	quest.30EA6BEFEEBF9650.quest_subtitle: "its brewin time"
	quest.30EA6BEFEEBF9650.title: "Buy an Apothecary Cauldron \\& Mortar"
	quest.318C7124088632D3.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBobbers&r from &lStarcatcher&r have many different effects. The &bBasic Bobber&r is the exception - it's just here for the food."
		""
		"- &bSteady Bobber&r: Sweet spots are larger and easier to hit"
		"- &bGolden Bobber&r: Golden fish are 5% more likely to bite"
		"- &bCloud Bobber&r: Your bobber no longer obeys gravity"
		"- &bClear Bobber&r: vanishing sweet spots stick around longer"
		"- &bVanilla-Flavored Bobber&r: Allows you to catch vanilla fish. &dPair this with the &bVanilla Hook&r to &dskip the minigame&r"
		"- &bSlimey Bobber&r: Prevents the fish from swimming away once by bouncing it back up. Also, a great insult - \"You slimey bobber, you!\""
		"- &bDripstone Bobber&r: Adds a dripstone sweet spot"
		"- &bGlowing Bobber&r: Adds a glowing sweet spot"
		"- &bLeafy Bobber&r: Adds leafy sweet spots"
	]
	quest.318C7124088632D3.quest_subtitle: "bobbing for... fish?"
	quest.318C7124088632D3.title: "Different Bobbers"
	quest.31CE923007EF1D03.quest_desc: [
		"There are a bunch of different types of &bMilk&r, which can all be made into &aunique and tasty cheeses&r."
		""
		"Although most of them come from &adifferent types of &eAnimals&r, you can also craft &bGrain Milk&r (vegan-friendly!) and &bAmethyst Milk&r. These last two types of milk are crafted using the &bRustic Cauldron&r. Grain milk is made with 2 Grains and one Wooden Water Bucket. Amethyst milk is made with Amethyst and, well, milk..."
		""
		"&eWater Buffalo&r can be found in &cRiver&r biomes."
		""
		"&eWarped Cows&r can be found in &cWarped Forest&r biomes."
	]
	quest.31CE923007EF1D03.title: "Many Milk Types!"
	quest.31D3A29B73BE3ABA.title: "Catch Nether Fish"
	quest.327660E1DFE7C9A0.quest_desc: ["The &bBasic Pipe Upgrade&r allows you to set a &aRedstone Mode&r for the Pipe. You can set it to &aonly be active&r when receiving a signal, or to &astop when it receives a signal&r. By default, it will &aignore Redstone input&r."]
	quest.3278B2F717A8F374.quest_desc: ["The &bBlack Eye&r, which once gave sight to the mighty Black Pearl, is now hidden beneath the surface in some &dBuried Treasure&r."]
	quest.327D93798A7BE211.quest_desc: [
		"A cauldron is fine and dandy, but you'll want something a little more magical for your endeavors. "
		""
		"The &bMixing Cauldron&r is used to craft many useful items, and accepts &bWater&r, &bLava&r, and &bBlood&r as a base in which to work. More on that later."
		""
		"For now, why not &6pop over to the shop&r and pick yourself up a nice little &bMixing Cauldron&r? You can also &acraft one&r, of course, if you're feeling clever."
		""
		""
		"{\"text\":\"The Mixing Cauldron\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"64E8A8E1C9A939C9/1\"},\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"aqua\"}"
	]
	quest.327D93798A7BE211.quest_subtitle: "A Cauldron that's just cauld-right!"
	quest.327D93798A7BE211.title: "Obtain a Mixing Cauldron"
	quest.329CC0CC1B48C600.quest_desc: [
		"The &bFilter Destination Tool&r is a multi-use tool which will allow you to &aset the destination&r of a &bfiltered item type&r."
		""
		"You can assign it an inventory by &6right clicking it &lon the face of the block the &bPipe&6 connects to&r. It will not work if you do not select the correct face of the inventory."
	]
	quest.32DCF4F0C230C940.quest_desc: [
		"But beds aren't the only things that can &abenefit from &bSheets&r and &bCushions&r!"
		""
		"For example, &6right click a &bSheet&r on a &bTable&r to give it a &atablecloth&r."
		""
		"And you can &aapply a &bCushion&r to a &bChair&r as well! Why not see what other items you can customize..."
	]
	quest.32DCF4F0C230C940.title: "Versatile Decorations"
	quest.3345FC1A378395B0.quest_desc: ["This quest is repeatable."]
	quest.338640D0D42E7EC4.quest_desc: ["The &bSimmer Pot&r allows you to create delectable &bJams&r and &bChocolate Spreads&r and such."]
	quest.33B84E3E74BE73B7.quest_desc: [
		"Many of the magical recipes you'll learn involve &aGrove Crafting&r, so let's get the basics of that squared away. Using your &bRunestone&r, you'll want to make both a &bGrove Stone&r and a &bGrove Crafter&r."
		""
		"The &bWild Grove Stone&r is the simplest to make, requiring only &bRunestone&r to make. Going forward, you'll want to &ainfuse &bGrove Stones&a with different types of magic&r to assist you in various ways. More on that later - for now, take these &bGrove Pedestals&r, which you'll want to use to &acraft &bWildwood Pedestals&r."
		""
		"Simply &6place the &bGrove Stone&r, &bGrove Crafter&r, and &bPedestals&r in &aclose proximity to one another&r, and then &6top the &bPedestals&r &6with your ingredients&r."
	]
	quest.33B84E3E74BE73B7.title: "Crafting Mystically"
	quest.33CFB64E32F26FC0.quest_desc: [
		"Collect a whole set of &bSlime Armor&r to complete this quest."
		""
		"The &bSlime Boots&r prevent fall damage by &amaking you bouncy&r! If you wear the &bChestplate&r and &bLeggings&r at the same time, you can &aclimb walls&r. And the &bHelmet&r allows you to &ahang from the ceiling&r."
		""
		"The more pieces of this set you wear, the &amore powerful the &bSlime Sling&r becomes."
	]
	quest.33CFB64E32F26FC0.quest_subtitle: "so slimy"
	quest.33CFB64E32F26FC0.title: "The Full Set: Slime Armor"
	quest.33F3FB13A3EAEF94.quest_desc: ["The &eSnuffle&r is a passive creature with a permanent blep. It can be found in snowy biomes, and &atamed with potatoes&r."]
	quest.33F3FB13A3EAEF94.quest_subtitle: "So warm and snuffly"
	quest.33F3FB13A3EAEF94.title: "Meet a Snuffle!"
	quest.34581095B797C667.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know that &aall true teas are the same plant&r? They're simply oxidized at different levels. Tisanes are a different story, of course, but I'll spare you the details."
		""
		"After your tea has been &aharvested&r, it needs to be &6dried out&r - this enhances the flavor and reduces the chance of spoilage (okay, it doesn't spoil in Minecraft. Don't get sassy with me)."
		""
		"You can dry your tea leaves one of two ways: with a &bSmoker&r (faster, costs fuel) or a &bDrying Rack&r (slower, but costs only time)."
	]
	quest.34581095B797C667.title: "Drying Tea"
	quest.34670D78DC22EC27.quest_desc: ["The &bSage Burning Plate&r will allow you to burn &bSage Bundles&r, which &aprevents hostile mobs from spawning&r within a large radius."]
	quest.34670D78DC22EC27.title: "Obtain a Sage Burning Plate"
	quest.346AD14E27A84B57.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you've got your charm, you just need a fashionable &bbelt&r to attach it to."
		""
		"Craft a &bbelt&r using five charm fragments of any flavour, and three leather. &6By right-clicking with the belt in your hand,&r you can equip as many charms as you'd like!"
	]
	quest.346AD14E27A84B57.quest_subtitle: "now you don't"
	quest.346AD14E27A84B57.title: "Craft a Mob Charm"
	quest.34D4613E61AF3AEF.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Pufferfish"
	quest.3556685D896ADA7C.quest_desc: [
		"&eGoats&r are ornery things. If you should happen across one, &abeware of their headbutts&r! "
		"However, if you can get it to &acharge into a hard block&r such as &bStone&r, it will drop a &bHorn&r."
	]
	quest.3556685D896ADA7C.title: "Meet the Goat"
	quest.3571AAEB58389A64.quest_desc: [
		"Basic chests and barrels are fine for a while, but the canny witch knows that &athe rules of space and time&r are meant to be bent a little. With a little magic, you can easily make your storage bigger - &aand smarter&r!"
		""
		"Let's begin with a simple &bBarrel&r. Place it in the world as usual, and then &6right click it with the &bBasic Tier Upgrade&r."
		""
		"Now, once you enter the inventory, you'll see some new additions."
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/sophstorage.png width:200 height:160 align:center}"
		""
		"The slot to the left &aaccepts upgrades&r which allow your storage to perform certain functions."
		""
		"The &acog wheel&r on the right gives you access to your &astorage settings&r."
	]
	quest.3571AAEB58389A64.quest_subtitle: "Let's get sophisticated"
	quest.3571AAEB58389A64.title: "Upgrading Your Storage"
	quest.358EB6DB33F203FE.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Powder Snow Bucket"
	quest.3657239C35390F17.quest_desc: [
		"The &eHydra&r is a fearsome foe that is only weak in one place: within its fire-spewing maw!"
		"It is best to take on this fight with &a Fire Resistance&r, and make sure you &aim attacks at the Hydra's open mouths&r! You can use a &branged weapon&r, or use a sword to &adeflect their bombs&r back at them."
		"Once you have defeated the beast, you have completed one task which will let you challenge the Highlands."
	]
	quest.3657239C35390F17.quest_subtitle: "Remove one head, and two appear!"
	quest.369DEAD83BD150DA.quest_desc: ["The best witches are those who are worldly. As such, &6prove your mettle by traversing all vanilla biomes&r!"]
	quest.369DEAD83BD150DA.quest_subtitle: "witches abroad"
	quest.369DEAD83BD150DA.title: "Visit all Vanilla Biomes"
	quest.36AC202292F23D2D.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Shroomlight"
	quest.3705ABBD8EE1A369.quest_desc: ["The first time you trade with a villager, their &aprofession and possible trades will become locked&r. This is a good way to ensure that the &aLibrarian&r doesn't suddenly run away to join the circus."]
	quest.3705ABBD8EE1A369.title: "Trade with a Villager"
	quest.374F93068ED863F7.quest_desc: [
		"Pottery &bSherds&r are relics of times long past, and also a handy crafting ingredient!"
		""
		"You can &aduplicate them&r by &6surrounding them with &bBricks&r."
		""
		"You can &agild &7(some of)&r&a them&r by &6crafting them with &bGold Nuggets&r. Gilded sherds can &aalso be duplicated&r."
		""
		"Finally, you can reconstruct them into &bPots&r by &6combining any 4 &bSherds or Bricks&r like so:"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/potterysherd.png width:205 height:200 align:1}"
	]
	quest.374F93068ED863F7.title: "Obtain A Sherd"
	quest.376F0C3219E696C9.quest_desc: ["This quest is repeatable."]
	quest.379BBBB45274DA68.title: "Tarot Cards 4"
	quest.37EB25189E81986C.quest_desc: [
		"The &bPyre&r is a place where you can &acraft and consecrate special items&r such as &bReagents&r for your spells. To use one, &6right click the crafting components onto the &bPyre&r, and then &6light it with &bFlint and Steel&r. Then, &await a few seconds for the fire to go out&r."
		""
		"&dIt is very important that you wait patiently, as right clicking the &bPyre&d while it's working will delete your spell&r! When the spell is completed, the item will pop into existence for you to pick up."
	]
	quest.37EB25189E81986C.title: "Pyres and Creation"
	quest.37FCA731EEAB2C0D.quest_desc: [
		"The ingredient &bTongue of Dog&r sounds like a rather unpleasant task to obtain, but it is in fact, just a name - it refers to the &abright red stamen&r of the &bWolfsbane Flower&r."
		""
		"You can harvest this by &6cutting the flower on a &bCutting Board&6 with an &bArthana&r."
	]
	quest.37FCA731EEAB2C0D.title: "Tongue of Dog"
	quest.3801F3578406768D.quest_desc: ["Although it doesn't provide &amuch protection&r, this hat will have you &aslingin' dishes&r and &aslicin' fishes&r like a pro!"]
	quest.3801F3578406768D.quest_subtitle: "what's cookin', good lookin'?"
	quest.3801F3578406768D.title: "Looking like a Cook"
	quest.38692155327FDE4B.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCircle Talisman&r is an item which allows you to &astore your magic circles&r for later use. To use one, you'll need to &6place one &bRedstone&r and the &bTalisman&r inside your circle and &6perform the &bRite of Binding&r."
		""
		"This will store your circle inside the &bTalisman&r."
	]
	quest.38692155327FDE4B.title: "Storing your Circles"
	quest.393CF105AAFA6CF0.quest_desc: [
		"Don't you get tired of having to &aopen your backpack to get things&r? Isn't it annoying to have to &aput food in your mouth&r every time you're hungry? Who has time to &aswitch between their axe and pickaxe&r when harvesting materials?"
		""
		"Get yourself a backpack that does it all with these upgrades. No more wasted time &agrabbing the next stack of blocks&r or even &aopening your backpack to refill it.&r You're busy and have more important matters to attend to."
		""
		"To get the most of these upgrades, we suggest &6checking out the settings tab&r for each one. "
		""
		"Your settings will be saved for each upgrade &aeven if you remove it.&r"
	]
	quest.393CF105AAFA6CF0.quest_subtitle: "\"i don't like to do anything\" - Docm77"
	quest.393CF105AAFA6CF0.title: "Shortcut Upgrades"
	quest.393FED910B541631.quest_desc: ["Forged in the time before history began by ancient Blacksmiths, the &bLost Eye&r is said to be found in &dMineshafts&r, deep beneath the crust of the earth."]
	quest.394A179160EB4AE8.quest_desc: ["What a majestic set of armor, often worn by bee warriors. While not very powerful, it is a very nice looking set."]
	quest.394A179160EB4AE8.quest_subtitle: "the bee's knees, and arms, and chest..."
	quest.394A179160EB4AE8.title: "The Bee Armor"
	quest.396C5F4A97427E6C.quest_desc: [
		"You can &6fill your watering can with water&r at &aa nearby water source&r (it does not consume the source block). To &afill it with fertilizer&r, &6hold the &bFertilizer&6 in your off-hand&r and the &bWatering Can&r in your main hand, and &6right click&r."
		""
		"Then, when you water your crops, it will not only &ahydrate the soil&r, but &aprovide a growth boost&r! You can also use it &aon grass&r to spawn tall grass and flowers."
	]
	quest.396C5F4A97427E6C.title: "Fill Your Watering Can"
	quest.39844F8340E6A438.quest_desc: [
		"&bFramed Blocks&r are a unique item similar to &lCreate's&r &bCopycat Blocks&r. They are frameworks which can &adisplay the texture of another block&r. To do this, &6place the &bFramed Block&r and then &6right click it with another block&r."
		""
		"Framed blocks come in &a multitude of different shapes&r, many of which are not available in vanilla, such as &aslopes and corners&r. You can use this mod to elevate your builds to a new level!"
	]
	quest.39844F8340E6A438.title: "Framed Blocks"
	quest.399D55B3452588FF.quest_desc: [
		"&dThe Twilight Forest&r is a night-ridden dimension filled with mysteries and odd creatures both friendly and hostile. Freely traveling the dimension is difficult - you must conquer each challenge in turn in order to traverse."
		""
		"To &amake the portal&r, you must &6dig a 3x3x1 (or 2x2x1) hole and fill it with water&r. Then, &6surround the pond with flowers or mushrooms&r. Finally, &6throw a Diamond into the pool&r. Beware, opening a portal can be dangerous!"
	]
	quest.399D55B3452588FF.quest_subtitle: "Throw it in a limpid pool and then back away"
	quest.399D55B3452588FF.title: "Obtain a Portal Key"
	quest.39AD0DDC4695E2D4.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBank Terminal&r is a block which allows you to keep a &abank account&r. Once placed, it will automatically be &abound to the user&r. Money placed in the &bTerminal&r becomes &aquantum in nature&r - if you have 1 &bSun&r, you can withdraw that, or you can withdraw &b4,096 Spurs&r, or anything in between!"
		""
		""
		"When using a linked &bCard&r at a shop, it will &awithdraw and deposit currency&r automatically."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/numibanker.png width:100 height:80 align:1 fit:true}"
	]
	quest.39C476A7C4682009.quest_desc: [
		"You can craft a &bPedestal&r to display an item!"
		""
		"After placing the Pedestal down, &6right click on it&r to store an item, and &6right click with empty hand&r to remove the item."
	]
	quest.39C476A7C4682009.quest_subtitle: "I got a bad case of display-sia"
	quest.39C476A7C4682009.title: "Obtain a Pedestal"
	quest.3A0205CA0568641F.title: "Defeat the Naga"
	quest.3A51A2B4DE09D7D7.quest_desc: [
		"Using &aFey Magic&r, you can ensnare villagers to do your bidding~"
		""
		"By &6shift right clicking on them&r, you bewitch them into item form, which allows you to carry them around until you have need of them. While in item form, you can &aplace them into a &bTrader&r, which transforms them into a &ehomunculus&r who will then trade with you."
		""
		"Should you decide to &arelease them&r, you can &6shift right click&r on the &bTrader&r to remove the &eVillager&r, then &6right click the villager&r onto the ground."
		""
		"&bTraders&r, and other blocks from the &lEasy Villagers&r mod, will retain their inventory when broken."
	]
	quest.3A51A2B4DE09D7D7.title: "Easy Villager Trading"
	quest.3A61711F03B28A75.quest_desc: [
		"The &bWooden Chute&r is a block which draws items from above it and &adrops them&r perfectly in the center of the block below it."
		""
		"It can be disabled with a Redstone signal, or by placing a block directly below it."
	]
	quest.3A61711F03B28A75.title: "Wooden Chute"
	quest.3A642C7C4A5C4334.quest_desc: ["Sometimes when &aStarcatching&r, you might fish up &asecret messages&r. Written who knows when, by who knows who, these letters may provide you insight or wisdom. Or not. It really depends."]
	quest.3A642C7C4A5C4334.quest_subtitle: "sending out an sos"
	quest.3A642C7C4A5C4334.title: "Find a Secret Message"
	quest.3A6AAE50897DE597.quest_desc: ["&bDog food&r, and its companion, &bHorse Food&r, will grant potion effects to their users such as &aspeed&r, &aresistance&r, or &ajump boost&r."]
	quest.3A6AAE50897DE597.quest_subtitle: "Hmmm... Maybe YOU should try eating it... Go on..."
	quest.3A6AAE50897DE597.title: "Feeding Your Pets"
	quest.3AADAC34ECDEF891.quest_desc: ["This eye is said to be favored by Chosen Undead. The &bUndead Eye&r can be crafted using an &bUndead Soul&r, acquired from killing a &eSkeleton Horse&r, or a large number of &eWraiths&r."]
	quest.3AE0F1C1159FBDDE.quest_desc: ["&bStraw&r can be used to make &bRope&r, which is very useful. It can also be used to make &bCanvas&r, &bCompost&r, and building materials such as &bDaub&r."]
	quest.3AE0F1C1159FBDDE.quest_subtitle: "Just don't draw the short one"
	quest.3AE0F1C1159FBDDE.title: "Obtain Straw"
	quest.3B1C91A3CD3EC221.quest_desc: ["Obtain a full set of &bIron Armor&r. Hey, it's better than Leather!"]
	quest.3B1C91A3CD3EC221.title: "The Full Set: Iron Armor"
	quest.3B33F8C27B3361AC.quest_desc: [
		"The &eForest Raven&r is a creature that can often be found near &aObsidian Obelisks&r in the Twilight Forest."
		""
		""
		"While normally you must &6slay one&r to obtain its &bFeathers&r, this quest grants you one so that you can make your &aMagic Map Focus&r without bloodshed."
	]
	quest.3B33F8C27B3361AC.title: "Find a Forest Raven"
	quest.3B84722A9CD28821.quest_desc: [
		"Those who experiment with altering their states may find themselves in quite the situation, not entirely knowing how they arrived at this conclusion."
		""
		"This achievement involves getting &aevery vanilla effect&r at once, as well as the modded effects."
	]
	quest.3C87581273ACB6A0.quest_desc: ["Find two animals and breed them in order to get this advancement and begin these quests!"]
	quest.3C87581273ACB6A0.quest_subtitle: "Animal husbandry is different than the name sounds"
	quest.3CEDCDDE9BCD7F5F.quest_desc: [
		"&dCongratulations&r on collecting every item in the hunt! Please enjoy your fabulous prizes (and the sense of personal satisfaction, which is the real treasure)."
		""
		"The check mark above unlocks &6once all Scavenger Hunt Quests are done&r."
	]
	quest.3CEDCDDE9BCD7F5F.quest_subtitle: "It's finally done"
	quest.3D221ECD9106F792.quest_desc: ["The &bPlanter&r is useful both as a decorative block, and as a utility. It can grow crops without the need for water, and without the danger of being trampled. It also just looks cute!"]
	quest.3D221ECD9106F792.quest_subtitle: "Mmm, so planty"
	quest.3D7070B95990779A.quest_desc: [
		"This backpack is no kid's toy - this thing is multipurpose and heavy duty! With access to a &aplethora of unique upgrades to equip&r and the ability to improve the backpack's storage by &6crafting it with increasingly expensive ingots&r, this is truly an endgame storage solution for on-the-go witches."
		""
		"You can place this backpack down/pick it up by &6shift right clicking&r it. You can &aopen it with &6b&r and &aequip it in your &bBack curio slot&r to free up inventory space."
		""
		"Caution: although you can block other players from opening your backpack while you wear it (&6check the mod's config&r!), &dthere is no way to protect against this backpack being stolen if you set it down or put it in a chest.&r"
	]
	quest.3D7070B95990779A.quest_subtitle: "its ~sophisticated~"
	quest.3D7070B95990779A.title: "Backpack For The Discerning Gentlewitch"
	quest.3D99932B0EAFD2DA.quest_desc: [
		"&bCherry Trees&r can be found in most &cForests&r. To obtain them, you must &6right click the cherried leaves&r. They do not drop if the tree is broken."
		""
		"&bStrawberries&r can be found growing in both &ccold biomes such as Taiga&r, and also in &cJungle Biomes&r!"
	]
	quest.3D99932B0EAFD2DA.title: "Collect Crops: Misc"
	quest.3DFE6CC659B005C6.quest_desc: ["The &bBloom Basket&r is a decorative block which you can &afill with certain flowers&r, such as &bPansies&r, or &bTwinflowers&r!"]
	quest.3E3157BF119F4F59.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCompacting Drawer&r is super useful, as it &ataps into the fabric of reality itself&r to offer you &aa single item in multiple forms&r."
		""
		"Let me explain. Placing in 9 &bIron Ingots&r will result in the block containing - simultaneously and mutually exclusively - either 1 &bIron Block&r, 9 &bIron Ingots&r, or 81 &bIron Nuggets&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/compactingdrawer.png width:200 height:200 align:1}"
		""
		"If you withdraw 1 &bNugget&r, you will then have 0 &bBlocks&r, 8 &bIngots&r, and/or 80 &bNuggets&r. It simply &dsaves you the step of up or down crafting items&r."
		""
		"The &bSimple Compacting Drawer&r is similar, but works with &atwo recipes&r instead of three."
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/simplecompacting.png width:200 height:200 align:1}"
	]
	quest.3E3157BF119F4F59.quest_subtitle: "also works with vegetables!"
	quest.3E3157BF119F4F59.title: "Compact Your Iron"
	quest.3E4527C883908239.quest_desc: ["&eMilo&r is a cat - a very special one. He wanders near and far bringing &agood deals&r to all, and all he asks in return is a few &bEmeralds&r. What does he want with them? No one knows. Rumor has it that he runs a secret charity to buy &afish for homeless kittens&r."]
	quest.3E509A27A92746F4.quest_desc: ["The Globe is a decorative item which is unique per world. When interacted with, or provided with Redstone signal, it will spin."]
	quest.3E509A27A92746F4.quest_subtitle: "Time to get a globe-up (that was bad, i'm sorry)"
	quest.3E509A27A92746F4.title: "Obtain a Globe"
	quest.3E8BB82A228A4727.quest_desc: ["Let's not leave our mycelial friends out of the crate action!"]
	quest.3E8BB82A228A4727.quest_subtitle: "shroom edition"
	quest.3E8BB82A228A4727.title: "Compact Your Crops: Mushrooms"
	quest.3EBAD94D079ACDD8.quest_desc: ["Defeat a horde of &eEndermen&r, take their SKIN and WEAR IT - oh, was that too much? Sorry. I got excited."]
	quest.3EDAAAB87F7C1022.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Fungi"
	quest.3EF4DABC6B496E19.quest_desc: ["This unusual fruit is not strictly edible in the usual sense. But you could &afeed it to a villager&r if you didn't like them very much... Or a &eCreeper&r, if you didn't like &oyourself&r very much."]
	quest.3F47F402ECEF06A3.title: "Tarot Cards 1"
	quest.3F5F93D7191952F9.quest_desc: ["For this quest, show your love of color by collecting each different type of wool."]
	quest.3F5F93D7191952F9.quest_subtitle: "Taste the rainbow"
	quest.3F5F93D7191952F9.title: "Obtain the Rainbow"
	quest.3FAE926346F1E576.quest_desc: ["50 deaths, and you're just getting started! Congrats...I guess? Anyway, here &6take this Totem&r, it seems like you need it."]
	quest.3FAE926346F1E576.quest_subtitle: "YOU DIED"
	quest.3FAE926346F1E576.title: "Die 50 Times"
	quest.4014D768E23552B0.quest_desc: [
		"The Moon Dust Brush makes your broom go &asignificantly faster&r, especially during a &dFull Moon&r."
		""
		"In all other regards, it is the &asame as the &bEnhanced Broom Brush&r."
	]
	quest.401B7E57628C88F5.title: "Catch Overworld Fish"
	quest.401E8078C11F8919.quest_desc: ["Breed 2 of each vanilla animal in order to obtain this reward!"]
	quest.40640000C8D2BDCD.quest_desc: [
		"Use your &bSpyglass&r to research 5 &bPlants&r! Did you know that you can &amake notes&r in your &bField Guide&r? You can add entries stating where you found the item, whether you need shears to harvest it, or just write a little poem about it."
		""
		"Here's mine:"
		""
		"&oRoses are red,"
		"&oWither Roses are black."
		"&oOnce you're a witch,"
		"&oYou never go back.&r"
	]
	quest.407BBCE05BCE9039.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations! You've found an &aancient being's egg&r. It may be an unusual familiar for a witch, but &awho knows what help it could provide you&r!"
		""
		"In the interest of science, which as we all know is just magic with the fun taken away, why not &6place this egg on some &bMoss&r and see if it &ahatches&r?"
	]
	quest.40BBDD8D814A55C1.quest_desc: ["Collect one each of every flower in the game to earn rewards!"]
	quest.40BBDD8D814A55C1.title: "Flower Picking: Yellow"
	quest.40C1DBE20E401EF9.quest_desc: ["You can also use &bHoglin Hides&r to create Soul &bCompost&r, which will slowly convert into &bRich Soul Soil&r. Simply &6place the Compost near Lava&r."]
	quest.40C1DBE20E401EF9.quest_subtitle: "Soul Compost? Boy that's a mood"
	quest.410FE13D777DE1C8.quest_desc: [
		"Now you can create your own consecrated space - your &bAltar&r. It can be placed either indoors or outdoors, although placing it outside is often a good choice due to the &apower of Nature&r being good to draw upon."
		""
		"Place &b6 Altar Blocks&r in a 2x3 configuration, and they will combine and change appearance. This is where many of your workings will take place, as it will take on and focus the energy you raise. You can &6augment this space in multiple ways&r: by placing &bFoci&r on top of the Altar, and &bobjects of power&r within a 16-block radius of it. More on this in the next quest."
		""
		"You can &aview the power of your altar by &6right clicking it&r with an empty hand."
	]
	quest.410FE13D777DE1C8.title: "Building an Altar"
	quest.4110A15F659422D5.quest_desc: ["The &bTrowel&r will place a random block from your hotbar when you &6right click with it&r. Perfect for easily &arandomizing your build's palette&r."]
	quest.4110A15F659422D5.quest_subtitle: "place blocks randomly"
	quest.4110A15F659422D5.title: "Obtain a Trowel"
	quest.414A7F60BF8F090A.quest_desc: [
		"Do you struggle to draw a &aperfect circle&r? Or do you want to &adraw a straight line&r? Then these tools are for you."
		""
		"The &bDrawing Compass&r allows you to draw a circle easily by &6anchoring the point with left click&r, adjusting the radius of your circle, and then &6holding left click and spinning your cursor&r. If you experience issues with this, don't forget to &dmake sure your pencil or marker is selected&r!"
		""
		"The &bRuler&r does what it says on the tin - it...uh...rules? No, sorry, I guess it doesn't. It does help you draw a straight line, though!"
	]
	quest.414A7F60BF8F090A.title: "Drawing Assistance"
	quest.4183514EA291214A.quest_desc: [
		"&bMandrake Root&r is obtainable, surprisingly enough, from &bMandrake Plants&r! However, one must be careful when harvesting Mandrake, as they can &aget a little rowdy if agitated&r."
		""
		"To harvest just the root, &6right click&r to gather gently. However, if one were to &6left click to harvest&r, it would &aawaken the &eMandrake&r, who will &ashriek horribly&r and attempt to flee."
		""
		"However, there are &dcertain drops only available from killing the &eMandrake&r."
		""
		"To avoid its harrowing scream, &bEarmuffs&r are recommended."
	]
	quest.41A361B4DEFCEFA6.quest_desc: [
		"&bIncense&r is often used as part of spellcraft, and it also smells nice! This type of incense, however, primarily exists to &asummon waves of mobs&r at an &bAncient Brazier&r, found in &cSwamp Dungeons&r."
		""
		"&bBasic Incense&r can be found by lighting &dnaturally spawning&r &bAncient Braziers&r and fighting the mobs that spawn."
		""
		"You can craft &bBasic Incense&r into four different special incenses, each with a different effect:"
		""
		"- &bBoiling Incense&r: summons &eBlazes, Magma Cubes, Husks, and Wither Skeletons&r"
		"- &bBrine Incense&r: summons &eBreeze, Drowned, Phantoms, and Witches&r"
		"- &bRot Incense&r: summons &eFilth, Bogged, Strays, and Slimes&r"
		"- &bWebbed Incense&r: summons &eInfected Spiders, Spiders, Cave Spiders, and Silverfish&r"
		""
		"After each wave of summoning is completed, the &bBrazier&r will reward your effort with &athematic loot&r."
	]
	quest.41A361B4DEFCEFA6.quest_subtitle: "don't be so incensitive"
	quest.41A361B4DEFCEFA6.title: "Incenses"
	quest.41CBB146259DAF34.quest_desc: [
		"The Yeti Cave can be found in the Snowy Forest, and houses both &eYetis&r (which are neutral), and the &eAlpha Yeti&r, who is the boss you must face in this area."
		""
		"Engaging this foe in melee combat can be dangerous, but even at range one must &abeware of falling icicles&r!"
		""
		"His death will grant you access to &dthe Glacier&r."
	]
	quest.41CBB146259DAF34.quest_subtitle: "Are you ready? Not yeti"
	quest.41CBB146259DAF34.title: "Find the Yeti Cave"
	quest.41FE37817AC6ACC6.quest_desc: [
		"The &bSmudge Tool&r, simply put, helps you to &ablend out hard edges&r. However, note that the color it smudges is &dbased on the color you place it on initially&r, and if you place it over multiple colors, it will mix them. It takes some getting used to."
		""
		"The &bMagnifying Glass&r helps you to &azoom into your drawing&r to ensure perfect pixel placement! It can be used with &bany other tool&r and can be &6stowed with right click&r."
	]
	quest.41FE37817AC6ACC6.title: "Drawing Assistance 2"
	quest.427FD234857AEBE8.quest_desc: ["&bInfused Fabric&r is the basis for creating your very first set of &bWitch Robes&r. The warp and weft are perfectly balanced, giving this extra defense despite only being fabric."]
	quest.427FD234857AEBE8.quest_subtitle: "Of course it's black"
	quest.427FD234857AEBE8.title: "Obtain Infused Fabric"
	quest.42C94ED483CD4AB8.quest_desc: [
		"The White &cSempiternal Sanctum&r grants a chance at the &bEssence of Continuity&r."
		""
		"Holding this item in your offhand will &aallow you to defy death&r - upon losing all HP, you will be &ateleported to your spawn point&r with full health, hunger bar filled, and all status effects removed."
		""
		"It only has &a1 use before it is depleted&r and needs 40 minutes to recharge. It will only recharge in the inventory of someone who has &aconsumed &bEssence of the Bees&r. Upon use, it will also set cooldown on all other Essences of Continuity."
		""
		"Upon prevention of death, the item will also give you a &bWritten Book&r with details of where you were and how you almost died."
	]
	quest.42C94ED483CD4AB8.quest_subtitle: "the color of life"
	quest.42C94ED483CD4AB8.title: "Sempiternal Sanctum: White"
	quest.42DD1CCF09065C51.quest_desc: [
		"It's hard to overstate my satisfaction with the job you've done &amaking these cakes&r. They're so delicious and moist!"
		""
		"But look at me still talking when there's questing to do. Take this reward, I figure you'll probably need some new teeth after this."
	]
	quest.42DD1CCF09065C51.quest_subtitle: "HUGE SUCCESS"
	quest.42DD1CCF09065C51.title: "Cake-a-holic"
	quest.4307E6EA2E01F82B.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Soul Lantern"
	quest.434E391D87C3EBD9.quest_desc: ["The &bEnder Satchel&r is a storage upgrade which &agrants easy access to your Ender Chest inventory!&r."]
	quest.435BD760D0F2E010.quest_desc: ["Mushroom colonies can be &agrown in complete darkness&r using &bRich Soil&r. If you &6harvest one with shears&r, you will get the whole colony. &6Harvest it with your hand&r and you will get up to 5 mushrooms. Hooray for mush!"]
	quest.435BD760D0F2E010.quest_subtitle: "So happy together"
	quest.435BD760D0F2E010.title: "Obtain a Mushroom Colony"
	quest.4388413B656A4336.title: "A Well-Equipped Chef"
	quest.439A33514ABCCEFA.quest_desc: ["The &bEpitaph&r is an item that the cautious witch should never be without! Upon death, it &aplaces a &bFleeting Memorial&r in your death location, allowing you to &bteleport directly back to your place of death&r from the nearest &bWaystone&r."]
	quest.439BC18CF8CE9960.quest_desc: ["These teas may be unflavored, but they're certainly not flavorless! Although &bCeylon Black Tea&r, &bOolong Tea&r, and &bSencha Green Tea&r do not provide ingame effects, they do function as &adecoration blocks&r!"]
	quest.439BC18CF8CE9960.title: "Plain Teas"
	quest.43B3A6804B59565E.quest_desc: [
		"Prove your mettle by killing...wait, just one &ezombie&r and one &eskeleton&r? That seems pretty easy..."
		""
		"Maybe the next quests will be more difficult."
	]
	quest.43B3A6804B59565E.quest_subtitle: "or wand, or... whatever"
	quest.43B3A6804B59565E.title: "First Swings of a Sword"
	quest.43CC7A6F8C1284B5.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCheese Press&r is a rudimentary machine which will help &acondense your Milk into Cheese&r. Although you can also achieve this via a &bMechanical Press&r from Create, it's always good to know the original methods of doing something!"
		""
		"Simply place your &bMilk&r and your &bRennet&r into the Press and then &6wait patiently&r (or use Time in a Bottle) for it to work its magic."
		""
		"Different &atypes of Milk&r will make unique cheeses... but more on that elsewhere!"
	]
	quest.43CC7A6F8C1284B5.quest_subtitle: "press cheese everyday"
	quest.43CC7A6F8C1284B5.title: "Obtain a Cheese Press"
	quest.443F18D755145E26.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Flowers"
	quest.4449135F7D10724F.quest_desc: [
		"&bRennet&r is a substance rendered from... actually, you know what? Let's not go into the details. It's protein. Let's just... grab some &beggs&r. And you'll need &bSalt&r and &bGlass Bottles&r to put it in!"
		""
		"The important part to know is that it makes &bCheese&r. Which you can now do! Well, once you &amake a Cheese Press&r. Let's do that now!"
	]
	quest.4470E2B09DB2B676.quest_desc: ["Congratulations, you have opened 10 trapped chests! An achievement worth celebrating. Now heal up."]
	quest.4470E2B09DB2B676.title: "Unlucky or just Ignorant"
	quest.4482909B2A137E38.quest_desc: [
		"The &bHoney Compass&r you just got is a special one - it will point you &atoward a &cThrone Pillar&r, where the &eQueen Bee&r can be found!"
		""
		"Make sure you are &aon your best bee-haviour."
	]
	quest.45964A10A11F9924.title: "Basic Spawn Eggs"
	quest.45ED6F2E8BA02BE1.quest_desc: ["The &bEnder Watcher&r transmits a Redstone signal when &aa player is looking at it&r. The signal intensity is determined by how far the player is."]
	quest.45ED6F2E8BA02BE1.title: "Obtain an Ender Watcher"
	quest.45FE520AC009290F.quest_desc: [
		"The Red &cSempiternal Sanctum&r grants a chance at the &bEssence of Raging&r."
		""
		"Holding this item in offhand will &ahighlight 4 nearby hostile mobs in red&r. Killing them will &agrant you &bStrength&r, and it will &ahighlight more hostile mobs&r nearby. Each highlighted kill makes your &bStrength&r effect more powerful, and maxes out at &bStrength 16&r after killing &a7 highlighted mobs&r."
		""
		"The &bStrength&r only lasts 15 seconds between kills. If time runs out, or if you kill a non-highlighted mob, the &aitem goes into 10 second cooldown&r. Making any kill after you've maxed your &bStrength&r will also set the item to cooldown."
		""
		"It has &a28 uses (highlighted kills) before it is depleted&r and needs 30 minutes to recharge. To recharge, it must &abe in the inventory of a player that has consumed &bEssence of the Bees&r. It will set cooldown on all other &bEssence of Raging&r items that player is holding as well, due to how powerful this item is."
	]
	quest.45FE520AC009290F.quest_subtitle: "the color of power"
	quest.45FE520AC009290F.title: "Sempiternal Sanctum: Red"
	quest.4655801A35B3BAB2.quest_desc: [
		"A witch's garden is a magical place, for it is here that they can commune the most deeply with nature. Placing your hands in the earth, bringing water to dry soil, feeling the breeze on your skin and the fire in your heart; it's little wonder that gardening is such a powerful feeling."
		""
		"Although any plants can bring mystic energy to a place, some are more special than others."
		""
		"The items you gather for this quest have myriad uses - they can be &abrewed into potions&r, &acrafted into spells&r, or act as &areagents&r."
		""
		"- &bWild Roots&r can be found under trees or &cunderground&r."
		"- &bWolfsbane&r, &bWater Artichoke&r, and &bSage Seeds&r can be found by &6breaking grass&r."
		"- &bMandrake&r, &bBelladonna&r, &bYellow Dock&r, and &bMugwort&r can be found &cin swamp biomes&r."
		"- &bGrove Moss&r can be found &agrowing on trees&r."
	]
	quest.4655801A35B3BAB2.title: "Happy Witch: Garden [Part 1]"
	quest.468D0B739D93E018.quest_desc: ["The &bCold Eye&r once belonged to an Iceologer, and can be found hidden in &dan igloo's hidden basement&r."]
	quest.470A6825C49EEFAF.title: "Defeat the Knight Phantoms"
	quest.47639E492B01312E.quest_desc: ["You discovered an &cEnd City&r! These structures, once occupied by the &aEnder Elite&r, are now home to vicious &eShulkers&r, who want nothing more than to &aensure you never touch solid ground again&r."]
	quest.47A3914CBE99E42D.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter will help you &atrack your progress through the modpack&r. As you complete &bchapters of the Quest Book&r, you'll be awarded &bKeepsakes&r, all of which contribute to one &afinal rite&r: &dthe Rite of the Wyldkeeper&r."
		""
		"Although &lCottage Witch&r is primarily a sandbox, this is your overarching goal as you complete the tasks that bring you the most joy. It can be ignored if you wish, but &agrants some special rewards&r."
	]
	quest.486FE1761F7E41E3.quest_desc: [
		"You did it! You've finally obtained the holy grail of foods: &bcheese&r. There are a number of incredible dishes which can be made with &ole fromage&r (pardon my French), but why not go straight to the source and make some &bFondue&r? You'll need a &bWhole Cheese Wheel&r for that, but for many recipes, you need just &aa single slice&r!"
		""
		"To &aobtain &bCheese Pieces&r, &6place down&r your Cheese Wheel and &6right click&r it with an empty hand."
	]
	quest.486FE1761F7E41E3.quest_subtitle: "that's the stuff, gromit!"
	quest.486FE1761F7E41E3.title: "Obtain a Cheese Wheel"
	quest.48D0F767CFD4070B.quest_desc: [
		"If you were particularly crude and uncultured, you might associate the &bStaff&r exclusively with &aWizardry&r, but in truth, that's a common misconception."
		""
		"As it turns out, Staves can be used by anyone, from &aHermits&r to &aDruids&r to - dare I say -  &aWarlocks&r, and yes, even &aWitches&r. In fact, &a&oespecially&r &aWitches&r. They are a marvelous way to &aconnect with Nature&r and an excellent Focus to use for spellcasting."
		""
		"You can craft one with &bLogs&r and &bWildroot&r. Then, you'll naturally be in want of &bsome spells&r to cast, don't you think?"
	]
	quest.48D0F767CFD4070B.quest_subtitle: "you're the staff manager now"
	quest.48D0F767CFD4070B.title: "A Trusty Staff"
	quest.48FB2E853260CF25.title: "Catch Special Fish"
	quest.4918B7871C3246B4.quest_desc: [
		"Collect a whole set of &bBee Armor&r to complete this quest."
		""
		"The &bStingless Bee Helmet&r, when worn, will &ahighlight all &eBees&r and &eBeehemoths&r when &6you crouch&r. You can also &6right click &eBees&r with an empty hand to &aput them on your head&r! The bee will leave your head if you &atake damage&r, &acrouch&r, &ago underwater&r, &aobtain Wrath of the Hive&r effect, or &aafter 30 seconds&r passes. &bNausea &aduration will also decrease&r twice as fast when this armor is on and &bPoison&r duration will be &aslightly decreased&r as well."
		""
		"The &bChestplate&r gives you &abrief flight&r if you &6jump after jumping&r. The &bBeenergized&r effect will improve this. It also makes you &aimmune to &bFreezing&r!"
		""
		"The &bLeggings&r allow you to resist &bSlowness&r from &lBumblezone&r blocks. You can also use them to &acollect &bPollen&r from flowers! You can use this to &6spawn a &ePollen Puff&r by &6crouching&r. Additionally, all &bSlowness&r durations will be &adecreased&r."
		""
		"These &bBoots&r can &aautomine many kinds&r of &bwood&r, &bbeehive&r, or &bhoneycomb&r blocks that you are standing on - simply &6look down and hold crouch&r."
		""
		"The boots can be enchanted with the normal boot enchantments but can also be enchanted with &bEfficiency&r, &bSilk Touch&r, and &bFortune&r. To go with Efficiency, the boots also mine faster when you have the full bee armor set on or have Beenergized status effect. These mining speed boosts &ado stack&r."
		""
		"The boots will also let you briefly hang on walls made of wood, beehive, or honeycomb blocks allowing you to wall jump or wall run!"
	]
	quest.4918B7871C3246B4.title: "The Full Set: Bee Armor, Variant 1"
	quest.492DDC880E65C534.quest_desc: [
		"A &bStove&r is an incredibly useful tool. Thanks to your inherent magic, it is fueled at all times! You can &6place up to 6 food items&r on the grill in order to cook them. They'll pop up into items when they're ready! You can &6place an upside-down &bBasket&r above it to collect them automatically."
		""
		"The &bStove&r can also be used as a heat source for the &bCooking Pot&r, but if you do it that way, you cannot place items on the grill."
	]
	quest.492DDC880E65C534.quest_subtitle: "Steve's Stove"
	quest.492DDC880E65C534.title: "Create a Stove"
	quest.4930ECD60EA9ED8D.quest_desc: [
		"You've obtained some &bseeds&r, congratulations! The first step of becoming a successful farmer is to have something to plant."
		""
		"As a reward, take this &bOrganic Compost&r - place it in the world and wait for it to decompose into &bRich Soil&r. Placing it near water, especially running water, will accelerate the process!"
		""
		"&bRich Soil&r will &aperiodically grant a growth boost&r to crops (when it's provided with water) and it &acannot be trampled&r. It &acan also be used to grow &bMushroom Colonies&r in complete darkness."
	]
	quest.4930ECD60EA9ED8D.quest_subtitle: "a bit seedy, perhaps"
	quest.4930ECD60EA9ED8D.title: "Obtain Some Seeds"
	quest.4971EB753FE0E6CC.quest_desc: [
		"Thank you for picking up this issue of &lThe Savvy Witch&r - the mail-order publication that no deal-conscious witch would dare be seen without!"
		""
		"This issue brings you the usual fare of &bneedful things&r such as &bIngredients&r, &bSupplies&r, &bEquipment&r, and of course, &bFashion&r!"
		""
		"In this &bCatalogue&r, you can spend &bNumismatic Coins&r &adirectly from your bank balance&r - although of course you can also pay &avia your inventory&r. Simply &6click the quest task&r to place your order, then &6click the reward&r to have it &asent automatically to your mailbox&r. You &odo&r have a mailbox, don't you?"
	]
	quest.4971EB753FE0E6CC.title: "The Savvy Witch's Sundry"
	quest.49EA7F3135E2CC74.quest_desc: [
		"The Blue &cSempiternal Sanctum&r grants a chance at the &bEssence of Calming&r."
		""
		"Holding this item in your offhand will &aprevent you from drawing aggro&r from hostile mobs!"
		""
		"The effect is lost early if player &agets hurt by or attacks any mob&r. If the player sprints while it is active, the &ditem loses power very quickly&r."
		""
		"It has &a600 durability&r before it is depleted and needs 10 minutes to recharge. It will only recharge in the inventory of someone who has &aconsumed &bEssence of the Bees&r."
	]
	quest.49EA7F3135E2CC74.quest_subtitle: "the color of peace"
	quest.49EA7F3135E2CC74.title: "Sempiternal Sanctum: Blue"
	quest.49EE2D61A0D4D01C.title: "The Crock Pot"
	quest.4A605045E159E5BD.quest_desc: ["Use your &bSpyglass&r to research 50 &bPlants&r!"]
	quest.4A8A373C89D91E51.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Sweet Berries"
	quest.4ABFB1778565B4B7.quest_desc: [
		"By the time you make yourself some &bstarting tools&r, you may already be hoping for some more storage."
		""
		"While you can eventually craft better &bBackpacks&r, in the meantime you'll certainly want this basic one! Do check them out - the smartest witch knows that inventory management is crucial!"
		""
		"Also, take this &bWishlist&r. If you &6hover over an item in JEI and press the hotkey&r (K by default), it will wishlist that item. Wishlisted items will &aglow yellow&r if you see them in the world, or find them in chests! Very helpful if you have a terrible memory, like I do."
		""
		"Finally, the &bTool Belt&r is a &bcurio&r which allows you to &astore your tools in a radial wheel and summon them with a hotkey&r (Y by default). It can be upgraded to &ahold more tools&r!"
	]
	quest.4ABFB1778565B4B7.title: "Obtain Stone Tools"
	quest.4ADE26321BA3720D.quest_desc: ["The &bCrafting&r and &bStonecutter&r upgrades provide those &acrafting interfaces&r in the storage you place them in."]
	quest.4ADE26321BA3720D.title: "Crafting Upgrades"
	quest.4B09C2508E25AD2B.quest_desc: [
		"This modpack comes with &aa lot of resourcepacks&r for you to use! However, we offer some profile options for you to easily pick what suits you best."
		""
		"Access the Profiles by clicking the hamburger menu:"
		""
		"{image:quest_enhance:textures/ftb/clipboard_1788216858374.png width:345 height:204 align:center fit:false}"
		""
		"and then choose the profile you prefer:"
		""
		"{image:quest_enhance:textures/ftb/clipboard_1788217044359.png width:345 height:272 align:center fit:true click_action:none:}"
	]
	quest.4B09C2508E25AD2B.quest_subtitle: "everything in its place"
	quest.4B09C2508E25AD2B.title: "Resource Pack Applications"
	quest.4B1050C983FA2708.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Sea Pickle"
	quest.4B26B50D268DBA07.quest_desc: [
		"It's important for us to make the distinction between simply &ofishing&r and &ostarcatching&r. You see, while both are important, one is significantly harder - and sometimes more rewarding - than the other."
		""
		"To go fishing, you'll need a &bFishing Rod&r."
		""
		"To go &ostarcatching&r (and don't ask me why it's called that - I'm a witch, not a fisherman), you'll need a &bStarcatcher's Rod&r. You can &aadd attachments&r to this rod such as new &bHooks&r and &bBobbers&r, but it cannot be otherwise upgraded, &aonly sidegraded&r, by &6using templates to change its appearance&r."
		""
		"&dSimply put - Starcatching allows you to catch unique fish&r. You go fishing for food, you go starcatching for fun."
	]
	quest.4B26B50D268DBA07.quest_subtitle: "for different, uh, bods?"
	quest.4B26B50D268DBA07.title: "Different Rods"
	quest.4B879A11C0823832.quest_desc: [
		"Should you wish to have &amore storage&r, you can &aupgrade your backpack&r to higher tiers by &6crafting it with the materials you wish to upgrade to&r."
		""
		"Here is an example of upgrading &bIron&r to &bGold&r:"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/backpackupgrade.png width:100 height:50 align:1 fit:true}"
	]
	quest.4BB2ED765707EA69.quest_desc: [
		"The &eFoliaath&r is an herbaceous yet carnivorous monster which lays in wait for its prey, only showing its toothy maw once a victim draws close enough."
		""
		"In general, &aranged weapons are effective&r against it. Once defeated, it may drop &bFoliaath Seeds&r, which can be planted and &anurtured into your very own Foliaath&r. Simply &6plant the seeds on Grass&r, and be sure to &6feed it some meat twice a day&r to help it grow big and strong. Awww, baby. It'll totally still try to kill you, though."
		""
		"&dA note from the witch: I am not sure that the babies are currently implemented&r. Either that, or I do not have a green thumb."
	]
	quest.4BB2ED765707EA69.title: "Surprise!"
	quest.4BD1E1D3ABC4BEE8.quest_desc: [
		"To &acraft &bPoppets&r, you'll need a &bSpinning Wheel&r and &acertain other reagents&r, as well as a &bpowered Altar&r. Place the correct ingredients into the &bSpinning Wheel&r, and if it's within range of your &bAltar&r (and you have enough altar power), it will begin crafting! This process takes a while, so &dbe patient&r. I feel like I say that a lot. I suppose any craft requires patience, doesn't it?"
		""
		"An &bArmor Poppet&r (they say Armour, but bear with me) will &aprevent a piece of equipment from being lost when it's about to break&r. The &bPoppet&r will break instead, and the equipment will be left with &aone durability&r (so you'll want to take it off quickly)!"
		""
		"But in order for this to work, first you have to &abind it to yourself&r."
	]
	quest.4BD1E1D3ABC4BEE8.title: "Intermediate Poppetry"
	quest.4BE2F61081D4D690.quest_desc: ["The &eAllay&r are kind and gentle creatures which are coveted for their &apropensity to collect items&r. Give them an item to hold, and they will &apick that item type from the ground&r and put it in a nearby inventory!"]
	quest.4BE2F61081D4D690.title: "Meet the Allay"
	quest.4C4835404E2B4DA3.quest_desc: [
		"Isn't it preposterous that you have to &acommit murder in order to sleep at night&r in early game? Okay, maybe I'm being a little dramatic. But if you ask the &eSheep&r..."
		""
		"Anyway, why not make things a little easier on yourself (and the &eSheep&r) with a pair of &bWooden Shears&r?"
	]
	quest.4C4835404E2B4DA3.quest_subtitle: "those sheep won't know what hit em"
	quest.4C4835404E2B4DA3.title: "Obtain Wooden Shears"
	quest.4CCF9884656CBD33.quest_desc: [
		"&lFunctional Storage&r also adds &bFramed Drawers&r, which can take on &atextures from blocks&r to help &amatch your decor&r."
		""
		"To customize a &bFramed Drawer&r, you must put the Drawer into a Crafting Grid with &a2 full blocks&r - you cannot use items like &bCarpets&r or &bDragon Eggs&r (I tried)."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/frameddrawers.png width:200 height:200 align:1}"
		""
		"The &bfirst block&r will be the texture of the &aoutside&r of the Drawer."
		""
		"The &bsecond block&r will be the texture of the &ainside&r of the Drawer."
		""
		"The &bthird block&r needs to be &athe Drawer itself&r."
		""
		"Using any two full blocks ensures you can create &astorage as awesome - or as ugly - as you choose&r!"
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/frameddrawers2.png width:100 height:100 align:1}"
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/frameddrawers3.png width:100 height:100 align:1}"
	]
	quest.4CCF9884656CBD33.quest_subtitle: "i've been framed!"
	quest.4CCF9884656CBD33.title: "Framed Drawers"
	quest.4CEA87A9E500920A.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know that you can &6use &bShears&6 to liberate a &eSnow Golem&r from its &bPumpkin&r prison?"
		""
		"Do so, and you shall be rewarded!"
	]
	quest.4CEA87A9E500920A.title: "Free the Snow Golem"
	quest.4D65AA1353AA0E1D.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCrafting Bowl&r is a ubiquitous kitchen tool used to &amix together ingredients&r for things such as &bDough&r, &bSweet Dough&r, and &bCake Dough&r! You can also use it to &6make &bButter&r."
		""
		"You can &6hover over it in your inventory and press U&r to &aview its recipes&r."
		""
		"To actually &ause it&r, first &6place it down&r and then &6click it with the ingredients&r. Once it's got everything, then you can &6hold right click to stir&r until it's fully blended, then &6right click again&r to claim the completed recipe!"
	]
	quest.4D65AA1353AA0E1D.quest_subtitle: "you feel something stirring"
	quest.4D77214933327DFB.quest_desc: [
		"Oops! You've garnered yourself the &dWrath of the Hive&r, a condition which makes &aall nearby bees furious&r. They will attack you, and any non-bee creatures nearby."
		""
		"It turns out, &eBees&r don't like it when you steal their hard-earned &bHoney&r, or &aattempting to harm them&r. The following actions will anger the hive:"
		""
		"- Damaging any &eBee&r or their &eQueen&r."
		"- Breaking translucent &bHoney Blocks&r."
		"- Using Glass Bottles on &bFilled Porous Honeycomb blocks&r."
		"- Destroying a &bHoneycomb Brood Block&r without &aSilk Touch&r."
		"- Entering a &cCell Maze&r."
		""
		"How can you avoid this negative effect? Well, you can &aingratiate yourself to the hive&r by &6feeding sweets to &eBees&r. This will sometimes grant you &bProtection of the Hive&r, which will cause Bees to come to your aid in battle, and provides a &done time forgiveness&r when doing any of the above actions."
		""
		"- &bSugar Water Bottles&r have a 7% chance of granting &bProtection of the Hive&r."
		"- &bHoney Bottles&r have a 30% chance"
		"- Feeding a bee a &bHoney Bucket&r will give an 80% chance, as well as putting nearby Bees into &alove mode&r, and fully heal the targeted bee. If the targeted bee is a baby, it has a chance of &agrowing up immediately&r."
		"- &bRoyal Jelly&r - either bottle or bucket - will fully heal the &eBee&r, age up a Baby one, and gives a 100% chance of &bProtection of the Hive&r."
	]
	quest.4DEE27DAF79C58ED.title: "Catch Oasis Fish"
	quest.4DFEEDE1DAACD8B7.quest_desc: [
		"You have met the regal &eQueen Bee&r! What an honor. As it turns out, the &eQueen&r loves &ato trade&r! You can try trading random items with her, and see what you may get in return! Items can be &6dropped in front of her&r or you can &6right click her while holding them&r."
		""
		"If you don't feel like experimenting - In &lJEI&r you can see a list of &aQueen Bee Trades&r. Find the &bQueen Bee Spawn Egg&r in JEI and &6right click it&r to view all trades."
		""
		"Upon the first successful trade, you will be given &aThe Queen's Desires&r advancement line, which gives a &bRoyal Jelly Bottle&r reward for each advancement completed. After completing the entire advancement line, you get the &bEssence of the Bees&r item!"
		""
		"To track your progress, &6check your advancements&r!"
		""
		"For more information on trading, please see the next page."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &eBee Queen&r will sometimes pick one tradable item as a &bBonus Trade&r, and tell nearby players that she &awants that item especially, for the next 20 minutes&r. If the player trades that item with the queen, they get &a3 times the reward and xp&r!"
		""
		"They can do this up to &a24 times&r before the Queen is satisfied and the &aBonus Trade is depleted until the 20 minutes runs out&r. Then the Queen picks a new item for Bonus Trading!"
		""
		"You can &astill trade other items with the Queen&r for normal amount of rewards at any time even when the Queen is not asking for that item."
		""
		"On &acertain days of the year&r, the Bonus Trade system will turn off and the &eBee Queen&r will ask for specific items to do &aspecial trades just for those days&r! You can still do normal trades with other items during this time. These &dspecial hidden trades do not show up in &lJEI&r."
	]
	quest.4DFEEDE1DAACD8B7.quest_subtitle: "not quite beyonce"
	quest.4DFEEDE1DAACD8B7.title: "An Audience with the Queen"
	quest.4E4341D997F9AE98.quest_desc: [
		"Making cheese is a little different than simple meal preparation. Hence why you should &aget yourself a &bCooking Frame&r, to help you in making some brand new recipes."
		""
		"This cooking device will help you to &arender &bRennet&r, but it can also &acook simple meats&r and even make some delicious meals."
	]
	quest.4E4341D997F9AE98.title: "Obtain a Cooking Frame"
	quest.4E8C0079E6F9A13A.quest_desc: [
		"You can obtain a &bCloud in a Bottle&r by ascending to &acloud height&r and &6right clicking the air with a glass bottle&r."
		""
		"You can release the Cloud by right-clicking the bottle in the air. It will shortly disappear. However, if the cloud is &6replaced with another block&r, it returns to the bottle. This allows you to &aplace blocks in midair&r."
	]
	quest.4EAB1C3073616E17.quest_desc: ["This &bBrick Sink&r is a one-block &ainfinite water source&r! Simply &6right click it&r to turn on the faucet and &afill it with water&r, then &6right click it with a &bBucket&r or &bBottle&r to collect the water!"]
	quest.4EAB1C3073616E17.quest_subtitle: "everything AND the kitchen sink"
	quest.4EAB1C3073616E17.title: "Obtain a Sink"
	quest.4EAE4C40B444930A.quest_desc: [
		"Find yourself a &eQuest Ram&r and you'll notice it seems to be missing something."
		""
		"Maybe give it some &amore wool&r. Specifically, &6one of each color of wool&r."
	]
	quest.4EAE4C40B444930A.title: "Complete the Quest Ram"
	quest.4F3616F8CE8F6F2B.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSniffer&r is an ancient being with a &avery developed sense of smell&r. They love to &adig up ancient seeds&r not available anywhere else!"
		""
		"In this modpack, there's an increased amount of &aitems they can find&r, and their functionality is also expanded! For example, you can now &6saddle and ride&r them, and even &6attach chests&r to them, which will allow them to &astore the items they sniff up&r!"
	]
	quest.4F3616F8CE8F6F2B.quest_subtitle: "sniffa"
	quest.4F3616F8CE8F6F2B.title: "Meet a Sniffer"
	quest.4F8BE51C9D3C16A2.quest_desc: ["&bKnives&r from this mod will guarantee you &aadditional drops from animals&r, such as &bfeathers&r or &bleather&r, as well as &aadditional drops when breaking grass&r. This makes it much easier to get started on your agricultural and culinary journey."]
	quest.4F8BE51C9D3C16A2.quest_subtitle: "what's that? a knife! NO!!"
	quest.4F8BE51C9D3C16A2.title: "Obtain a Knife"
	quest.4F9A1B244734638F.quest_desc: [
		"Who doesn't love the joyful bright colors and enchanting scent of &bFresh Flowers&r?"
		""
		"There are many different ways for you to &adisplay these plants in your base&r. Why not try each option and decide which you like best?"
		""
		"Note that &dnot all flowers can be planted in all flower boxes&r. Some may only accept flowers from the mod that adds them (such as &lMeadow&r), and some may only accept &avanilla flowers&r."
	]
	quest.4F9A1B244734638F.quest_subtitle: "there's a lot of em"
	quest.4F9A1B244734638F.title: "Flower Display Options"
	quest.4FDB48B5AE01AFB4.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Mangrove Propagule"
	quest.4FEE0688A44D8421.quest_desc: [
		"Before you can chow down on your &bStuffed Hoglin&r, you must first &6carve off the finest delicacy&r - the &bears&r. Delicious!"
		"Then, you can &aobtain dishes&r from the remainder of the meal by &6clicking on the Hoglin with a bowl&r. Don't waste any!"
	]
	quest.4FEE0688A44D8421.quest_subtitle: "He even carved the Roast Beast!"
	quest.4FEE0688A44D8421.title: "Carve the Stuffed Hoglin"
	quest.505C0E55270CBFBC.quest_desc: [
		"Looking for something to spend some time on? Why not &aa Scavenger Hunt?&r. Obtain these items for the ability to claim an incredible prize!"
		""
		"&6Click the checkbox in this quest to begin.&r. This can be done at any time."
	]
	quest.505C0E55270CBFBC.quest_subtitle: "Time to scavenge!"
	quest.507ACD6D650DECA2.quest_desc: ["&bHoglin Hide&r can be used in cooking recipes, or cleaned on a &bCutting Board&r to create &bLeather&r."]
	quest.507ACD6D650DECA2.quest_subtitle: "Hoglin, hide!"
	quest.5085CFDE1E14144D.quest_desc: [
		"The &eFerrous Wroughtnaught&r is an ancient magical construct from the early days, when magic was raw and uncontrolled, and got everywhere (what a nuisance having to dust constantly). It is overwhelmingly powerful, and borderline invulnerable. In fact, only one brave witch was able to &apierce it with his sword&r, and he paid the ultimate price in doing so."
		""
		"You must be sure to &aavoid its attacks&r, as it can easily &adestroy a shield in a single hit&r. However, it moves ponderously, so perhaps it's possible to keep dodging."
		""
		"Who knows what manner of treasures it would drop upon death? Not to mention, you'll get a pretty penny from me, as well. All that creaking it does has really been disturbing my meditation."
	]
	quest.50C0D0CE7E13EE91.title: "Cat Ears"
	quest.50DA655C90509B80.quest_desc: ["Ah, a familiar sight, yet somehow new! A &cWitch's Hut&r, home to one of your kin and their cat. Perhaps it would be nice to &astop in and say hello&r?"]
	quest.50DA655C90509B80.title: "Find a Better Witch Hut"
	quest.50DC32C40279EF48.quest_desc: [
		"A &bSilkworm&r is the larval form of the &bSilk Moth&r, and are often found in &bSilkworm Cocoons&r growing &aon the sides of &cCottonwood&r or &cDark Oak trees&r. If you find one of these &bCocoons&r, you can either &6right click it with a torch&r to &aencourage it to hatch into a &eSilk Moth&r (this takes a few seconds) - or you can &6break the Cocoon&r to obtain the &bSilkworm&r."
		""
		"&bSilk Fiber&r can be obtained by &afeeding &bLeaves&a to &eSilkworms&r (in a crafting grid). You can then place the Fiber &6in a &bSpinning Wheel&r to produce &bSilk Thread&r, which can be used in many important recipes such as the making of &bPoppets&r and &bClothing&r. &bSilk Thread&r can also be obtained from &bSilk Cocoons&r found near &eJumping Spiders&r."
		""
		"Note that the &bSpinning Wheel&r &dmay not appear to be doing anything&r, but it is. Just be patient!"
	]
	quest.50DC32C40279EF48.title: "Silk and Sewing"
	quest.50E64308D7D56C48.quest_desc: [
		"&bBellows&r are blocks that can &aspeed up furnaces&r, &aprevent fires from extinguishing&r, and even &apush entities&r."
		""
		"The rate at which the Bellows pump is determined by the strength of the &aRedstone signal&r it is receiving."
	]
	quest.50E64308D7D56C48.quest_subtitle: "Holler and bellow"
	quest.50E72CE5ED450E23.quest_desc: ["Psst - you can also &6click a &bChocolate Cake&r with a &bCherry&r to make a &bChocolate Gateau&r!"]
	quest.5107C3DE453627D5.quest_desc: ["Although it is difficult to make, the &bTarot Deck&r will allow you to hold &aall your cards in a single slot&r, when &aequipped as a Curio&r."]
	quest.511581BF899A9D1D.quest_desc: [
		"A &bDrawer&r is a storage item that can store &large amounts&r of single items, &astacking beyond the normal limit&r. A 1x1 drawer can hold a single item type. A 2x2 drawer can hold four item types, but less of each."
		""
		"The &bDrawers&r are also handy in that they &adisplay their contents&r, making them an excellent choice for items you need frequent access to."
	]
	quest.511581BF899A9D1D.quest_subtitle: "drawers and artists are distinct things"
	quest.511581BF899A9D1D.title: "Functional Storage through Drawers"
	quest.512561271D178D2D.quest_desc: [
		"Collect a whole set of &bBee Armor&r to complete this quest."
		""
		"The &bStingless Bee Helmet&r, when worn, will &ahighlight all &eBees&r and &eBeehemoths&r when &6you crouch&r. You can also &6right click &eBees&r with an empty hand to &aput them on your head&r! The bee will leave your head if you &atake damage&r, &acrouch&r, &ago underwater&r, &aobtain Wrath of the Hive&r effect, or &aafter 30 seconds&r passes. &bNausea &aduration will also decrease&r twice as fast when this armor is on and &bPoison&r duration will be &aslightly decreased&r as well."
		""
		"The &bChestplate&r gives you &abrief flight&r if you &6jump after jumping&r. The &bBeenergized&r effect will improve this. It also makes you &aimmune to &bFreezing&r!"
		""
		"The &bLeggings&r allow you to resist &bSlowness&r from &lBumblezone&r blocks. You can also use them to &acollect &bPollen&r from flowers! You can use this to &6spawn a &ePollen Puff&r by &6crouching&r. Additionally, all &bSlowness&r durations will be &adecreased&r."
		""
		"These &bBoots&r can &aautomine many kinds&r of &bwood&r, &bbeehive&r, or &bhoneycomb&r blocks that you are standing on - simply &6look down and hold crouch&r."
		""
		"The boots can be enchanted with the normal boot enchantments but can also be enchanted with &bEfficiency&r, &bSilk Touch&r, and &bFortune&r. To go with Efficiency, the boots also mine faster when you have the full bee armor set on or have Beenergized status effect. These mining speed boosts &ado stack&r."
		""
		"The boots will also let you briefly hang on walls made of wood, beehive, or honeycomb blocks allowing you to wall jump or wall run!"
	]
	quest.512561271D178D2D.title: "The Full Set: Bee Armor, Variant 2"
	quest.512C813AEE3A5BCD.quest_desc: [
		"The &bCandelabra&r is a decorative block which can be placed above or below blocks in order to light the surrounding area."
		""
		"It seamlessly connects to hanging &bChains&r."
		""
		"And, I should mention, you can use it to &aupgrade your altar&r!"
	]
	quest.512C813AEE3A5BCD.quest_subtitle: "Abracandelabra!"
	quest.512C813AEE3A5BCD.title: "Obtain a Candelabra"
	quest.513067CD571D369E.quest_desc: ["Rumors swirl about the &bCorrupted Eye&r, of its ability to bring infinite fortune to its owner. However, the greedy king who last owned it faded into obscurity, so perhaps those rumors are just that. Legend has it that it's kept in a &dPillager Tower&r somewhere."]
	quest.51383D499E0DF0DA.quest_desc: [
		"You might be wondering where all the quests are, when your screen looks like this:"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/questmenu.png width:300 height:200 align:1}"
		""
		"See that &aarrow on the left bar&r? &6Hovering over that&r will show you all the categories."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/questmenu2.png width:300 height:200 align:1}"
		""
		"Be sure to &6click the Pin in the upper right&r to keep this sidebar open permanently!"
	]
	quest.51383D499E0DF0DA.title: "Don't Lose Your Place"
	quest.51F84C9F2CA50DA7.quest_desc: [
		"The inner world of &eBees&r is a deep one. They possess incredible intelligence, problem solving, and even have a cultural hierarchy. They the only insects which have been observed to &adance for fun&r! They represent innovation, creativity, wisdom, community, and love. &bHoney&r is often used in rituals, especially for sweetening spells."
		""
		"If you wish to delve deeper into the lives of these magical creatures, find a &bBee Nest&r and &6throw an &bEnder Pearl&r at it!"
	]
	quest.51F84C9F2CA50DA7.title: "Find a Bee's Nest"
	quest.52BC8196E858B238.quest_desc: [
		"Gain this advancement by taming and befriending an animal!"
		""
		"Using the &bCage&r reward from this quest, you can right click to place an entity in your inventory so you can easily move them large distances. Simply &6right click the &bCage&r on the animal, and then &6right click it on a block&r to place the animal down again."
		""
		"You can also &6shift right click&r to place the &bCage&r as a block to display your new pal. Putting your friends in cages is &ototally normal&r."
	]
	quest.52BC8196E858B238.quest_subtitle: "IDK, my BFF Cow?"
	quest.52C4175797FFE14B.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Diamond"
	quest.52D20498843EECD3.quest_desc: [
		"Within your storage settings, you have the ability to change the way your storage behaves."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/sophsettings.png width:200 height:140 align:center}"
		""
		"Select the &aBarrel icon&r to choose whether your settings apply to &aPlayer&r - ie, &oall&r your storages  - or &aStorage&r - ie, this container only."
		""
		"Select the &aA/Z icon&r you can select (with &6left click&r) or deselect (with &6right click&r) slots to be auto-sorted."
		""
		"Select the &aBrain icon&r to &6choose slots to be locked to the item currently in them&r."
		""
		"Select the &aSword icon&r to choose a slot whose &aitem will be displayed&r on the front of your storage."
		""
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/sophbarreldisplayy.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.52D7D562012B3B7C.quest_desc: ["To make &bCakes&r, you'll first need to &ainvent the universe&r. Wait, no, that's pies. With cakes you just need &bCake Dough&r."]
	quest.537CCA9E121868CC.quest_desc: ["The &bExotic Eye&r is associated with Atlantis - the legends say that folks used it to find the sunken city, but they never returned to confirm the tale. &6Craft it with aquatic items&r."]
	quest.53AE00DAF3CD587F.quest_desc: [
		"You've found your first &bArtifact Shard&r! Collect 9 of these and combine them in a crafting table to &arestore an &bUnidentified Artifact&r."
		""
		"Take this &bArcheology Table&r, you'll need it for the next step."
	]
	quest.53AE00DAF3CD587F.quest_subtitle: "it's pronounced \"shAHHrds\""
	quest.53AE00DAF3CD587F.title: "Find Your First Shard!"
	quest.53AF5433A87A542B.quest_desc: [
		"&eFerrets&r are adorable obligate carnivores which can be &atamed with raw rabbit&r!"
		""
		"Be aware that they will &dhunt Chickens and Rabbits&r even once tamed, so be sure to keep your livestock separated from them!"
		""
		"Tamed &eFerrets&r can also &adig for loot&r once every 5 minutes when &afed raw &bchicken&r."
	]
	quest.53AF5433A87A542B.quest_subtitle: "Terror to Chickens everywhere"
	quest.53AF5433A87A542B.title: "Meet the Ferret"
	quest.5435D7182F5A0C8D.quest_desc: ["Collect one each of every flower in the game to earn rewards!"]
	quest.5435D7182F5A0C8D.title: "Flower Picking: Blue"
	quest.545AAD86EA0B7701.quest_desc: ["The &bFramed Blueprint&r allows copying &bFramed Blocks&r including their &acosmetic block&r and &aglowing state&r. The &drotation of the Framed Block itself is not copied&r."]
	quest.546DF8992DABB86A.quest_desc: [
		"&bTree Resin&r is a key component in various spells, and is also a base ingredient for making &bIncense&r."
		""
		"You can obtain it by &6right clicking a &bLog&r or &bStripped Log&r with the &bAthame&r. However, not all trees contain resin! Instead, look for the following types of trees:"
		""
		"- Mahogany"
		"- Witch Willow"
		"- Witch Hazel"
		"- Alder"
		"- Hawthorne"
		"- Rowan"
		"- Wildwood"
		"- Grimholt"
		"- Hemlock"
		"- Dark Oak"
		"- Cottonwood"
		"- Willow"
	]
	quest.546DF8992DABB86A.title: "Obtain Some Tree Resin"
	quest.5470141CF083E30C.quest_desc: [
		"The &bConfiguration Tool&r allows you to &acustomize the appearance and performance&r of your drawers. &6Hold the Tool and shift right click&r to change its mode. Once it's set to the mode you want, &6right click it&r onto the &bDrawers&r to alter them."
		""
		"Ta-da! Magic!"
	]
	quest.5470141CF083E30C.quest_subtitle: "i see you quiver with configur.......ation"
	quest.5470141CF083E30C.title: "Configuring your Drawers"
	quest.548376041885F6D1.quest_desc: ["&bCanvas&r is a versatile material which can create &bMats&r, &bSigns&r, and more!"]
	quest.548376041885F6D1.quest_subtitle: "A blank canvas is a powerful thing"
	quest.5490D2048FF6E2AB.title: "Miscellaneous Teas"
	quest.54A57B37E1C04785.title: "Defeat The Hydra"
	quest.54A7BCDC7909E576.quest_desc: [
		"Although &bEmeralds&r are a nice currency to use among &eVillagers&r and such, when dealing with other witches, you'll want &bNumismatics&r. They're a far more robust system, including things such as &aBanking&r and &aplayer-to-player sales&r."
		""
		"The denominations, and their value in &bSpurs&r, are as follows:"
		""
		"- &bSpur&r: 1"
		"- &bBevel&r: 8"
		"- &bSprocket&r: 16"
		"- &bCog&r: 64"
		"- &bCrown&r: 512"
		"- &bSun&r: 4,096"
	]
	quest.54A7BCDC7909E576.title: "Obtain Special Currency"
	quest.54AAA9079FF8E65B.quest_desc: [
		"The Green &cSempiternal Sanctum&r grants a chance at the &bEssence of Life&r."
		""
		"Holding this item in offhand will &agrow crops and saplings nearby&r, revive &bDead Bushes&r into a random sapling, &aheal mobs tamed by you&r, and &aheal other mobs or players&r on the same team as you! Also, will cure &bPoison and &bWither effects&r."
		""
		"It has &a1000 uses before it is depleted&r and needs 10 minutes to recharge by being in the inventory of a player that had consumed &bEssence of the Bees&r in the past."
	]
	quest.54AAA9079FF8E65B.quest_subtitle: "the color of healing"
	quest.54AAA9079FF8E65B.title: "Sempiternal Sanctum: Green"
	quest.54B176A22CBFD31F.quest_desc: [
		"Scattered throughout your world are various &bSky Structures&r, of which &bCloud Islands&r are a part!"
		""
		"You may need a &bBroom&r to reach them. Or a whole lot of &bBlocks&r."
	]
	quest.54B176A22CBFD31F.quest_subtitle: "gamers DO look up"
	quest.54F9B41F96399DE6.quest_desc: [
		"As you might know, the &bEnchanting Table&r is a device which is used to &aimbue your gear with magic&r, and requires the power of &bKnowledge&r, both in &bBookshelf&r and &bExperience&r form."
		""
		"Unlike in vanilla, however, this &bEnchanting Table&r has a chance to &aapply Curses&r to your gear in addition to beneficial enchantments. In order to navigate this new challenge, it's encouraged to check out options such as &6disenchantment&r."
		""
		"&bDisenchantment&r can be pursued either through &lCognition's&r &bPrecision Dispeller&r, or &lTombstone's&r &bBook of Disenchantment&r."
	]
	quest.54F9B41F96399DE6.title: "Challenging Enchanting"
	quest.55E84F0C46D17AF5.title: "The Cooking Pot"
	quest.561E0AC36A0C1DB4.quest_desc: ["To use the &bFondue Pot&r, you must first place it atop a &bStove&r, and then &6right click it with a &bCheese Wheel&r to fill it. Once filled, take some &bBread&r and &6dip it in&r - you can get up to &a3 servings&r of a highly nutritious food this way!"]
	quest.561E0AC36A0C1DB4.quest_subtitle: "well that's a 'fon' how 'due' you do"
	quest.5688211768F55F90.quest_desc: [
		"Practicing witchcraft is just one aspect of actually being a witch, but it is arguably the most important - and the most fun!"
		""
		"A happy witch has three things: a &agarden&r, a &asacred space&r, and &blots of books&r. And probably also &bcoffee&r. And &ecats&r! Okay, so a happy witch has lots of things. But let's begin with the &bBooks&r."
	]
	quest.5688211768F55F90.title: "The Pursuit of Magic"
	quest.56A1AFEE3581AF89.quest_desc: ["The &bIron Grate&r works to keep animals inside, as they are afraid to walk over it, although you can lead them across by attaching a &bLead&r to them. &aItems will fall through it&r."]
	quest.56A1AFEE3581AF89.quest_subtitle: "well that's just grate"
	quest.56A1AFEE3581AF89.title: "Obtain Iron Grates"
	quest.56D87707F4EA479B.quest_desc: [
		"The &bRobe&r is the second part of the 3-part &bWitch&r set. This set is slightly weaker than &bDiamond&r, but stronger than &bIron&r due to its inherent magically protective properties."
		""
		"Unfortunately, witches seem not to care for pants - if you want those, you'll have to look elsewhere."
	]
	quest.56D87707F4EA479B.quest_subtitle: "Timelessly stylish, and powerful too"
	quest.56D87707F4EA479B.title: "Witch's Robe"
	quest.56DBC16948476CBE.title: "Scavenger Hunt: End Rod"
	quest.56F3B965C1198BE9.quest_desc: ["Collect one each of every flower in the game to earn rewards!"]
	quest.56F3B965C1198BE9.title: "Flower Picking: Misc"
	quest.573269BC454A499D.quest_desc: [
		"You &aprint your photographs&r using the &bLightroom&r. Here you can &aview your developed negatives&r in detail, as well."
		""
		"&bBlack and White Film&r requires &bPaper&r and &bBlack Dye&r. Printing in &acolor&r additionally requires &bCyan&r, &bMagenta&r, and &bYellow Dyes&r."
		""
		"Once you have &6chosen your photo with left click&r, you can then &6click the checkmark&r to begin printing. And ta-da! Photographs!"
	]
	quest.573269BC454A499D.title: "Printing Photos"
	quest.5763626E3E3E440B.quest_desc: [
		"Looking for a particular item in a nearby inventory?"
		""
		"Hover over the item in JEI or your inventory and &6press the keybind&r. This &dneeds to be bound by the user&r, so find a key you like and change it in your &akeybindings menu&r."
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/findme1.png width:220 height:150 align:1}"
		""
		"Then, inventories containing that item will be highlighted with these little particle effects:"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/findme2.png width:100 height:100 align:1 fit:true}"
	]
	quest.5763626E3E3E440B.title: "Finding Items In Containers"
	quest.57742DD8F99DBAF1.quest_desc: ["Much like Mushroom colonies, &bNether Fungus&r can be grown in &acomplete darkness&r using &bRich Soul Soil&r. If you &6harvest one with shears&r, you will get the whole colony. &6Harvest it with your hand&r and you will get up to 5 fungi. I've heard they're enjoyable to hang out with."]
	quest.57742DD8F99DBAF1.quest_subtitle: "I bet you're a really fun Gus"
	quest.57742DD8F99DBAF1.title: "Obtain a Nether Fungus Colony"
	quest.57B6789EE4B210E9.quest_desc: [
		"Witches are no strangers to &bCauldrons&r, and they know very well that you should never brew and cook in the same place!"
		""
		"Note that in order to use this strange cauldron, you'll need to have &abred a pair of &eSniffers&r!"
	]
	quest.57B6789EE4B210E9.title: "Beroot Cauldron"
	quest.57B830324890E32C.quest_desc: [
		"&bPies&r from this mod can be eaten one of two ways. You can place them down like a &bcake&r and eat them slice-by-slice, or you can place them on a &bCutting Board&r and use that to cut them into &bportable slices&r."
		""
		"When eaten, they grant you a short speed boost!"
	]
	quest.57B830324890E32C.quest_subtitle: "Tastes so good, makes a grown man cry"
	quest.57B830324890E32C.title: "Make a Pie"
	quest.57CEB5677AF42CCB.quest_desc: [
		"&bBrooms&r are incredibly useful to have. Not only do they make a stylish decoration, but you can use them to &asweep up messes&r such as &bSalt&r, &bAsh&r, and more! Pretty cool, right?"
		""
		"Okay, yeah, fine, you can also use them to fly. But it's not easy! Taking a mundane &bBroom&r and turning it into a &bflying Broom&r requires some power, some components, and some time!"
		""
		"Make yourself some &bFlying Ointment&r, and we can move on to the next step."
	]
	quest.57CEB5677AF42CCB.quest_subtitle: "cleanliness is next to goddessliness"
	quest.57CEB5677AF42CCB.title: "The Importance of Brooms"
	quest.5842543AA1FF2F36.quest_desc: [
		"If you're lucky enough to be playing with a friend, you can use a &bHeartstone&r to keep track of them. This item will allow you to &alink with another player&r and &6right click to locate them&r."
		""
		"Additionally, the &bTwinbound Feather&r will allow you to &ateleport to a matching player&r - if both players &6hold their &bFeathers&6, face one another, and hold right click&r, the &bTwinbound Feathers&r will link, and each player will become a &aWaystone Location&r for the other&r. The feathers can be &alinked to multiple people&r, and also &aequipped as a Curio&r. A player must have the item in their inventory or curio slot for the teleportation option to appear."
	]
	quest.5842543AA1FF2F36.title: "Keeping Track of One Another"
	quest.58AA2A38728EC475.title: "Catch Cherry Blossom Fish"
	quest.58F9F0CC133CC7F7.quest_desc: [
		"&lBetter Archaeology&r catacombs are a winding underground structure with a very modest above-ground entrance. Can you &aplumb the secrets from this place&r?"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/catacombs.png width:100 height:70 align:1 fit:true}"
	]
	quest.58F9F0CC133CC7F7.title: "Discover the Catacombs"
	quest.592DF5A6484F1988.quest_desc: ["The &bMegatorch&r is a way to &apermanently disable hostile spawns in an area&r."]
	quest.592DF5A6484F1988.title: "Preventing Mob Spawning"
	quest.593B80E42F663D6A.quest_desc: [
		"The &bWitch's set &agrants bonuses&r depending on how many pieces you're wearing (out of 3)."
		""
		"Hold shift on any item from this set to view what the bonuses are."
	]
	quest.593B80E42F663D6A.quest_subtitle: "These boots were made for witchin'"
	quest.59B0992CDA1B5797.quest_desc: ["A &bRogue Eye&r can be found in a &dJungle Temple&r, and is rumored to have given our ancestors Redstone."]
	quest.5A0A46815A9FE05D.quest_desc: [
		"The &bFaucet&r is an item which will &awithdraw, and drop, items from the sides of blocks&r (inventories, beehives, or jars). This is opposed to Hoppers, which can only withdraw from the bottom."
		""
		"They also function like &bDripstone&r, slowly dripping liquids into a cauldron beneath them."
	]
	quest.5A0A46815A9FE05D.quest_subtitle: "Just hope it's not too leaky"
	quest.5A0A46815A9FE05D.title: "Obtain a Faucet"
	quest.5A1DD637C09F0D13.quest_desc: [
		"What soothes the soul more than houseplants?"
		""
		"Plant &a50 lovely green (or pink or blue) friends&r in basic &bFlower Pots&r."
	]
	quest.5B185B1B72278050.quest_desc: ["Winning a &aRaid&r can be a satisfying challenge. Even better, win a bunch of raids, and you'll get rewarded!"]
	quest.5B185B1B72278050.quest_subtitle: "please can someone go healer"
	quest.5B185B1B72278050.title: "Raid Master"
	quest.5B5DB6950BD9BC15.quest_desc: [
		"The &bOre Magnet&r can sometimes be found inside &dHollow Hills&r, and when used, will &apull entire veins of ores from the ground&r! Simply &6hold right click while aiming at the ground&r and the ores will be moved up to you!"
		""
		"It can be enchanted with Unbreaking or Mending."
	]
	quest.5B5DB6950BD9BC15.quest_subtitle: "I'm a total ore magnet"
	quest.5B5DB6950BD9BC15.title: "Obtain an Ore Magnet"
	quest.5B74E777CB3DF54B.quest_desc: ["Once you have procured some &bWildroot&r or &bGrove Moss&r, you can use it to craft &bRunestone&r, a simple and yet deeply magical material which will help you to &abuild yourself a grove&r."]
	quest.5BC2DC2C73F83B30.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know that you can &atake selfies&r with your new &bCamera&r? Simply &6activate your camera and press F5&r."
		""
		"Take a selfie to complete this quest."
	]
	quest.5C0698C5831F824F.quest_desc: ["Take a photo of &aall 19 vanilla Animals&r!"]
	quest.5C44B803FBB46C7F.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Raw Rabbit"
	quest.5C463B10FDE8CEF2.quest_desc: [
		"In the Center of the &dDark Forest&r, the Dark Tower can be found. It is a massive structure, filled with monsters, and ruled over by a deadly &eUr-Ghast&r."
		"There are four smaller turrets, each containing a &bTower Key&r. These keys are used to unlock the central tower. There are many challenges here to undergo, so be prepared for a long expedition."
		"To defeat the &eUr-Ghast&r, you must defeat his &eCarminite Ghastlings&r in the nearby rooms, near the Ghast Traps. Then and when the beast draws near, activate the trap."
		"The Ur-Ghast is one of the 3 bosses you must defeat to access the &dHighlands&r."
	]
	quest.5C463B10FDE8CEF2.quest_subtitle: "I ain't afraid of no ghast"
	quest.5C5768D4346FD3FE.quest_desc: [
		"The &bVendor&r is a block which allows players to &atrade items for currency&r in multiplayer."
		""
		"You can &6right click the vendor&r to buy the contents, as long as you have either &bexact change&r or a &bCard&r in your inventory. Look at the tooltip to determine &awhat you're buying and how much it costs&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/numibuy.png width:200 height:180 align:center click_action:none:}"
		""
		"See the next page to view how to &aset up your &bVendor&r to buy or sell!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/numivendor.png width:200 height:180 align:center click_action:none:}"
		""
		"&eA&r: These sections allow you to determine the price of the item you're selling. For example, something could cost 1 &bCrown&r and 2 &bSpurs&r."
		""
		"&bB&r: This section is where your profits will go if you don't have a card inserted to transfer your profits directly to your bank."
		""
		"&cC&r: This box determines what you're selling. You can place up to a stack of items in this slot. This slot will &adisplay the item&r, but it will show as &dout of stock if slot E isn't filled&r. If you wish to sell a bundle of items, you can put it inside a &bShulker Box&r. If you use a &bSack&r or similar, the &dcontents will not be displayed to your customers&r."
		""
		"&9D&r: You can place a &blinked Card&r in this slot to have all profits deposit straight into your &bBank Account&r."
		""
		"&dE&r: This section is where you place your &ainventory of items&r to sell."
		""
		"&aF&r: This section determines whether you are &abuying or selling&r. "
	]
	quest.5C5768D4346FD3FE.title: "Multiplayer Bartering"
	quest.5C59C06355C7DC77.quest_desc: ["Your &eHamster&r can wear a cute little &bAcorn Hat&r, so why shouldn't you?"]
	quest.5C59C06355C7DC77.quest_subtitle: "matchy matchy"
	quest.5C59C06355C7DC77.title: "Get Matching Hats"
	quest.5CC06EBF8D36316A.quest_desc: ["Use your &bSpyglass&r to research 100 &bPlants&r! You madman!"]
	quest.5D02706F32B44B08.title: "The Simmer Pot"
	quest.5D1EFA0ECBE9891C.quest_desc: [
		"The &bEye of Ender&r was once used to find the &cStrongholds&r of old. However, these no longer function the way they once did."
		""
		"To locate the &cStronghold&r, the modern witch uses an &bExplorer's Compass&r! You can also throw &bEyes&r from &lEnd Remastered&r, but as they are harder to come by, this is not advised."
	]
	quest.5D37E0A2F297C49E.quest_desc: [
		"Ah, here we are! Combine the &bChocolate Spread&r and &bCake Dough&r you made in a &bBaking Station&r."
		""
		"An indulgent treat, this &bChocolate Cake&r should keep you sated for a while!"
		""
		"Or, if you're so inclined, you could &aprogress to the next quest&r and &afind a way to &6display it&r! Actually, here, take these two &bCake Slices&r. That way you can &aeat your cake, and have it, too&r."
		""
		"Yes, I know that's now how the phrase goes. But if you think about it, it really makes more sense this way."
	]
	quest.5D439CB08EE5A923.quest_desc: [
		"There are many types of pie, and by crafting them all, you have proven yourself a master piesmith."
		""
		"Now, I recommend &aplacing these pies&r in your pie hole!"
	]
	quest.5D439CB08EE5A923.quest_subtitle: "3.14159265359"
	quest.5D439CB08EE5A923.title: "Pie Lovers Anonymous"
	quest.5D51C92D31F9974B.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Horn Coral Block"
	quest.5D5261F404366454.quest_desc: ["The &eWither&r is a fearsome foe, but I have faith that you're a powerful enough witch to &6defeat one in combat&r."]
	quest.5D5261F404366454.title: "Defeat the Wither"
	quest.5D56599E8A52F61B.quest_desc: [
		"There are a number of different &bDrawer Upgrades&r. There are the &bMetal Upgrades&r, which &aincrease drawer capacity&r. There is the all-important &bVoid Upgrade&r, which prevents the server from lagging by &avoiding excess items&r. And there are the utility upgrades:"
		""
		"- &bPulling Upgrade&r: It pulls items from an adjacent inventory"
		""
		"- &bPushing Upgrade&r: It pushes items to an adjacent inventory"
		""
		"- &bCollecting Upgrade&r: It collects items on the ground directly in front of it"
		""
		"- &bRedstone Upgrade&r: Gives off a redstone signal based on how full the drawer is. Can be configured to read different slots in multi-slot drawers"
	]
	quest.5D56599E8A52F61B.title: "Drawer Upgrades"
	quest.5D7D1F5AEDE61466.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Sugar"
	quest.5DB08A394A7B8122.quest_desc: [
		"The &bWayward Lantern&r will allow any pets in unloaded chunks to &afind their way home&r. Place it near your base, and if you should lose your pet while exploring, watch for them there."
		""
		"If you &alose your pet in another dimension&r, you will need to &6place a Lantern in that dimension&r to get them back."
		""
		"In &dMultiplayer&r, your pets will respawn at the &aclosest Lantern&r, so be careful in other people's areas."
	]
	quest.5E0E4D3BFE9A205F.quest_desc: ["The &bAdvanced Upgrade&r gives you access to the previous two modes, as well as &aFiltering&r. You can &awhitelist or blacklist&r selected items from being extracted by the pipes."]
	quest.5E3D0655F0A08890.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBasket&r can be used as a chest, but also as a hopper! It has the &astorage capacity of a chest&r, and when dropped or thrown items land on top of it, they will &aautomatically go into its inventory&r."
		""
		"For example, you could &6place one upside-down&r above a &bStove&r in order to collect the finished products! Or put one at the end of a &bConveyer Belt&r."
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/basket.png width:100 height:80 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.5E3D0655F0A08890.quest_subtitle: "I wonder if you could play ball with it."
	quest.5E3D0655F0A08890.title: "Obtain a Basket"
	quest.5F03012DC9E38D8D.quest_desc: ["Although they may not all be hostile, it would still be pretty cool if you killed one of every type of &eCreeper&r. It's like a world tour, but with murder!"]
	quest.5F03012DC9E38D8D.quest_subtitle: "Kill one of each Creeper type"
	quest.5F03012DC9E38D8D.title: "Creeper Collector"
	quest.5F1A07D19C09FFE6.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Bell"
	quest.5F2C26D1C6302016.quest_desc: [
		"Some meals, like &bGlazed Ham&r or &bShepherd's Pie&r, need to be &6placed in world&r in order to eat them. They also make great decoration for your (visual) feasting pleasure!"
		""
		"You'll also need a &bbowl&r in order to eat them, so here, take this one."
	]
	quest.5F2C26D1C6302016.quest_subtitle: "Stuffed Pumpkin is the new cake"
	quest.5F2C26D1C6302016.title: "Make Placeable Meals"
	quest.5F701DECF017C7BF.title: "New Ring Slot"
	quest.5FC2335FA7C31389.quest_desc: [
		"The &lBeautify&r &bLattices&r can hold flowers! You can use"
		""
		"- &bSunflowers&r"
		"- &bPeonies&r"
		"- &bRose Bushes&r"
		"- &bLilac&r"
		"- &bGlow Lichen&r"
		"- &bVines&r"
		"- &bWeeping Vines&r"
		"- &bTwisting Vines&r"
		""
		"Be aware that the &lSpawn&r mod &dreplaces vanilla &bSunflowers&r, which means they need to &abe converted to vanilla in your crafting grid&r before you can use them."
	]
	quest.5FC2335FA7C31389.title: "Flowering Lattices"
	quest.5FFDCF4E36648791.quest_desc: ["Need a place to keep your &bBroom&r? You can place the &bBroom Stand&r either on the ground or &ahanging on the wall&r, and then &6right click your Broom&r onto it!"]
	quest.6016A3D8B7FD7A14.quest_desc: [
		"The Labyrinth, found in the depths of &dthe Swamp&r, houses a number of nasty creatures, culminating in the vicious &eMinotaurs&r and &eMinoshroom&r."
		""
		"The Minoshroom will drop &bMeef Stroganoff&r, which when eaten, will innoculate you against the curse of the &dFire Swamp&r, allowing you to progress."
	]
	quest.6016A3D8B7FD7A14.quest_subtitle: "Unfortunately, no Goblin Kings here..."
	quest.60205D338359F03C.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Raw Blocks"
	quest.60445E736AE3B5B4.quest_desc: [
		"Much like its browner brother, &bRich Soul Soil&r is formed of &bSoil Compost&r that has been &aleft adjacent to Lava&r."
		""
		"You can use it to grow &bNether Crops&r more quickly!"
	]
	quest.605D30BFA0C1C6A7.quest_desc: ["The &bEvil Eye&r is a symbol of protection, staring down the foes of its owner. It can be purchase from a &dMaster Cleric&r."]
	quest.60E911F7FF96F190.quest_desc: ["This &bItem Display&r will allow you to, well, display any &bitems&r, &das long as they don't have a &aBlock form&r. For example, you can display a &bCupcake&r or a &bPickaxe&r, but not a &bCake&r or a &bDiamond Block&r."]
	quest.61101043D3A5BB43.quest_desc: [
		"Every witch - for that matter, every &operson&r - should know how to &asew&r. It is an endlessly useful skill for mending and altering, and here, it will allow you to &acraft many fashionable and powerful &bArmors&r."
		""
		"You'll need to begin with the &bTailoring Bench&r, and you'll also need a &bSewing Needle&r (to be clear, not a magical one!) and a pair of &bScissors&r. The &bTailoring Station&r has an inventory which can hold your tools and also &byour ingredients&r. "
		""
		"&6Select your recipe from the top dropdown&r and click &aStart Sewing&r if you have never made this item before. After you successfully complete the item for the first time, you unlock the ability to &aQuick-Craft&r it, which will produce the item &awithout any bonuses or penalties&r."
		""
		"Once you have selected the seam you wish to begin sewing, you'll &aenter a minigame&r where you must &6hit spacebar in time with each stitch&r. The more green stitches you get, the better quality the garment will be. &aExpert or Master quality&r garments will grant additional bonuses."
		""
		"{image:quest_enhance:textures/ftb/clipboard_1785795465609.png width:345 height:432 align:center click_action:none:}"
	]
	quest.61101043D3A5BB43.quest_subtitle: "a \"sewist,\" not a \"sewer\""
	quest.612B4F05F1E3636D.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have pigments on your &bPalette&r, you can &6mix them together&r on the &aright side of your Palette&r."
		""
		"Use the &aWater&r on your Palette to erase a mixed color. Use the &ablending options&r on the right of the &bCanvas&r to blend your colors together. Change your &abrush size&r there, too! If you make a mistake while painting, you can &6ctrl+z to undo&r, or &6right click to erase&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/joyofpainting.png width:100 height:80 align:1 fit:true}"
		""
		"You can toggle tooltips using the button in the &atop right&r (not pictured)."
		""
		"At any time, you can &6shift left click&r the &bEasel&r to take your painting down. You can &6hang the painting by right clicking it&r on a wall. You can remove it and edit it &aas long as you haven't signed it yet&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/joyofpaintingsign.png width:100 height:90 align:1 fit:true}"
		""
		"Once you've signed it, it can no longer be edited, but it will be named what you titled it, and will show your name as the artist! Nice work!"
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/joyofpaintingdone.png width:100 height:100 align:1 fit:true}"
	]
	quest.612B4F05F1E3636D.title: "Begin a Painting"
	quest.6138C299ED7CE80C.quest_desc: [
		"The &bHammock&r is an item which allows you to &aprogress the time to night&r by taking a &anice, relaxing nap&r during the day."
		""
		"You'll need to first make sure you have exactly &dfour blocks of space&r for the &bHammock&r. Place the &bRope and Nail&r on two blocks, four blocks apart. Then you can &6right click the &bHammock Cloth&r into place."
	]
	quest.6138C299ED7CE80C.title: "Daytime Relaxation"
	quest.617540753B3AA2DD.quest_desc: ["Look to the &cSubterranean&r to find these fish..."]
	quest.617540753B3AA2DD.title: "Catch Cave Fish"
	quest.61FE7F469313BD70.title: "Center Point"
	quest.621ACA8319D6CB93.quest_desc: ["The &bDrying Rack&r allows you to &6hang your herbs to dry&r. It also makes a lovely decoration."]
	quest.6246E8289C638CCE.quest_desc: ["There are many different historical locations where &atraps&r, &bfossils&r, &bloot&r, and more can be found! Visit the &athree most prominent&r ones and see what you're able to dig up!"]
	quest.6246E8289C638CCE.quest_subtitle: "Indiana Jones' dream"
	quest.6246E8289C638CCE.title: "Remnants of the Past"
	quest.628D5F4ACDE2C665.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Feather"
	quest.62A0D663EF2B58C1.quest_desc: [
		"The &bPeacock Feather Fan&r is an item which sends out a mighty gust of wind when &6right clicked&r."
		""
		"You can use this to gain an advantage in combat, or even to give yourself a boost in midair, when jumping or using &bElytra&r!"
	]
	quest.62A0D663EF2B58C1.quest_subtitle: "Ostentatious but very useful"
	quest.62A0D663EF2B58C1.title: "Obtain the Peacock Feather Fan"
	quest.62D95F91881F228C.quest_desc: [
		"There are a number of &ajar types&r in this modpack."
		""
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/jartypes.png width:150 height:100 align:1}"
		""
		"The one from &lSupplementaries&r can hold up to &athree buckets of liquid&r and can also hold &bCookies&r, or even &bBucketed Fish&r! You can &aeat edibles&r from the jar by &6right clicking&r."
		""
		"You can also capture small mobs such as &eSlimes&r and &eBees&r. You can &aplace the jar by crouching and right clicking&r it. If you &6simply right click&r, you will release the creature."
		""
		"The &bJar&r from &lBakery&r can hold &bJams&r."
		""
		"The &bJar&r from &lHearth and Home&r can be used to &acraft jams&r, but can also be &aplaced down&r, fitting up to &a4 jars in one block&r!"
	]
	quest.62D95F91881F228C.quest_subtitle: "jar jar is the heart of it"
	quest.62D95F91881F228C.title: "Differentiating Jars"
	quest.62F2784763AD1938.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you've got your &bStarcatcher's Rod&r, you're ready to revolutionize the fishing industry. Put Big Fish to rights! Or something."
		""
		"Anyway, the minigame is different! When a fish bites and your bobber dunks, &6right click to open the Starcatching minigame&r. This features your reel, with the handle spinning around. &6Click or press space&r when the handle passes over the &bSweet Spots&r to reel in your fish. Miss, and your fish begins to escape. Wait too long, and the same thing happens. When the fish gets pulled to the top of the line, you win!"
		""
		"&dYou can read more about the minigame in your &bFishing Grimoire&r - er, &bGuide&r. Make sure to read it carefully, as there is more to know than what this quest suggests."
		""
		"Keep in mind that some fish can only be caught under &acertain conditions&r, such as &cdeep underground&r, or &aonly at night&r... Check your &bGuide&r to see the requirements!"
		""
		"{image:quest_enhance:textures/ftb/clipboard_1787860617290.png width:345 height:232 align:center fit:true click_action:none:}"
	]
	quest.62F2784763AD1938.title: "More about Starcatching"
	quest.62F755926795DBB6.quest_desc: [
		"It's time for you to fight - actually, no. Let's try something different. Take a &bselfie&r with the &eLich&r in its tower, and develop it."
		""
		"I mean, you should probably still fight that thing. It's like, evil and stuff. But there's no reason you can't commemorate the moment."
	]
	quest.62F755926795DBB6.title: "Take a Selfie with the Lich"
	quest.634BC93E44B404C2.quest_desc: [
		"The &bLunch Basket&r is an item which can hold your &afood items in a single slot&r! Place food inside by &6holding food in your offhand and the &bBasket&r in your main hand, then &6click&r."
		""
		"You can &achange from fill mode to eat mode&r by &6left clicking in the air while holding it&r."
		""
		"To eat from it, simply &6hold right click&r while in eating mode!"
		""
		"It can also be &aplaced on the ground&r and accessed that way."
	]
	quest.634BC93E44B404C2.quest_subtitle: "a tisket, a tasket"
	quest.635FE9332FFCE4A7.quest_desc: [
		"The &bEssence of the Bees&r is acquired by &acompleting the &bQueen's Desire&r advancement line, which is unlocked after &atrading with her&r for the first time."
		""
		"It is a consumable item which &agives you pleasant pheremones&r, soothing nearby &eBees&r. You gain the following &dpermanent bonuses&r:"
		""
		"- Actions which previously activated &bWrath of the Hive&r will no longer do so."
		"- Entering the &cThrone Pillar&r will no longer grant &bMining Fatigue&r."
		"- Entering &bHoney Fluid&r will grant Regenerative effect."
		"- Entering &bRoyal Jelly Fluid&r will grant a short lived Beenergized effect and stronger Regenerative effect."
		"- &bBeehive/Bee Nests&r can be mined, &bhoney&r taken by bottle, or sheared for &bhoneycombs&r without angering the bees. No campfire needed!"
		"- &eHoney Slime&r will not get angry at you for taking its honey."
		"- Standing on &bLuminescent Wax&r will start granting beneficial effects instead of negative ones."
		"- Allows usage of endgame Bumblezone &bEssence&r items. Their abilities are now usable by the player."
		""
		"Additionally, new &bHoney Compasses&r pointing towards &cSempiternal Sanctums&r will begin showing up in &cBumblezone Loot&r."
	]
	quest.63984978A1AADF30.title: "Color Film"
	quest.63A2968E78D4A9A7.quest_desc: ["This quest exists purely so that when you make a &bS'more&r...you get some more!"]
	quest.63A2968E78D4A9A7.quest_subtitle: "please sir, i want..."
	quest.63A2968E78D4A9A7.title: "S'mores"
	quest.63B74A5A3FC47CAA.quest_desc: ["These fish can be found in &athe void of &cThe End&r."]
	quest.63B74A5A3FC47CAA.title: "Catch Void Fish"
	quest.6414EFB17FFD56CB.quest_desc: [
		"&eRibbits&r are delightful little frogfolk, peaceable in nature, who love music and - as you could guess - live in &cSwamps&r."
		""
		"Why not attempt to &apay them a visit?&r You may even find a &eRibbit Merchant&r, who will trade you &aunique goods&r in exchange for &bAmethyst&r!"
	]
	quest.6414EFB17FFD56CB.title: "Visit the Ribbits"
	quest.644439D23D454629.quest_desc: [
		"There are few things more enjoyable than a delicious hot beverage. As with all kitchen witchery, making tea and coffee can be an important daily ritual, and the same goes for doing so in game. To begin, you'll need a &bKettle&r."
		""
		"The &bKettle&r must be &6placed on a heat source&r in order to brew tea. You can use a &bcampfire&r, &bmagma block&r, or other source of warmth."
		""
		"Use 2 &bwater buckets&r to fill the &bkettle&r with water by &6inserting them into the interface&r. Then, you can place your brewing ingredients inside!"
	]
	quest.644439D23D454629.quest_subtitle: "Don't let it call your Cooking Pot black."
	quest.644439D23D454629.title: "Obtain a Kettle"
	quest.649CD989B90CED8A.quest_desc: [
		"The &cSempiternal Sanctums&r are endgame structures which should not be visited until one has consumed the &bEssence of Bees&r. Visiting without bee pheremones will result in &aMining Fatigue&r, &aincreased damage from &eSentries&r, and &athe inability to trigger &bSanctum Events&r."
		""
		"At the top of the structure is &aa garden full of Rootmins on patrol&r. Flowers matching the structure's color will be spawned. Upon entering the hole in the center, the player can navigate a &cdeadly maze&r full of &eSentry Watchers&r and collect great loot!"
		""
		"But if the player manages to find their way into the center heart of the structure, they will find a room with a colorful &bEssence Block&r in the center, which matches the color of the structure. &6Touching this Essence Block&r will trigger an &aarena event&r! Each sanctum has a different event and a different endgame reward item for beating said event. The events can be very difficult, so come prepared! Once an event is finished, it &acan be repeated&r by &6clicking the &bEssence Block&r again."
		""
		"The powerful items you can obtain are as follows:"
		""
		"&bEssence of Raging&r (red)"
		""
		"&bEssence of Radiance&r (yellow)"
		""
		"&bEssence of Life&r (green)"
		""
		"&bEssence of Calming&r (blue)"
		""
		"&bEssence of Knowing&r (purple)"
		""
		"&bEssence of Continuity&r (white)"
	]
	quest.649CD989B90CED8A.title: "Find a Sempiternal Sanctum"
	quest.64E8A8E1C9A939C9.quest_desc: [
		"The central crafting station for the savvy witch - the most mechanically complex cauldron in our catalogue!"
		""
		"How it works:"
		""
		"- Has a full GUI: 8 ingredient slots, 1 fluid slot, 1 sigil slot"
		"- Fill with a fluid first (water, tallow, blood, lava, or potion fluid)"
		"- Add up to 8 ingredients"
		"- Some recipes &arequire heat&r below (lava, magma block, campfire, etc.)"
		"- Some recipes &arequire a specific moon phase&r (check in-game Book of Shadows)"
		"- The &bCandle Dipper&r attaches on top to dip string/candles into the cauldron's fluid"
		""
		"&lWhat it makes&r: Most Hexerei crafting outputs - Blood Sigil, Flying Ointment-adjacent items, brewed items, magical essences, and more!"
		""
		"&bBlood&r is also produced here: place a &bBlood Sigil&r in the sigil slot and jump in 3 times to fill the cauldron with delici - uh, I mean, regular human blood."
	]
	quest.64E8A8E1C9A939C9.title: "The Mixing Cauldron"
	quest.6605ED243F07A169.quest_desc: ["You can obtain &bGhost Gypsum&r by putting &bCalcite&r into a &bDistillery&r. Unlike naturally spawning Gypsum, which makes regular &bChalk&r, &bGhost Gypsum&r is used in making &bRitual Chalk&r."]
	quest.6605ED243F07A169.title: "Obtain Ghost Gypsum"
	quest.6630D27FC9E3F285.quest_desc: [
		"Have you &aautomated your farm&r? Then you probably know the pain of excessive crop ownership. &6Submit your crops to this quest&r to earn rewards."
		""
		"[Repeatable Quest]"
	]
	quest.6630D27FC9E3F285.title: "Ship Your Crops"
	quest.66B094500E40DA3D.quest_desc: ["So, you died. It happens to us all, eventually! Don't worry, all your items are safe in a &bgrave&r marking your last resting place."]
	quest.66B094500E40DA3D.quest_subtitle: "handbook for the recently deceased"
	quest.66BFC51EB4E7FDFB.quest_desc: [
		"One of the treasured items you can find in loot chests are &bTarot Cards&r. Each grants a &astrong buff while held&r in your inventory."
		""
		"Can you find the whole Arcana?"
	]
	quest.66BFC51EB4E7FDFB.quest_subtitle: "what's in the cards for you?"
	quest.66BFC51EB4E7FDFB.title: "Obtain Tarot Cards"
	quest.67D148EB436BE069.quest_desc: [
		"You did it. You made the Perfect Backpack. a lever of infinite size could not pry this backpack from reality. "
		""
		"&dJust don't lose it somewhere.&r"
	]
	quest.68360A5DB4102013.quest_desc: ["The &bWhiff of Magic&r is a very key item, as it is the pathway that leads to &bAttuned Stones&r."]
	quest.68360A5DB4102013.quest_subtitle: "a wheEEf of magic"
	quest.684AF61973DB643F.quest_desc: ["&bSalt&r is an important ingredient in &bCheesemaking&r. It can be found in &cMeadow biomes&r, embedded in &bLimestone&r, as well as in &aOases&r and &aunderground&r."]
	quest.684AF61973DB643F.quest_subtitle: "getting salty"
	quest.684AF61973DB643F.title: "Obtain Salt"
	quest.68F4901B115FF9E0.quest_desc: ["The &bFishing Eye&r is said to have once belonged to an &eAncient Mariner&r, who lost his eye in a fight with a fearsome sea serpent. He replaced his eye with this item, but upon his death, he was buried with it at sea. Perhaps you could be so lucky as to &afish it up&r."]
	quest.692725454B955B4C.quest_desc: ["Collect one each of every flower in the game to earn rewards!"]
	quest.692725454B955B4C.title: "Flower Picking: Pink"
	quest.694D0C4F0DCF078C.quest_desc: [
		"Your Sophisticated &bBarrels&r and &bChests are capable of &aholding more than a stack per slot&r, if you use the &bStack Upgrades&r on them. The higher the tier, the more stacks each slot can hold."
		""
		"You can also &ause more than one Stack Upgrade&r, and they will add &amultiplicatively&r!"
		""
		"So if you use a &bTier 1&r and a &bTier 2&r, you will hold 2 stacks by 4 stacks, meaning 8 stacks, or &d512 items per slot&r."
	]
	quest.694D0C4F0DCF078C.title: "Stack Higher"
	quest.698D0D2656B94C43.title: "Catch River Fish"
	quest.69ACDC95A5F78C82.quest_desc: [
		"&eEnder Luggages&r are a tight knit group - unlike regular &eLuggages&r, every &eEnder Luggage&r you own will share the same storage space!"
		""
		"it's just like an &bEnder Chest&r - with feet!"
	]
	quest.69ACDC95A5F78C82.quest_subtitle: "A safer way to store"
	quest.69ACDC95A5F78C82.title: "Not Quite A Chest"
	quest.69E3182321452B88.quest_desc: [
		"The &bEasel&r allows you to &acustomize which painting you want to hang&r!"
		""
		"Simply &6insert the painting and click the rectangles&r to select the painting size, then &6select the image&r with the arrow buttons, and withdraw your painting!"
		""
		"When selecting the size: The rectangles are not a toggle, so left clicking more than once will not unselect the one you've chosen. You need to click the one above or to the left to select a smaller size."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/easel_interface.png width:250 height:180 align:center}"
	]
	quest.69E3182321452B88.title: "Choose Your Paintings"
	quest.6A5281FA52C785C6.quest_desc: [
		"&bSteeleaf&r is a material which can be used to create pre-enchanted armor that is slightly better than Iron."
		""
		"Additionally, blocks of Steeleaf will &areduce fall damage by 25%&r when landed on."
	]
	quest.6A5281FA52C785C6.quest_subtitle: "Steel yourself"
	quest.6A71E1C275F02732.quest_desc: ["&bHot Cocoa&r is made with &bBottled Milk&r. While &bBottled Milk&r will remove one effect from you, positive OR negative - &bHot Cocoa&r will &aonly remove negative effects&r! I always knew Swiss Miss knew what she was doing."]
	quest.6A71E1C275F02732.quest_subtitle: "Cures what ails ya"
	quest.6A71E1C275F02732.title: "Make Some Hot Cocoa"
	quest.6A89D2D688203ADF.quest_desc: [
		"Now, perhaps you're thinking, what exactly does farming have to do with being a witch?"
		""
		"To this, I say, goodness, you've got a one-track mind, haven't you? Well, that's fair enough. Why don't we look at some &apractical spell application&r?"
		""
		"You've already gotten a &bStaff&r, right? If not, you'll want to &ascurry on over and make one&r:"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"A Trusty Staff\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"48D0F767CFD4070B/1\"},\"underlined\":true,\"color\":\"aqua\"}"
		""
		"And once you've got that ready, you'll want to &aprepare two spells&r: &bHarvest&r and &bGrowth Infusion&r. The former will &aharvest crops in an AoE&r, and the latter &aencourages the targeted plant to mature quickly&r. I wonder what other spells you could use in your agricultural pursuits?"
	]
	quest.6A89D2D688203ADF.title: "Magical Farming"
	quest.6AF9BE2037D01B2A.quest_desc: [
		"Your &bAltar&r can be &aupgraded with various foci and sources of power&r. A &bFocus&r is &dplaced on top of the altar&r, and &bsources of power&r should be placed around it, &dwithin 16 blocks&r."
		""
		"Examples of &bFoci&r are:"
		"- Light sources such as &btorches&r, &bcandles&r, and &bcandelabras&r"
		"- &bSkulls&r or &bplayer heads&r"
		"- &bChalices&r or &bgoblets&r"
		""
		"Different options may provide more or less power, so &ado some experimenting&r to see what works the best for you."
		""
		"&bSources of power&r are items which, when surrounding your &bAltar&r, will lend &amagical energy to it&r. Here are some examples:"
		"- &bWooden Altars&r"
		"- &bBudding or growing Crystals&r"
		"- &bHerb Jars&r"
		"- &bWitchy plants and trees&r"
		""
		"Also, be sure to include your other witchy tools such as the &bMixing Cauldron&r, &bKettle&r, &bMortar \\& Pestle&r, and more! If you use it in your practice, it's good to have it near your &bAltar&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/altarsetup.png width:300 height:250 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6AF9BE2037D01B2A.quest_subtitle: "you could say you're...altaring it"
	quest.6AF9BE2037D01B2A.title: "Upgrading Your Space"
	quest.6B0E280BDBD4ACF5.quest_desc: [
		"The &bPet Bed&r allows your pets to &arespawn&r in the morning, should anything unpleasant happen to them. Simply have your pet &6set their spawn point&r by pushing them onto the &bPet Bed&r."
		""
		"Note that &eHamsters&r have their own beds!"
	]
	quest.6B0E280BDBD4ACF5.title: "Get your Pet a Bed"
	quest.6B3AD3CDE8EC90F1.quest_desc: ["Mushrooms are rad as hell. Why not try collecting all of them? Then you can have a super beautiful mushroom glade."]
	quest.6B3AD3CDE8EC90F1.quest_subtitle: "Is fungiphilia a thing?"
	quest.6B3AD3CDE8EC90F1.title: "Cool Mushrooms"
	quest.6BADAB3BD0E50555.quest_desc: [
		"The Yellow &cSempiternal Sanctum&r grants a chance at the &bEssence of Radiance&r."
		""
		"This item is active when &athe player is in a place visible to the sun&r. While held in the offhand, it provides &bRegeneration&r, &bSaturation&r, &bSpeed&r, &bHaste 2&r, and &bDamage Resistance 2&r. It also &aslowly repairs armor over time&r."
		""
		"It has &a4800 durability before it is depleted&r and needs 10 minutes to recharge. It will only recharge in the inventory of someone who has &aconsumed &bEssence of the Bees&r."
	]
	quest.6BADAB3BD0E50555.quest_subtitle: "the color of sunshine"
	quest.6BADAB3BD0E50555.title: "Sempiternal Sanctum: Yellow"
	quest.6BE389D26249D046.quest_desc: [
		"In order to perform &bCircle Magic&r, you'll need different &bChalks&r, in addition to the ritual &bFoci&r, and of course, a nearby &bAltar&r with &aenough Power&r."
		""
		"Using this type of magic, you can do everything from &aforging a Mixing Cauldron&r to &amaking a flying broom&r to &ataming a Familiar&r!"
		""
		"There are four sizes of chalk circle you're likely to use - tiny, small, medium, and large. They - hmm? What's that? Those aren't very witchy names, you say? Look. You want a venti chalk circle, you head on over to Moonbuck's and leave me alone."
		""
		"Anyway, where was I? Oh, yes."
		""
		"In addition to the chalk circles on the outside, every rite requires a &brune of Golden Chalk&r in the center, which should be &6right clicked&r after the reagents are placed. This will &aactivate the ritual&r."
		""
		"A successful ritual will consume your reagents one by one and then provide the desired output. If at the end, your reagents are spat back out, then &dthe ritual has failed&r. Double check your &bingredients&r and that your &bAltar&r is &aclose enough and has enough Power&r."
		""
		"Need to clean up your chalk? Take this &bBroom&r, it will remove the Chalk in one easy swipe! Disclaimer: this broom does not fly...yet."
	]
	quest.6BE389D26249D046.quest_subtitle: "equal rites"
	quest.6BE389D26249D046.title: "Performing Rituals"
	quest.6C25F07248AC8170.quest_desc: [
		"Although the two are not commonly thought of together, &bwitchcraft&r and &barchaeology&r are actually well interwoven. Both revere the bones of our ancestors, both emphasize a respect for the natural world, and both are deeply interested in &aancient ways&r."
		""
		"Anthropology and archaeology are excellent fields of study for witches who want to uncover and decipher ancient mysteries. So why not get yourself started with a &bBrush&r?"
	]
	quest.6C25F07248AC8170.title: "Anthropology 101"
	quest.6C3861D0B545A88F.quest_desc: [
		"&bSugar Water&r is a substance commonly found in the &cSugar Water Floor&r biome of the &bBumblezone&r. You can &6bottle it&r and then use those bottles to &6feed Bees&r or &bHoneycomb Brood Blocks&r. When doing the latter, it &afeeds the growing pupa&r and will eventually &aspawn a baby &eBee&r."
		""
		"When doing the former, you can possibly get the &aProtection of the Hive&r effect!"
	]
	quest.6C3861D0B545A88F.title: "Obtain Sugar Water"
	quest.6C413B091C8DBE2A.quest_desc: ["A full set of &bNetherite Tools&r, well! That's an achievement to be lauded. Congratulations!"]
	quest.6C413B091C8DBE2A.title: "The Full Set: Netherite Tools"
	quest.6C519AFAC9A8866F.quest_desc: [
		"Although the most basic &bCauldron&r had for years languished in obscurity, recent discoveries have made it an incredibly handy tool for the enterprising witch: &apotion combining&r."
		""
		"Now, certainly, we have all been told by our clever parents not to mix multiple potions together, but did you know that the cast iron &atemporarily nullifies any dangerous magical effects&r due to it's anti-fey properties? It's true!"
		""
		"So you can now &6place up to 4 potions&r in a &bCauldron&r and then &6right click with empty bottles&r to retrieve the mixed result! Note that this dilutes the potions somewhat. And be careful, as certain combinations may still cause unpleasant results..."
	]
	quest.6C519AFAC9A8866F.title: "The Humble Cauldron"
	quest.6C75BE906A574DAE.quest_desc: ["There are many meals which can be &6placed down and eaten&r. Craft one of each and show your prowess as a kitchen witch."]
	quest.6C75BE906A574DAE.title: "Placeable Meal Diversity"
	quest.6C7EB11A659D7914.quest_desc: [
		"Perhaps this is too obvious to explain, but the &bTurntable&r is a block that, when provided with a Redstone signal, will rotate the block it is touching."
		""
		"When placed sideways, it can turn an &bHourglass&r to reset it."
	]
	quest.6C7EB11A659D7914.quest_subtitle: "How the turn tables!"
	quest.6CD4F0A4650CBA2F.quest_desc: ["He's just a good boi. Don't let him stay out in the sun too long."]
	quest.6CD4F0A4650CBA2F.quest_subtitle: "that's no golem!"
	quest.6CD4F0A4650CBA2F.title: "Meet the Snow Golem"
	quest.6CD94FF2310068FE.quest_desc: ["The &bDragon Scale&r is an incredibly valuable item which is obtained after defeating the Ender Dragon &6a second time&r. It can be used to &aduplicate Elytra&r."]
	quest.6CD94FF2310068FE.quest_subtitle: "the scale of the universe"
	quest.6D3D3329A2772A3F.quest_desc: ["The &bCharging Station&r will &aburn fuel in order to charge your Building Gadgets&r."]
	quest.6DBD018A4FB32DD8.quest_desc: [
		"Depending on weather, this decorative block will output a redstone signal."
		""
		"When it is &araining&r, it will output a signal of 1. When it is &athundering&r, it will output a signal of 2."
	]
	quest.6DBD018A4FB32DD8.quest_subtitle: "Make it rain"
	quest.6E1B07BEB8F423BC.quest_desc: ["Every witch should be familiar with &aBrewing&r! The creation of &bPotions&r is a key aspect in magical livelihood, as it can significantly improve how one interacts with the world around them!"]
	quest.6E1B07BEB8F423BC.quest_subtitle: "bubble bubble"
	quest.6E1B07BEB8F423BC.title: "Beginner Brewing"
	quest.6E447D4984BAA0EB.quest_desc: [
		"The &bStorage Controller&r is a block which &amagically communes with the surrounding drawers&r. This will allow you to &atransfer items into or out of your network&r through a single block, instead of needing to hook up every single inventory."
		""
		"It requires a &bLinking Tool&r in order to communicate with the surrounding &bDrawers&r. &6Hold the Linking Tool&r to view the radius the &bController&r can reach. Then, simply &6right click the &bTool&6 onto the &bController&r to assign it. Then &6right click your drawers&r to connect them!"
	]
	quest.6E447D4984BAA0EB.quest_subtitle: "one block to rule them all!"
	quest.6E447D4984BAA0EB.title: "Storage Controller"
	quest.6E5DCE8167CB2932.quest_desc: [
		"Hmm, looks like a &bJar of Chocolate Spread&r is exactly what we're going to need for the next recipe."
		""
		"Well, don't just stand there looking at me. &6Get cooking&r!"
	]
	quest.6E5FC4F24E0EDAFE.quest_desc: [
		"The &cCastle Tower&r floats high above the ground, and it, well, towers. It looms. And legend has it that there are &auntold treasures&r kept within its coffers."
		""
		"Should you make it to &athe top of the tower&r, it might be &dworthwhile to look for hidden secrets&r."
	]
	quest.6E5FC4F24E0EDAFE.title: "Find the Castle Tower"
	quest.6E90234166580EEB.quest_desc: ["The &bBig Wooden Spoon&r allows you to &acarve servings off of &bFeasts&r which would normally require a &bBowl&r to collect!"]
	quest.6E90234166580EEB.quest_subtitle: "ursa majora is that you?"
	quest.6EEBE18A146001AC.quest_desc: ["The &bBank Card&r can be used to &afacilitate transactions without you carrying coinage&r! Once linked to your &bBank Terminal&r, you can use your &bCard&r to &abuy items at Shops&r and also to &aaccept money at a &bSelling Bin&r."]
	quest.6EEBE18A146001AC.title: "Obtain a Bank Card"
	quest.6EFFB8ED37DC8A47.quest_desc: [
		"The &lSpice Of Life&r is a mod which rewards you for eating a &adiverse diet of well-balanced foods&r. While you can survive on nothing but &bBread&r and &bGolden Carrots&r, you'll find that you thrive if you make and eat more rewarding foods - which this pack offers a LOT of."
		""
		"You can view the benefits in your &bFood Book&r in your &bEccentric Tome&r."
		""
		"When you hover over a piece of food, you'll be able to see its &adiversity value&r, and the &aamount of diversity it will add to your score&r (in parentheses). If you have a high diversity score and eat something of low diversity, it will &alower your average diversity&r and the number will show in red instead of green."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/spiceoflife1.png width:180 height:180 align:1}"
		""
		"Additionally, &aeating the same food repeatedly&r will not improve your diversity score. But wait, you say, I can't go carrying around that much food! I'm a witch, not a pack mule! To this I reply: go to the next quest."
	]
	quest.6EFFB8ED37DC8A47.quest_subtitle: "(psst, it's variety)"
	quest.6EFFB8ED37DC8A47.title: "The Spice of Life"
	quest.706D91D3C11487E5.quest_desc: ["Prove to the world that you can handle the heat in the kitchen by &6cooking one of every dish&r from the base &lFarmer's Delight&r mod. Earn your cap and have lesser cooks telling you, \"Yes Chef!\""]
	quest.706D91D3C11487E5.quest_subtitle: "you know, like the guy from halo"
	quest.70804E3448872FDE.quest_desc: [
		"Use your &bSpyglass&r to research ALL OF THE &bPlants&r!"
		""
		"Wow, that's quite the accomplishment. I admire your dedication to looking closely at things!"
	]
	quest.70B1F4C0D65D12D1.quest_desc: ["It might take a while, but why not &acollect all &bCheese&r types and have yourself a little tasting?"]
	quest.70B1F4C0D65D12D1.quest_subtitle: "it's not easy being cheesy"
	quest.70B1F4C0D65D12D1.title: "Collect All Cheeses"
	quest.70C4F17973F6492E.quest_desc: [
		"&bEmeralds&r! These are the bread and butter of the &eVillagers&r which live in your world. You will need these to obtain rare items such as the new &bEnd Portal Eyes&r."
		""
		"To find a &alist of all villager professions and their job blocks&r, hover over an &bEmerald&r and &6press \"u\"&r, then &6choose the top tab with a villager face&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/villagers.png width:200 height:200 align:1}"
	]
	quest.70C4F17973F6492E.title: "The Basis of an Economy"
	quest.7126D9210A7E072C.quest_desc: [
		"You can use a &bTanning Rack&r to make &bLeather&r. Simply place an &bAnimal Hide&r on the rack, optionally &6right click it with &bLye&r - then wait!"
		""
		"Hmm, you got &bRotten Flesh&r by mistake? Perhaps you should &ascrape the &bHide&r with something..."
	]
	quest.717B733896BBB2AA.quest_desc: [
		"Step one on your journey to the ultimate burger is this: the humble &bHamburger&r."
		""
		"The humbleburger, if you will. Hambumble? I don't know."
	]
	quest.717B733896BBB2AA.quest_subtitle: "Don't think too hard about the reward"
	quest.717CF92CE4A34A5F.quest_desc: [
		"If you're feeling a little mischievous, you might want to make a &bVoodoo Poppet&r to &aprank your server-mates (or yourself)&r!"
		""
		"You craft and bind a &bVoodoo Poppet&r similarly to other poppets, but its use is different. You'll &6hold the doll in your main hand&r and do the following:"
		""
		"- &6Prick the doll with a &bSimple Bone Needle&r or &bIcy Needle&r in your offhand. This causes 2 damage to your target."
		"- &6Hold right click&r to push your target in the direction you're facing."
		"- &6Throw the doll&r into Water, Fire, or Lava to cause drowning or fire damage."
	]
	quest.717CF92CE4A34A5F.quest_subtitle: "you remind me of the babe"
	quest.717CF92CE4A34A5F.title: "Obtain a Voodoo Poppet"
	quest.7232C9D413054886.quest_desc: ["Need to get somewhere in a hurry? Why not try &aslinging&r? The &bSlime Sling&r, when &6pointed at the ground and drawn&r, will shoot the player in the opposite direction upon release. You can achieve &aquite a bit of air time&r this way! And the &bSlime Boots&r make it so you...you know...&adon't die from fall damage&r. A winning combination!"]
	quest.7232C9D413054886.quest_subtitle: "slimy transport"
	quest.72337CD5CE36F9EF.quest_desc: [
		"Catch &b25 Fish&r and you'll be presented with this &bCopper Trophy&r!"
		""
		"You're just getting started on your starcatching journey, and I think you'll find it's a very rewarding one!"
	]
	quest.724475964CA8B68D.quest_desc: [
		"These upgrades allow your backpack to operate outside the confines of its leather!"
		""
		"- &bPickup Upgrade&r will reroute any items you pick up to enter your backpack instead of your inventory. "
		"- &bMagnet Upgrade&r will draw items to your backpack from a distance! "
		"- &bJukebox Upgrade&r will allow you to be that one hiker who always brings their bluetooth speaker with them to bless the entire trail with the soothing tunes of Nicki Minaj."
		""
		"To get the most of these upgrades, we suggest &6checking out the settings tab&r for each one. "
		""
		"Your settings will be saved for each upgrade &aeven if you remove it.&r"
	]
	quest.724475964CA8B68D.quest_subtitle: "let 'em know you're coming"
	quest.724475964CA8B68D.title: "Environmental Upgrades"
	quest.726336858C8FB767.quest_desc: ["These special buttons function similarly to other &bButtons&r, except that the &bIron Button&r gives a &amuch longer signal&r than usual, and the &bGold Button&r a &amuch shorter signal&r than usual."]
	quest.726336858C8FB767.quest_subtitle: "can't stop the signal"
	quest.726336858C8FB767.title: "Obtain Iron and Gold Buttons"
	quest.72AEC02678301699.quest_desc: ["Just theoretically speaking... in a completely hypothetical situation...what would happen if you - or anyone, it doesn't have to be you - what would happen if someone were to (and understand, I'm not suggesting you do this or anything), but &awhat if someone were to throw an &bEgg&r at the &eWarden&r?"]
	quest.72CE099C5784339A.quest_desc: [
		"The &bSpyglass&r is quite an underrated tool. To begin with, it allows you to &aview distant things&r without having to leg it all the way over yonder. But that's just the beginning!"
		""
		"Perhaps more importantly, they allow you to &aresearch the world around you&r. Encounters with even the most mundane creatures will &agrant you experience&r and &aunlock &lField Guide&r &aentries&r."
		""
		"There have been some improvements made to the &bSpyglass&r experience, as well - for one thing, the &aoverlay is now customizable&r, which means you can actually see the world around you!"
		""
		"You can also &6equip it as a curio&r, and access its functionality with a hotkey!"
	]
	quest.72CE099C5784339A.title: "Zooming In"
	quest.730964D8E1FD059F.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the Twilight Forest! This dimension can be dangerous to navigate, although it is convieniently laid out with its &amajor landmarks in a grid&r."
		""
		"The first thing you will want is a &bMap&r, and for that, you'll need to find a &eRaven&r."
		""
		"And remember! &6If you get lost or wander into an inaccessible zone, look for &eKobolds&r. They will be carrying the journal of previous adventurers, which will clue you in to your next goal."
	]
	quest.730964D8E1FD059F.quest_subtitle: "Entering a crepuscular zone"
	quest.730964D8E1FD059F.title: "Reach the Twilight Forest"
	quest.732D5D711B04EA36.quest_desc: [
		"The &bIce Crystal&r can be obtained one of two ways. The first way is to defeat the mighty &eFrostmaw&r, which is a fearsome boss which deals &afreezing damage&r and &ais immune to arrows&r."
		""
		"Or, you could &awork smarter and not harder&r, and &6find a way to steal the &eFrostmaw's &bIce Crystal&r before it awakens."
		""
		"However, there may still be a &bspecial reward&r for defeating the &eFrostmaw&r anyway..."
	]
	quest.732D5D711B04EA36.quest_subtitle: "we can do this the hard way, or..."
	quest.732D5D711B04EA36.title: "Obtain an Ice Crystal"
	quest.737B48AA3FE651BD.quest_desc: ["You can &adisplay your delicious &bpastries&r using a &bCake Stand&r, &bCupcake Display&r, or &bCake Display&r."]
	quest.737B48AA3FE651BD.title: "Displaying Your Pastries"
	quest.73B26E8BA35A9C25.quest_desc: [
		"There are two ways you can upgrade your storage, &alevel by level&r, or &abasic on upwards&r."
		""
		"Assuming you used the reward from the last quest, you'll now have an &bIron Barrel&r. You can upgrade this to &aGold tier&r with an &bIron to Gold Upgrade&r. This is taking it up &alevel by level&r."
		""
		"To upgrade from &aBasic upwards&r, you'll need the &bBasic to Gold&r (or other level) Upgrade. This will, as you could guess, take a &bBasic Storage&r and bring it directly to &aGold tier&r."
		""
		"With each tier of upgrades, &ayour storage improves&r. At Gold tier it has &amore slots and an additional upgrade slot&r on the left."
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/sophgold.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.73B26E8BA35A9C25.quest_subtitle: "mo storage, mo problems"
	quest.73B26E8BA35A9C25.title: "More Storage, More Upgrades"
	quest.73DC7CDFA4B7E09A.quest_desc: ["The &bWall Bread Display&r can be used to show off your &bBreads&r from the &lBakery&r mod!"]
	quest.73EAABCF703B9DC9.quest_desc: ["You killed the Dragon twice? Well, my goodness."]
	quest.73EAABCF703B9DC9.quest_subtitle: "Well that's just excessive"
	quest.740C9D783E4018EC.quest_desc: ["&bSweet Dough&r is the basis for many delicious pastries. The aspiring Kitchen Witch would do well to familiarize themself with its recipe!"]
	quest.740C9D783E4018EC.quest_subtitle: "sweet, dough!"
	quest.74403CDD36E19E5B.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Honey"
	quest.747EC7F313519A0F.quest_desc: [
		"Whether or not you're a consumer of adult beverages, a &bDistillery&r can be a very useful tool! In this case, what it distills is &bVapor&r, producing unique and advanced &bfumes&r for you to work with!"
		""
		"It accepts up to 3 inputs, one of which &dmust be a &bClay Jar&r."
	]
	quest.747EC7F313519A0F.quest_subtitle: "dis still is very neat"
	quest.747EC7F313519A0F.title: "Obtain the Distillery"
	quest.74A5C07E1CC1BDCB.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Hay Bale"
	quest.7527E0A9EF5C3697.quest_desc: [
		"The &bWarp Scroll&r is a one-time use item which can &awarp to any Waystone from anywhere in the world&r. It does not have a cooldown, but the item is consumed upon use."
		""
		"Simply &6hold right click with it in your hand&r in order to activate it. If you take damage or let go while it is charging, &dthe warp will cancel&r."
	]
	quest.7527E0A9EF5C3697.title: "Obtain a Warp Scroll"
	quest.7557E8749BF869DF.quest_desc: [
		"A &bcutting board&r will allow you to prepare advanced ingredients for your meals, such as &bbacon&r or &bfish filets&r. Simply &6place the item on the cutting board&r and &6right click it&r with your knife."
		""
		"This isn't the only use for the &bcutting board&r! Try experimenting with items like &bwooden logs&r (using an &baxe&r) or even unwanted &bleather armor&r (with &bshears&r)!"
	]
	quest.7557E8749BF869DF.quest_subtitle: "Back to the ol' Cutting Board"
	quest.7557E8749BF869DF.title: "Obtain a Cutting Board"
	quest.755902F379AFB989.quest_desc: ["What every witch - every person, really - needs is a &acollection of &bHats&r. Why not accumulate all of them and get a nice reward?"]
	quest.755902F379AFB989.quest_subtitle: "some very fine hats"
	quest.755902F379AFB989.title: "Handsome Haberdashery"
	quest.7565DBC1E7DFF142.quest_desc: [
		"Some magic requires &aessences of your targets&r, known as &bTaglocks&r. Hair, blood, toenail clippings... anything that was very closely tied to the target of the spell can be used."
		""
		"To collect such things, you will need a &bTaglock Kit&r, which consists of a &bGlass Jar&r and a &bBone Needle&r."
		""
		"You can use a &bTaglock Kit&r on &eanother player directly&r, but it might be better to &6shift right click on their bed&r instead. If you are planning to target &ayourself&r, you can use &ayour own bed&r for this!"
		""
		"You can also collect &ablood&r from &bBlood Poppies&r which have been walked through."
		""
		"From there, you'll need a &bPoppet&r to infuse."
	]
	quest.7565DBC1E7DFF142.quest_subtitle: "she turned me into a newt!"
	quest.7565DBC1E7DFF142.title: "Baneful (or Beneficial) Magic"
	quest.75794697E256EFCC.quest_desc: ["Once you have &acombined those &bSherds&r, you'll have a &bDecorated Pot&r, into which you can &aplace things&r! I don't have any &bRupees&r, but here, try these &bEmeralds&r."]
	quest.75794697E256EFCC.quest_subtitle: "its pronounced \"shERRds\""
	quest.75794697E256EFCC.title: "Combine Four Pottery Sherds"
	quest.75A98C846E56A570.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Ink Sacs"
	quest.75AD4BD901CEA061.quest_desc: ["Can you tame one of each type of cat in the game? There are eleven. Good luck!"]
	quest.761DD39F82235893.title: "Defeat the Ur-Ghast"
	quest.762A6A61693A5BBA.quest_desc: [
		"In order to &aprint your photographs&r, you must first &adevelop the film&r."
		""
		"This is done by crafting &bThick&r, &bAwkward&r, and &bMundane Potions&r together with the &bColor Film&r. To develop &bBlack and White Film&r, you only need a &bWater Bottle&r. Simply &6combine them in a crafting grid&r and ta-da!"
	]
	quest.762A6A61693A5BBA.quest_subtitle: "mundane, thick, and awkward? same tho"
	quest.762A6A61693A5BBA.title: "Developing Photos"
	quest.76A73E61526B9EE1.quest_desc: ["Much like the Waterproof Tip, the &bNetherite Broom Tip&r will prevent players getting dismounted due to lava. It is recommended to use this with a &bMahogany Broom&r, as it is fire resistant."]
	quest.76A73E61526B9EE1.quest_subtitle: "resist the fire"
	quest.76A73E61526B9EE1.title: "Obtain Broom Netherite Tip"
	quest.76D5DB6E94816C80.quest_desc: ["Congratulations on cheating death! Sorry about your totem, though."]
	quest.773834D44C436587.quest_desc: ["By killing &eHoglins&r with your trusty &bKnife&r, you can gain &bHoglin Loin&r, &bHoglin Hide&r, and sometimes &bHam&r! These can be used in cooking recipes."]
	quest.773834D44C436587.quest_subtitle: "Gird this"
	quest.775A1B6549572BEB.quest_desc: [
		"The &bVoid Upgrade&r is an item which will &aremove unwanted items from your storage&r. It will, quite simply, delete them, ensuring that your storage is both well-organized and your server un-crashed. &dIt is especially important to use this upgrade for farms&r!"
		""
		"You can configure it to &adelete only overflow items&r or, if you prefer, &adelete all items of specific type&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/voidoverflow.png width:100 height:25 align:1 fit:true}"
		""
		"The &bAdvanced Void Upgrade&r is capable of sorting by NBT and Damage levels."
	]
	quest.775A1B6549572BEB.quest_subtitle: "a very important upgrade"
	quest.7793743B2F9DE215.quest_desc: ["As you use your Broom, the Brush will eventually lose durability and need replacing. Begin by making the standard &bWet Broom Brush&r, which can be either immediately upgraded to an &bEnhanced Broom Brush&r, or dried out for use on a &bDrying Rack&r."]
	quest.7793743B2F9DE215.quest_subtitle: "Re-up your flight subscription"
	quest.7793743B2F9DE215.title: "Obtain a Replacement Broom Brush"
	quest.77CCC4FD3E93E79C.quest_desc: ["Hmm, this &bGravel&r (or &bSand&r) looks weird."]
	quest.77CCC4FD3E93E79C.title: "Something is Suspicious..."
	quest.77F821E672D8FE6B.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Sea Lantern"
	quest.781003E78C236E0D.quest_desc: ["The &bCog Block&r performs the same way that &bplaced Redstone&r does. However, it doesn't wash away in water, and can be placed vertically both up and down to send a signal."]
	quest.781003E78C236E0D.quest_subtitle: "You know the joke I wanna make."
	quest.78311C38AC02A32C.quest_desc: ["Full Iron tools! Feels good to make progress, huh? Congrats!"]
	quest.78311C38AC02A32C.title: "The Full Set: Iron Tools"
	quest.78A59A17FEDDE305.quest_desc: ["Eat a bunch of cake! It's a delicious treat and you deserve it."]
	quest.78A818CEEFA49F95.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Chorus Fruit"
	quest.78FB1E1156B8A23C.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Magma Cream"
	quest.794CACBA42AE1AB2.quest_desc: [
		"The &bAthame&r, conversely to the &bKnife&r, is a ritual dagger, and can be used to &acarve &bRitual Braziers&r, by &6shift right clicking on &bPlanks&r."
		""
		"It can also be used to harvest certain items from plants, such as &bTongue of Dog&r from &bWolfsbane Flowers&r."
		""
		"To craft it, you'll want to take a &bGold Knife&r and &aanoint it with herbs&r inside a &atiny&r ritual circle."
	]
	quest.794CACBA42AE1AB2.quest_subtitle: "knife to meet you"
	quest.794CACBA42AE1AB2.title: "The Athame: Ritual Dagger"
	quest.795033CC78FE8CCE.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Poisonous Potato"
	quest.79B6B78157E7D32C.quest_desc: [
		"&bThe Moonworm Queen&r is an...item...that is filled with Moonworms. When you &6right click her&r, they will be dispensed - either directly onto a surface, or shot like an arrow."
		""
		"The moonworms serve no purpose other than &aas a light source&r."
		""
		"You can replenish the Queen by crafting her with &bTorchberries&r, and get... even more worms. Yay."
	]
	quest.79B6B78157E7D32C.quest_subtitle: "You might want to sit down for this one"
	quest.79E6711262027491.quest_desc: [
		"Monsters will occasionally drop these &bcharm fragments&r on death. Collect 6 from one mob (and some string and leather) to craft a &bMob Charm&r! &bMob Charms&r will completely conceal you from that type of monster- even if you hit them! "
		""
		"Be careful though, &aMob Charms do have durability and will break over time&r."
	]
	quest.79E6711262027491.quest_subtitle: "now you see me"
	quest.79E6711262027491.title: "Fragments of Hostility"
	quest.7A21FD3210AE7792.quest_desc: [
		"The &bGacha Machine&r is a truly wondrous object, utilizing a force called RNG (which stands for Ritual Necromancy Gifting) to grant the player &brandom items&r that could be used to &adecorate your living space&r!"
		""
		"For example, it is one of the best ways to obtain &bplushies&r."
		""
		"To use it, simply &6right click it with a valid currency&r (either &bDiamonds&r or &bSprockets&r). Here, have some pocket change. Good luck."
	]
	quest.7A31753911D1CCFC.quest_desc: ["Catch one each of the &abasic fish in vanilla&r!"]
	quest.7A31753911D1CCFC.title: "Catch Basic Fish"
	quest.7A5B3B02E109BCCA.quest_desc: [
		"Make sure you &aload your Palette with dye first!&r You can do this by &6crafting Dyes together with the Palette&r."
		""
		"{image:fabled_wylds:textures/questimages/palette.png width:100 height:100 align:1}"
	]
	quest.7A5B3B02E109BCCA.quest_subtitle: "a refined palette"
	quest.7A5B3B02E109BCCA.title: "Load up Your Palette"
	quest.7A91474C948416AC.quest_desc: ["The &bFramed Wrench&r (and &aall other &bWrenches&r) can be used to rotate the Framed Block. On most blocks, the &arotation behaviour is dependent on the face&r that was clicked."]
	quest.7AD175287E3F0B68.quest_desc: [
		"&bWaystones&r allow you to quickly traverse your world along a network of invisible &aleylines&r. &dThey are not craftable&r, but you can &afind them in &cVillages&r or occasionally &ain the wild&r. The bulk of your fast travel will happen &aVia Romana&r - which is to say, &aby placing signs along charted paths&r."
		""
		"You can find more information about &athe different kinds of Waystones&r in the &lDiscovery&r chapter."
	]
	quest.7AD175287E3F0B68.title: "Waystones 101"
	quest.7AD80A3479D0B0A8.title: "Scavenger Hunt: Dead Bush"
	quest.7AE10F46E005B646.title: "Demon Horns"
	quest.7B3D377F253BFF4A.quest_desc: [
		"&bHerbal Teas&r are commonly used in witchcraft as &atreatments to various ailments&r."
		""
		"&bLavender Tea&r, for example, is good for anxiety and can also call &alove into your life&r. It will boost your &bFortune&r for a while."
		""
		"&bYerba Mate&r is a strongly stimulating tea, making it &agood for fatigue&r or other such maladies. It does not grant ingame effects."
		""
		"&bRibwort Tea&r"
		""
		"&bNettle Tea&r"
	]
	quest.7B3D377F253BFF4A.quest_subtitle: "edit me"
	quest.7B3D377F253BFF4A.title: "Herbal Teas"
	quest.7B4772B066474C41.quest_desc: ["The &bPortstone&r is a method of accessing Waystone travel, but cannot be traveled to, itself."]
	quest.7B8261F4787E6EA7.quest_desc: [
		"The Purple &cSempiternal Sanctum&r grants a chance at the &bEssence of Knowing&r."
		""
		"&6Holding this item in your offhand&r will &ahighlight mobs and outline certain block entities&r near you, allowing you to see what monster is nearby - or &ahidden chests or suspicious blocks&r!"
		""
		"It will also tell you the name of any structure you are in."
		""
		"It has &a1200 durability before it is depleted&r and needs 15 minutes to recharge.  It will only recharge in the inventory of someone who has &aconsumed &bEssence of the Bees&r."
	]
	quest.7B8261F4787E6EA7.quest_subtitle: "the color of secrets"
	quest.7B8261F4787E6EA7.title: "Sempiternal Sanctum: Purple"
	quest.7B961AF6E8BF8EE0.title: "Tarot Cards 3"
	quest.7C3C2D24D60C6C1F.quest_desc: ["Collect one each of every flower in the game to earn rewards!"]
	quest.7C3C2D24D60C6C1F.quest_subtitle: "Red for passion, love, blood"
	quest.7C3C2D24D60C6C1F.title: "Flower Picking: Red"
	quest.7C44602D8680B3BB.quest_desc: [
		"To perform miracles of nature, you'll be wanting a &bRitual Table&r. Yes, you may have already made a &bRitual Pedestal&r - we're very big on ritual around here. This is &odifferent&r - one is a &bRitual &lPedestal&r and one is a &bRitual &lTable&r. Totally different things!"
		""
		"Anyway, so &acraft a &bHex Focus&r and &6right click it on some &bDeepslate&r to transform it into the &bRitual &lTable&r."
		""
		"The &bRitual Table&r requires &b8 fully grown crops&r at &athe same Y level&r to surround it, in order to power your rites. Completing a rite &asacrifices these plants&r and resets them to seedlings."
		""
		"Place offerings on &bRitual Braziers&r that have been &aanointed with &bRitual Salt&r, and finally, &6click the &bRitual Table&6 with your &bHex Focus&r."
	]
	quest.7C47161393ACC4BE.quest_desc: [
		"This advancement requires you to &6put all &eFrog&6 variants on a &bLead&r."
		""
		"&eFrogs&r only spawn in &cSwampy&r areas, but you can &6breed them with &bSlimeballs&r to make them lay &bFrogspawn&r. Once that Frogspawn hatches, you can &6capture the &eTadpoles&r with &bBuckets&r! Then you can &abring those &eTadpoles&r to different biomes to grow into &aregional variant&r adult &eFrogs&r."
	]
	quest.7C47161393ACC4BE.quest_subtitle: "squad goals"
	quest.7C4B0608CCE37793.quest_desc: [
		"The &eCastle Keeper&r is the &aLord of the Twilight Forest&r, and in him is the power of &aevery boss you've defeated so far&r. Especially &afire&r - good gravy is there ever &a<glow color=\"ff0000\">fire</glow>&r."
		""
		"You will want to come to this boss fight well-prepared, as he has an &aenormous health pool&r, is &aimmune to arrows&r, and &ais strongly resistant to physical damage&r."
		""
		"During the fight, &eHarbinger Cubes&r and &eAdherents&r will spawn - some may die to the &aincessant fireballs falling from the sky&r, but if ignored, they will rapidly accumulate! And that's not all - as you deplete his health, the &eCastle Keeper&r will &dsummon the bosses you've already fought&r, sometimes &atwo at once&r."
		""
		"The fight will not be easy. You will need all your tools and all your cunning to make it through alive."
		""
		"But once you defeat him - you will be rewarded with &aloot from all the bosses&r, as well as the &bTalisman of the Cube&r, used to craft his weapon, the &bCube of Annihilation&r. This item can be used to &adestroy blocks and harm your enemies&r."
	]
	quest.7C4B0608CCE37793.title: "Defeat the Castle Keeper"
	quest.7C899C8C278B0998.quest_desc: [
		"The &bBroom Seat&r is an item which allows more than one person to be seated on the same &bBroom&r, &amuch like a boat&r!"
		""
		"All you need is a friend. And you've got at least one of those, right?"
		""
		"...right?"
		""
		"Anyway, the &bBroom Seat&r can be dyed like Leather Armor."
	]
	quest.7C9FD049608453D0.quest_desc: [
		"To begin with the &bFramed Screwdriver&r can be used to &acycle through different states of the &bcosmetic block&r."
		""
		"It can also be used to &aremove the &bPhantom Membrane&r from intangible &bFramed Blocks&r by &6shift right clicking&r it onto the block."
	]
	quest.7CB21D08253F62F6.quest_desc: ["A charming addition to any witch's workspace, this &acompletely decorative&r cauldron may not have a use, but it deserves a place in your collection nevertheless!"]
	quest.7CB21D08253F62F6.title: "The Small Cauldron Set (decorative)"
	quest.7CB901D8FE793DF6.quest_desc: ["The &bDestruction Gadget&r is a dangerous tool which will &acompletely delete blocks&r. It is mostly used to clear a large area for building."]
	quest.7CB901D8FE793DF6.quest_subtitle: "Delete! Delete! Delete!"
	quest.7D15924C5AEAC669.quest_desc: [
		"Be honest, this is the whole reason you came to this dimension, isn't it?"
		""
		"One of the most valuable items in the game, &bThe Uncrafting Table&r allows you to &arecoup materials from crafted items&r in exchange for experience levels. &6Place the unwanted item in the left slot&r and then &6click one of the ingredients&r in the center to remove it."
	]
	quest.7D15924C5AEAC669.quest_subtitle: "Uncraftables are delicious. Wait..."
	quest.7D82FBD000D41F84.quest_desc: ["You can &6right click the &bHammer&r on Handcrafted blocks to &achange their appearance&r."]
	quest.7D82FBD000D41F84.title: "Handcraft your Home"
	quest.7DB8FFF48188EC9C.quest_desc: [
		"&oRoses are red&r"
		"&oViolets are blue&r"
		"&oCandy is sweet&r"
		"&oGo get some (for you)&r"
		""
		"Collect &aone of each type of Candy&r to get a sweet reward!"
	]
	quest.7DB8FFF48188EC9C.title: "Sweet Tooth"
	quest.7DD918D36463CF71.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know you can grind the enchantment off of the &bEnchanted Golden Apple&r?"
		""
		"That would be utterly ridiculous to do, and yet..."
	]
	quest.7E223824125871A6.quest_desc: [
		"The &eShima Enaga&r is a snowy songbird, often compared to a ball of cotton fluff. Although it looks harmless, it is capable of such fierceness as &aconsuming seeds&r! And &acheeping&r! Truly a beast to behold."
		""
		"You can &6tame it with &bSeeds&r, but &dcannot be bred&r."
	]
	quest.7E223824125871A6.quest_subtitle: "Tweet tweet"
	quest.7E223824125871A6.title: "Meet the Shima Enaga"
	quest.7E2641B15D6AF49E.quest_desc: [
		"Why not travel a while by Pig? It may not be fast, or efficient, or even particularly fun."
		""
		"No, that's it, that's the whole sentence."
	]
	quest.7E2641B15D6AF49E.title: "Traveling Piggyback"
	quest.7E532A89B21B20D1.quest_desc: ["The &bSkillet&r allows you to cook on the go! Simply &6stand near a heat source&r and &6add your ingredients&r!"]
	quest.7E936E10896FA3D5.quest_desc: [
		"The &bHanging Sign&r is a versatile decoration block which can hang beneath or off the side of a block."
		""
		"You can add text to it by &aright clicking with an empty hand&r, or you can use it as an item frame by &aright clicking it with an item&r."
	]
	quest.7E936E10896FA3D5.quest_subtitle: "It opened up my eyes"
	quest.7E936E10896FA3D5.title: "Obtain a Hanging Sign"
	quest.7E93B4F1F00B1740.quest_desc: [
		"The &bArena&r is a structure &anot to be taken lightly&r! It is for the most battleborn witches, and those well-geared at that. Filled with &bTrial Spawners&r but beckoning with the promise of &atempting loot&r, it will make you question your sanity in daring to seek it out."
		""
		"To be fully prepared, consider bringing:"
		""
		"- a full set of &bDiamond Armor&r or other set with high durability"
		"- a weapon capable of &adamaging multiple enemies at once&r, such as a &bSword&r enchanted with &bSweeping Edge&r"
		"- a delicious &bhome-cooked meal&r"
		"- items that increase survivability such as the &bVampiric Gloves&r or the &bCross Necklace&r"
		""
		"With these things, a strong heart, and the force of will, you should come out victorious!"
		""
		"&d(but also be warned that some of the &bVaults&r &dare bugged and won't open&r."
	]
	quest.7E9C70F7B0CFD820.quest_desc: ["Collect one each of every flower in the game to earn rewards!"]
	quest.7E9C70F7B0CFD820.quest_subtitle: "Orange for health, warmth, fortune"
	quest.7E9C70F7B0CFD820.title: "Flower Picking: Orange"
	quest.7EE0905786616EA8.quest_desc: [
		"&bPoppets&r are small dolls &asewn from &bStraw&r and &bThread&r, and are used to &arepresent a spell's target&r - either yourself, or another player. In order to function, they must be in &athe target's inventory&r or &aon a poppet shelf&r. The exception is &bVoodoo Poppets&r, but we'll cover that later."
		""
		"There are different types of &bPoppet&r, the first being &abasic&r, then &asturdy&r, then &ainfused&r. A &bBasic Poppet&r has a single use. A &bSturdy Poppet&r has two. And although an &bInfused Poppet&r is single-use, it grants &astronger effects&r."
		""
		"Now, it's important to note that you &dcan't bind a plain Poppet&r, including the plain Sturdy and Infused versions. You must craft a &apoppet with a purpose&r. A purpet, if you will. Oh, you won't? Oh well."
		""
		"Take this &bHint of Rebirth&r to help you in the next step."
	]
	quest.7EE0905786616EA8.quest_subtitle: "poppet. twist it. pull it."
	quest.7EE0905786616EA8.title: "Beginning Poppetry"
	quest.7EE75A2EC8609271.quest_desc: [
		"These upgrades will help you take your workshop with you. Each one does what it says on the tin... &bcrafting tables&r, &banvils&r, &bstonecutters&r... who needs a base? You can live the life of a true adventurer."
		""
		"To get the most of these upgrades, we suggest &6checking out the settings tab&r for each one. "
		""
		"Your settings will be saved for each upgrade &aeven if you remove it.&r"
	]
	quest.7EE75A2EC8609271.quest_subtitle: "live out of your backpack"
	quest.7EE75A2EC8609271.title: "Utility Upgrades"
	quest.7EF04ED51BC1C8D6.quest_desc: [
		"&aNeedle Felting&r is the perfect craft for when you want to stab something several hundred times :)"
		""
		"Usually including yourself :("
		""
		"To begin with, you'll need a &bFelting Needle&r, and some &bWool&r. &6Hold the &bWool&6in your off hand and &6hold the &bNeedle&r in your main hand, then &6hold right click&r to &lSTAB THAT WOOL LIKE IT BETRAYE&r - eh, uh, ahaha. Sorry. Anyway."
		""
		"Not all wools will work with this process, but why not &atry several different kinds&r and see what you can come up with?"
		""
		"And remember to &dbe patient&r - you'll need to hold right click &afor a while&r."
	]
	quest.7EF04ED51BC1C8D6.quest_subtitle: "it's like therapy"
	quest.7EF04ED51BC1C8D6.title: "Obtain a Felting Needle"
	quest.7EF7EE2181ECA4E9.quest_desc: ["Traverse all Nether biomes!"]
	quest.7F52A3C01776886D.quest_desc: [
		"When you die, you &alose most of your experience levels&r - but it doesn't have to be this way! We are magic, after all. "
		""
		"There are many methods through which you can &abank your experience&r to use for later. For example, your &bBackpack&r has an upgrade which allows you to &astore liquid exp&r."
		""
		"There is also the &bHero's Medallion&r, which you can &6right click or shift right click&r to deposit/retrieve experience."
	]
	quest.7FDCB7F0C6C8EADA.quest_desc: [
		"Selling &bDyes&r for only &b3 Spurs&r? Why, to do that would be simply &zcrazy&r!"
		""
		"Welcome to &zCrazy Joe's Dye Emporium&r! Where our deals are &lcrazy&r!"
	]
	quest.7FDCB7F0C6C8EADA.title: "Dyes"
	quest.7FFDEC31AD094335.title: "Tarot Deck"
